a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/447494-mnemon-doesn-t-want-to-be-old-how-about-immortality\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/SDa3pJ0.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T22:52:47-07:00","id":1202141,"title":"","content":"It feels great that the series is now well and truly alive again with a reasonable production cycle of the books. It was starting to feel like being a fan of Berserk or HXH for awhile there.<br /> <br /> <br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber (140$) was the highest I could make myself pledge for this, hopefully we keep blowing through those stretch goals","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T02:23:07-07:00","id":1202168,"title":"","content":"I just dropped my Developer Charm spot if anyone wants to jump in and grab it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T03:45:35-07:00","id":1202181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1201980#post1201980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> the only reason why I'd go for the Developer Charm is really to see the idea in print hoping that more people would use it than the practically zero people who would use something I'd homebrew.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't count on that to be true. Especially with Exalted I've found people to be very excited about homebrew, since the setting and system lends itself to &quot;oh look another neat thing, what else cool stuff could my char/this npc do?!&quot; I've looked up homebrew years old for stuff in games I've played in/run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T04:18:32-07:00","id":1202190,"title":"","content":"I see language that bugs me in the preview, but I'm not certain that it's an outright error.<br /> <br /> \u200bPage 77 in the Iselli description &quot;the house\u2019s gutted but once-venerable espionage machine.\u200b&quot; I've always thought that venerable meant old. A few checks around web dictionaries tells me that venerable means being respected <u>due</u> to its advanced age.<br /> <br /> \u200b&quot;Now it is gutted but it used to be respected because of how old it was&quot;, strikes me as not likely to be the message the author would want to convey.<br /> <br /> \u200bIs there a way to bring this to the attention of the author or editor?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","user":"Apromor","date":".  edited for clarity 04-02-2018, 07:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T05:36:28-07:00","id":1202200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Apromor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1202190#post1202190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200b&quot;Now it is gutted but it used to be respected because of how old it was&quot;, strikes me as not likely to be the message the author would want to convey.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is that?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T05:46:05-07:00","id":1202202,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that makes sense to me. They used to have one of the best intelligence operations, as they'd had so long building it up, but now it is gutted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T06:05:23-07:00","id":1202204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1202200#post1202200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why is that?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bBecause it's now older than it was, and because age is not a thing I'd expect to make an intelligence operation respected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T06:31:15-07:00","id":1202206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Apromor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1202204#post1202204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bBecause it's now older than it was, and because age is not a thing I'd expect to make an intelligence operation respected.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would think age is the kind of thing that can make an organisation respected if it can be seen to contribute to resources and experience, and surviving an environment of adversity.<br /> <br /> \u200bY'know, respecting the Iselsi operation because it had managed to not die in several hundred years, and having several hundred years worth of log books.<br /> <br /> \u200bSomething that might be especially noteworthy when many of the personalities that it would have been spying upon would be almost as old as it is.<br /> <br /> A 290 year old Dynast respecting the Iselsi intelligence network because they know what she did on a wild summer when she was 21.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T06:34:20-07:00","id":1202207,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of prestige in age as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T06:45:24-07:00","id":1202210,"title":"","content":"Age also implies experience, which is the base for most venerations of age. The Iselsi having a venerable spy network also means that its been running for a long time, is well established and has lots of resources to call upon (or had anyway). The wording is fine imho.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T16:24:46-07:00","id":1202330,"title":"","content":"190,000 for digital wallpaper has been achieved","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T22:19:05-07:00","id":1202451,"title":"","content":"New stretch goal, at 205,000 we get more forest witch stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T06:26:16-07:00","id":1202538,"title":"","content":"So the new chapters are out. I guess my only criticism so far is with regards to the line &quot;He hadn't asked the Dragons to be born a man and his mother's only son!&quot; I've always tried to stay away from topics such as sexism, homophobia, and racism in my Exalted games, because those things exist in abundance in real life and I want my Exalted games to be an escape from the depressive reality. Simply reversing the traditional patriarchal society to a matriarchal one is in no way progressive. It's still a gender-based structural hierarchy but with the pronouns reversed, and it doesn't make the Realm a very attractive society for me to immerse myself in. I don't mind the details of marrying into the female's family because she's basically carrying the bloodline, or that it reflects in the matriarchs. I do want to stay away from topics that actively suppresses a gender before the other, though, or that involves characters cursing their own gender (which they have no control over) because of their societal norms. I'm studying to become a social worker in real life to be able to fully explore and deal with such issues. But when I play Exalted, I just want to be a mythic hero in a fantastic world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T06:55:03-07:00","id":1202545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1201746#post1201746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep, very old part of the FAQ. I'll mention it to Ian and get it updated. Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Awesome, thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11633-thesly9","name":"TheSly9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11633_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T07:04:42-07:00","id":1202552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1202538#post1202538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I've always tried to stay away from topics such as sexism, homophobia, and racism in my Exalted games, because those things exist in abundance in real life and I want my Exalted games to be an escape from the depressive reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're free to have your take on the setting but Creation was never supposed to be some perfect utopia.<br /> It has widespread slavery and colonial empires. It has super-powered beings that rule over the masses.<br /> It has never ending wars.<br /> I'd much rather live in our world than creation.<br /> Exalted is escapist only because you get to play someone that is so above ordinary people and you have someone that makes sure you're always the hero of the story","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11671,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11671-dramaflo","user":"DraMaFlo","date":". 04-03-2018, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11671-dramaflo","name":"DraMaFlo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11671_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T07:21:15-07:00","id":1202559,"title":"","content":"Let's not forget the one who doused slaves in molten rubber to use as torches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T07:28:59-07:00","id":1202562,"title":"","content":"While the fluff has been very informative, and interesting to read, I'm really looking forward to Character Creation next Tuesday. I'm wondering what Merits will be introduced, or changed, and just what does Breeding do (Mechanics wise) in 3e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T07:40:34-07:00","id":1202571,"title":"","content":"Wait, wait, wait. A dragonblooded husband taking a male lover is considered <i>scandalous</i> now? It's an <i>embarassment</i> to his wife that he's a disobedient philanderer?<br /> <br /> <s>\u200bOh, so, it is <i>out</i> with the old line that exalted were so lusty that taking lovers was <i>expected</i> and accepted as long as they were same sex to avoid pregnancies.</s><br /> <br /> \u200bNope, despite the implication of the fiction, that line is still there. Page 24.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 04-03-2018, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T07:42:10-07:00","id":1202575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DraMaFlo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1202552#post1202552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're free to have your take on the setting but Creation was never supposed to be some perfect utopia.<br /> It has widespread slavery and colonial empires. It has super-powered beings that rule over the masses.<br /> It has never ending wars.<br /> I'd much rather live in our world than creation.<br /> Exalted is escapist only because you get to play someone that is so above ordinary people and you have someone that makes sure you're always the hero of the story</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a matter of presenting a setting devoid of cruelty. I just want to avoid the specific themes that reverbeate the current political climate. But I think I can do that by simply deciding how I want to shift my focus and how I want to portray my NPCs when I storytell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T08:10:43-07:00","id":1202595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1202575#post1202575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a matter of presenting a setting devoid of cruelty. I just want to avoid the specific themes that reverbeate the current political climate. But I think I can do that by simply deciding how I want to shift my focus and how I want to portray my NPCs when I storytell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly, I'd say that the setting is big enough that one can plausibly have scenarios in which those things aren't really at the foreground, at the very least.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think there are merits to presenting the world with some more unpalatable aspects present in principle, whether it be presenting it in a context of players engaging with sufficient power to do something about it, or even just a sense of how the absence of those things would do a disservice to people that have to face their real life counterparts; I've known people who dislike the idea of settings in which things resonant with their struggles aren't present, if it makes the world feel less real to them or less able to immerse in it.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat's not to say that such an approach is superior to one based on the sense of wanting to escape from the reality of them, just that it's a benefit that it can have to some people, that there's an unfortunate opportunity cost to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T08:12:14-07:00","id":1202597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1202571#post1202571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, wait, wait. A dragonblooded husband taking a male lover is considered <i>scandalous</i> now? It's an <i>embarassment</i> to his wife that he's a disobedient philanderer?<br /> <br /> <s>\u200bOh, so, it is <i>out</i> with the old line that exalted were so lusty that taking lovers was <i>expected</i> and accepted as long as they were same sex to avoid pregnancies.</s><br /> <br /> \u200bNope, despite the implication of the fiction, that line is still there. Page 24.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;same-sex activity only earns remark in exceptional indiscretion&quot; <br /> <br /> The fiction made a point that he was indeed being <i>exceptionally</i> indiscreet about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T08:27:27-07:00","id":1202601,"title":"","content":"The Heptogram admits un-exalted. That's going to make a change in my model of the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T09:17:30-07:00","id":1202620,"title":"","content":"I think all the main 4 admit mortal students because there's always dynast parents going &quot;she's definitely gonna exalt soon! Just give her a year or two!&quot;<br /> <br /> A lot of late bloomers probably wind up in less prestigious schools because their parents couldn't swing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 04-03-2018, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T09:24:46-07:00","id":1202622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1202620#post1202620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think all the main 4 admit mortal students because there's always dynast parents going &quot;she'd definitely gonna exalt soon! Just give her a year or two!&quot;<br /> <br /> A lot of late bloomers probably wind up in less prestigious schools because their parents couldn't swing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, for the Heptagram: &quot;Fuck all man, I'm already a sorcerer. Are you gonna help me <i>not </i>blow up the continent because you're too busy whining that I doing is sans anima?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T09:38:42-07:00","id":1202628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1202538#post1202538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simply reversing the traditional patriarchal society to a matriarchal one is in no way progressive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of all the problems I see in the quoted wall of text (seriously, line breaks!), I call most issue with this.<br /> <br /> It is <i>really </i>progressive, and extremely in-line with modern feminist thought, as it acknowledges the female gender as no more or less capable of bad behavior as the male. It doesn't put women on a pedestal, it just states that people given unearned social privileges tend to abuse them because they think that's the natural order. And to be frank, the Realm has more enlightened social policies than the real world simply by embracing the LGBT part of LGBTQ: You are assumed to be who you say you are, and that cultural openness allows more flexibility than real-world gender roles by default.<br /> <br /> As for the misandrist undercurrents? The Realm is, in-setting, a lurching dinosaur of a country in desperate need of reform. Nothing stops you from starting the Gender Revolution now that Her Redness is vanished; a king who isn't a walking stereotype of male buckling under pressure like Fokuf is more than a good start.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, if you don't want to deal with sexism-the game allows for that too, because it seems to me Realm sexism is low-key unexamined stuff. It's hardly something that comes up all the time, even with men; if you're Exalted, you're a badass by default and they will judge you on that instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 04-03-2018, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T09:54:46-07:00","id":1202629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1202628#post1202628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is <i>really </i>progressive, and extremely in-line with modern feminist thought, as it acknowledges the female gender as no more or less capable of bad behavior as the male. It doesn't put women on a pedestal, it just states that people given unearned social privileges tend to abuse them because they think that's the natural order. And to be frank, the Realm has more enlightened social policies than the real world simply by embracing the LGBT part of LGBTQ: You are assumed to be who you say you are, and that cultural openness allows more flexibility than real-world gender roles by default.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want you to misrepresent my intentions. &quot;Role reversal&quot; (or reversing gender norms) is a standard exercise in gender- and intersectional studies, and it's especially important in my field of social work because it teaches us to evaluate our preconceptions so that we can be more objective towards our clients. It's a healthy exercise, and the purpose of the exercise is to learn how to see beyond social norms in your interaction with other individuals. But role reversal as an exercise and role reversal as a systematic reality are different things; one teaches you to evaluate destructive social norms and work to overcome them. The other encourages destructive social norms where the culprit-victim relationship has been swapped.<br /> <br /> That's my two cents, and it's the last I'll speak of it in this thread.<br /> <br /> Edit: I do agree with you about your individual points, though, but I wanted to clarify my line of thinking. I don't think we inherently disagree with each other about intersectionalism or feminism itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":482,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","user":"Ekorren","date":". 04-03-2018, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T09:56:50-07:00","id":1202631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1202538#post1202538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the new chapters are out. I guess my only criticism so far is with regards to the line &quot;He hadn't asked the Dragons to be born a man and his mother's only son!&quot; I've always tried to stay away from topics such as sexism, homophobia, and racism in my Exalted games, because those things exist in abundance in real life and I want my Exalted games to be an escape from the depressive reality. Simply reversing the traditional patriarchal society to a matriarchal one is in no way progressive. It's still a gender-based structural hierarchy but with the pronouns reversed, and it doesn't make the Realm a very attractive society for me to immerse myself in. I don't mind the details of marrying into the female's family because she's basically carrying the bloodline, or that it reflects in the matriarchs. I do want to stay away from topics that actively suppresses a gender before the other, though, or that involves characters cursing their own gender (which they have no control over) because of their societal norms. I'm studying to become a social worker in real life to be able to fully explore and deal with such issues. But when I play Exalted, I just want to be a mythic hero in a fantastic world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well to be clear, no one suggested it was progressive in-universe. The Realm is not progressive place. They\u2019re slaver imperialists. The goal with representing matriarchy well in fiction like this is to comment on patriarchy via its mirror, not present a better alternative.<br /> <br /> For example, the fact that 8 of the heads of houses are women, and two are men, is pretty consistent with the balance most fantasy settings would give in favor of men without even intentionally making it patriarchal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-03-2018, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T09:58:10-07:00","id":1202633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1202629#post1202629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want you to misrepresent my intentions. &quot;Role reversal&quot; (or reversing gender norms) is a standard exercise in gender- and intersectional studies, and it's especially important in my field of social work because it teaches us to evaluate our preconceptions so that we can be more objective towards our clients. It's a healthy exercise, and the purpose of the exercise is to learn how to see beyond social norms in your interaction with other individuals. But role reversal as an exercise and role reversal as a systematic reality are different things; one teaches you to evaluate destructive social norms and work to overcome them. The other encourages destructive social norms where the culprit-victim relationship has been swapped.<br /> <br /> That's my two cents, and it's the last I'll speak of it in this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think that's what's happening at all (it's not presented as a good thing in-universe, and not universal), but I get it. I'll drop it too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T10:06:40-07:00","id":1202637,"title":"","content":"I've got my fingers crossed that The Realm will have more information on third-tier secondary schools in the Threshold. A schooling system that creates a privileged (collaborator) class in the satrapies while also enforcing an imbalance of education between Cadet Houses and the Great Houses sounds absolutely fascinating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T10:18:04-07:00","id":1202639,"title":"","content":"Having read the description of Pasiap's Stair: The final exam where the students are pitted against each other, is that meant to have a deadly outcome? What I mean is, is the battle actually real or is it a glorified exercise? I think a real, violent battle would be more in line with common manga troupes, or Harry Potter's goblet game thingy. But wouldn't that put DBs at risk? Or maybe it doesn't matter if most of them are Outcastes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T10:20:49-07:00","id":1202641,"title":"","content":"It's a real battle, in the sense that people actually get stabbed, but they're expected to refrain from delivering killing blows. The Exalted resistance to dying of bleeding or sepsis comes in handy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T10:28:05-07:00","id":1202642,"title":"","content":"Still, slaves and legionnaires must die by the numbers. Goes to show the value of DBs to the Realm, even if they are Outcastes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T10:31:56-07:00","id":1202644,"title":"","content":"Pasiap's Stair is no joke, nor are its graduates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T11:37:17-07:00","id":1202658,"title":"","content":"Say, if we notice an error somewhere in the preview where are we supposed to send that info? Message them on the Kickstarter website?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T11:39:38-07:00","id":1202659,"title":"","content":"Nowhere. Save it until the final laid-out preview .pdf; apparently we don\u2019t want anyone reporting an error here, and then not reporting it during the big push to get the layout .pdf fixed because they remember reporting it here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T11:50:41-07:00","id":1202662,"title":"","content":"Ah, okay I'll save it until then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T12:47:11-07:00","id":1202687,"title":"","content":"I'll admit, I raised an eyebrow at the bit where the Great Houses turned up their noses at graduates of Pasiap's Stair. Like, they're part of a rare group of superhumans who have been trained since childhood to be really good at waging war. Why would you, in a time when civil war was imminent, not want as many in your employ as possible? The possibility that they might be more loyal to the Empress than your house doesn't strike me as that big a threat when there's no Empress to be loyal to. And surely, if you hand them a position of responsibility, treat them with respect, and pay them well (and maybe promise to fudge the rule that says they have to serve for 50 years), it would be easy enough to suborn them at least enough to get your money's worth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1529-srgrvsalot","name":"SrGrvsaLot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T12:59:06-07:00","id":1202692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SrGrvsaLot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1202687#post1202687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit, I raised an eyebrow at the bit where the Great Houses turned up their noses at graduates of Pasiap's Stair. Like, they're part of a rare group of superhumans who have been trained since childhood to be really good at waging war. Why would you, in a time when civil war was imminent, not want as many in your employ as possible? The possibility that they might be more loyal to the Empress than your house doesn't strike me as that big a threat when there's no Empress to be loyal to. And surely, if you hand them a position of responsibility, treat them with respect, and pay them well (and maybe promise to fudge the rule that says they have to serve for 50 years), it would be easy enough to suborn them at least enough to get your money's worth.</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019re expecting classist prejudice to be logical?<br /> <br /> It\u2019s been engrained for centuries that Lost Eggs are unfit for the Great Houses and are left to serve the Empress because it\u2019s not like they can climb the ladder of power themselves. Of course the real motivation here was so the Empress could cultivate powerful skilled agents completely loyal to her - but the social programming doesn\u2019t disappear in a proof of logic.<br /> <br /> It does provide an opportunity for those Houses that are able to get past said prejudice. Specifically V\u2019neef as it builds its ranks from scratch, and Tepet trying to rebuild.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T13:24:31-07:00","id":1202707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1202641#post1202641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a real battle, in the sense that people actually get stabbed, but they're expected to refrain from delivering killing blows. The Exalted resistance to dying of bleeding or sepsis comes in handy.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWould you say there's a convention or rule in which students who get a bad hit are expected to stay down, at which point they're supposed to be left alone, with the occasional one who keeps pushing themselves regardless and might invite more damage than they can survive?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T13:45:18-07:00","id":1202714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1202707#post1202707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bWould you say there's a convention or rule in which students who get a bad hit are expected to stay down, at which point they're supposed to be left alone, with the occasional one who keeps pushing themselves regardless and might invite more damage than they can survive?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm willing to bet that most students at that academy would be too proud to willingly stay down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T14:31:58-07:00","id":1202739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1202714#post1202714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm willing to bet that most students at that academy would be too proud to willingly stay down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the ones that lived to make it to the graduation 'party' anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T14:48:41-07:00","id":1202745,"title":"","content":"Am I alone in thinking that since they received one of the coveted Prestige Spreads, the Forest Witches would have gotten a section in the latest chapter? Between the section on Lookshy and the section of Outcastes? Or in the Outcaste section at least?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T15:00:43-07:00","id":1202751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1202745#post1202745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I alone in thinking that since they received one of the coveted Prestige Spreads, the Forest Witches would have gotten a section in the latest chapter? Between the section on Lookshy and the section of Outcastes? Or in the Outcaste section at least?</div> </div> </div> </div>That surprised me, but it\u2019s not that off from the other Exalted types getting their spreads in the corebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T15:24:13-07:00","id":1202758,"title":"","content":"Pasiap's Stair's curriculum leans heavily on instilling loyalty to the Realm in toto and to the Empress as an authority figure. The Houses are nervous about putting people with that sort of indoctrination in command