hogunate supplement","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T16:02:52-07:00","id":1202783,"title":"","content":"Prasad is getting detailed in the Realm supplement, in addition to the Heirs stretchgoals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T16:12:58-07:00","id":1202785,"title":"","content":"Ah, well works for me either way since I am getting both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T16:25:06-07:00","id":1202791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1202620#post1202620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think all the main 4 admit mortal students because there's always dynast parents going &amp;quot;she's definitely gonna exalt soon! Just give her a year or two!&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> A lot of late bloomers probably wind up in less prestigious schools because their parents couldn't swing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shades of \u201cFamiliar of Zero / Zero no Tsukaima\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T18:21:13-07:00","id":1202828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1202714#post1202714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm willing to bet that most students at that academy would be too proud to willingly stay down.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bMaybe if you took a bad hit embarrassingly early or against somebody you had a particular enmity against? Otherwise, what do you have to prove?<br /> <br /> \u200bHeck, from whence comes this pride? Did your peasant upbringing instil in you values of it being totally unforgivable to yield a fight under any circumstances? Are the instructors teaching you to be really up on yourself, such that being tagged out of a mock battle is a terrible insult? I can see at least two problems with that; seems like it would really hurt their graduate output, and not exactly be suitable for people intended to serve in the legions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1202739#post1202739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the ones that lived to make it to the graduation 'party' anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIt will certainly be the last thing you do before graduation, but don't overlook how the entire student body takes part. The final-years are just the generals, with the others filling lesser ranks.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T18:40:07-07:00","id":1202835,"title":"","content":"Idle note that I'm gonna have to mull on- but according to the preview, a *majority* of Dynastic Dragon-Blooded don't live to 100. That's... pretty steep. Especially with progenitive Essence's &quot;once a decade&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> Gonna have to tinker with my old demographic app thingy to see what hypothetical replacement rate exaltation rates look like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T18:51:29-07:00","id":1202840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1202835#post1202835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idle note that I'm gonna have to mull on- but according to the preview, a *majority* of Dynastic Dragon-Blooded don't live to 100. That's... pretty steep. Especially with progenitive Essence's &quot;once a decade&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> Gonna have to tinker with my old demographic app thingy to see what hypothetical replacement rate exaltation rates look like.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is probably a reason they bother offering the coin and razor to poorly bred mongrels from the sticks despite their clear and utter disdain for them. I wouldn't be shocked to find out that they would be dying at an unsustainable rate without having them around to handle so much of the fighting and danger for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T19:59:46-07:00","id":1202851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1202835#post1202835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idle note that I'm gonna have to mull on- but according to the preview, a *majority* of Dynastic Dragon-Blooded don't live to 100. That's... pretty steep. Especially with progenitive Essence's &quot;once a decade&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> Gonna have to tinker with my old demographic app thingy to see what hypothetical replacement exaltation rates look like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember too, even if the child does not exalt, the grandchildren and greatgrandchildren may, even from mortal-mortal pairings.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T21:23:20-07:00","id":1202865,"title":"","content":"I just realized something;<br /> <br /> In 1 and 2E, Sesus Nagezzer is a washed-up old fart who dealt with the stress of being a failure by the standards of his House by proving he was smarter than all of them put together.<br /> <br /> In 3e, Sesus Nagezzer is a washed-up old fart who dealt with the stress of having been a failure by the standards of his House by proving he was smarter than all of them put together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 04-04-2018, 12:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T23:14:32-07:00","id":1202882,"title":"","content":"I think we just had our first day without hitting a stretch goal....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T04:07:51-07:00","id":1202940,"title":"","content":"XD that would happen eventually; this rising curve felt a bit prolonged. The pace picks up again by the last week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T06:53:15-07:00","id":1202982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1202835#post1202835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idle note that I'm gonna have to mull on- but according to the preview, a *majority* of Dynastic Dragon-Blooded don't live to 100. That's... pretty steep. Especially with progenitive Essence's &quot;once a decade&quot; thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIt feels pretty steep if considered from the perspective of living for several centuries, but if viewed from the perspective of a real life/mortal life span, it's about what one might expect, and entirely sustainable.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat's how I'm viewing it; the majority of the Dynasty consisting of people whose length and experience of life corresponds approximately to a collection of individuals as I might know them (even if they all stay fresh and vital throughout), punctuated by the occasional venerable supernatural ancestor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T08:19:45-07:00","id":1203016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1202982#post1202982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bIt feels pretty steep if considered from the perspective of living for several centuries, but if viewed from the perspective of a real life/mortal life span, it's about what one might expect, and entirely sustainable.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat's how I'm viewing it; the majority of the Dynasty consisting of people whose length and experience of life corresponds approximately to a collection of individuals as I might know them (even if they all stay fresh and vital throughout), punctuated by the occasional venerable supernatural ancestor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it also matters as to *when* those deaths occur. Like, if there is a relatively low attrition rate from 20 to 40 (prime adventuring years), and then a steadily increasing rate from 40 to 100 (prime settled down with a family years), that squares, but man it means a helluva lot of assassination is going on.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, if there is a relatively high attrition rate from 20 to 40 and then a decline from 40 to 100, that pushes the 'assassination rate' down, but also means you're going to lose a number of friends from secondary school in relatively short order.<br /> <br /> I'm definitely going to toy with the app when I get a chance <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T08:40:34-07:00","id":1203020,"title":"","content":"New stretch goal time.<br /> <br /> $208k gets us a Dragon-Blooded novella.<br /> $214k gets us a second Outcastes expansion.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T10:35:02-07:00","id":1203059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1203016#post1203016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it also matters as to *when* those deaths occur. Like, if there is a relatively low attrition rate from 20 to 40 (prime adventuring years), and then a steadily increasing rate from 40 to 100 (prime settled down with a family years), that squares, but man it means a helluva lot of assassination is going on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that attrition need not be continuous. Events like the loss of the Tepet legions or the purge of the Iselsi are not unique, but merely the extreme end of a variety of intermittent major events.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T12:04:25-07:00","id":1203089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1203059#post1203059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that attrition need not be continuous. Events like the loss of the Tepet legions or the purge of the Iselsi are not unique, but merely the extreme end of a variety of intermittent major events.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Excellent point; I think I had been tinkering with relatively stable growth / death rates, but having periodic 'disasters' would probably be valuable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T12:14:44-07:00","id":1203092,"title":"","content":"200,000 achieved and they added new stretch goals, a novella and an expansion for out caste dragon blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T12:16:19-07:00","id":1203093,"title":"","content":"I've always held that the undisclosed period in which the number of legions rose to eighty was at least partially driven by a desire to bleed off an excess of Dynasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T13:32:55-07:00","id":1203115,"title":"","content":"Well, just finished reading the second preview- while I was a bit disappointed to not see anything new about Parsad and the Forest Witches, I did enjoyed quit a lot from the description of the many new Outcast groups, especially the Wanasaan. In fact, depending on how Heirs would turn out, they may even be my favorite Dragon Blooded organization (the title belongs to the Forest Witches for now, because I like weird things :P). Anyway, I liked the presentation so much that I bumped my pledge from the basic 5 to 40- so yeah, I'm expecting for a lot from this Kickstarter :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T08:49:38-07:00","id":1204191,"title":"","content":"I might have missed it, but has the Dragon-blooded manuscript previews actually discussed the Immaculate Dragons in detail yet? Like who they are in lore, which name assoicates with which element, etc? There's a lot of knowledge we carry over from previous editions, but I sometimes mix up 1 or 2 of the names myself and it occurs to me I'm not sure I (or someone new to the gameline) has anywhere to reference these names yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T08:52:16-07:00","id":1204192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1204191#post1204191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might have missed it, but has the Dragon-blooded manuscript previews actually discussed the Immaculate Dragons in detail yet? Like who they are in lore, which name assoicates with which element, etc? There's a lot of knowledge we carry over from previous editions, but I sometimes mix up 1 or 2 of the names myself and it occurs to me I'm not sure I (or someone new to the gameline) has anywhere to reference these names yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI expect more will be given in The Realm, but the basics of that info are actually in the core book's setting chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T08:57:44-07:00","id":1204193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1204192#post1204192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI expect more will be given in The Realm, but the basics of that info are actually in the core book's setting chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I knew it had to be somewhere, but I couldn't remember. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T09:05:25-07:00","id":1204195,"title":"","content":"Oh, speak of the Dragon, we've got a preview of The Realm's writing on the Order and all. <br /> <br /> \u200bThat resolves one question that I had on whether or not something that Holden said a while back was still going on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T09:22:17-07:00","id":1204198,"title":"","content":"Glad to see that the Dragon cults got mentioned. Although poor Hesiah apparently isn't too popular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T09:46:27-07:00","id":1204201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1204198#post1204198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glad to see that the Dragon cults got mentioned. Although poor Hesiah apparently isn't too popular.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well his domain is pretty esoteric and abstract for mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T09:57:50-07:00","id":1204206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1204195#post1204195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, speak of the Dragon, we've got a preview of The Realm's writing on the Order and all.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat resolves one question that I had on whether or not something that Holden said a while back was still going on.</div> </div> </div> </div>What did he say?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T11:20:44-07:00","id":1204235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VioletDreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1204206#post1204206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What did he say?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe whole part about how, if you're more deeply initiated in the Order's education, you have a more complete and accurate picture of the history of Creation, nature of the Solar and Lunar Exalted, and allegorical quality of the Immaculate Dragons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T11:37:24-07:00","id":1204237,"title":"","content":"The monks kinda sound like Father Brown crossed with an MI6 spook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T11:48:57-07:00","id":1204243,"title":"","content":"While I've never had the urge to play a monk, I do like the presentation of the Order- they look both merciful and terrifying, which is always a good combination. The way that the Order's members actually know the truth (or at least, a big part of it) about their religion makes them much more interesting, IMO, and I do like the different heresies presented in the book, and the &quot;illegal Dragon cults&quot; thing which is going on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T11:57:53-07:00","id":1204245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1204237#post1204237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The monks kinda sound like Father Brown crossed with an MI6 spook.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never seen Father Brown, but a brief Google investigation suggests that I really should.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T12:19:01-07:00","id":1204251,"title":"","content":"*Immaculate Order Preview*<br /> <br /> Wow. And the nominee for Best Fictional Religion goes to...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T13:20:50-07:00","id":1204273,"title":"","content":"They\u2019re Disraeli conservative functionalists. Tolkien would approve. In fact I can even see popular Immaculate-approved fiction in the Realm that reads like Lord of the Rings - with a self-sacrificing humble commoner protagonist POV character bearing heroic burden among epic Dragon-Blooded heroes who are reliant on him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T14:18:42-07:00","id":1204290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1204273#post1204273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> a self-sacrificing humble commoner protagonist POV character bearing heroic burden among epic Dragon-Blooded heroes who are reliant on him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sound like Journey to the West","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11671-dramaflo","name":"DraMaFlo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11671_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T14:49:50-07:00","id":1204304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DraMaFlo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1204290#post1204290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sound like Journey to the West</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean... kinda... but a monk on a spiritual journey isn't really the same thing as an idealized agriarian commoner nobly supporting the entire social hierarchy above him on his back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T17:06:24-07:00","id":1204339,"title":"","content":"I actually want to play an immaculate monk now<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, $210,686 has been surpassed","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T17:33:16-07:00","id":1204350,"title":"","content":"Sorcerer of the White Register tier available for anyone who still wants a Custom Charm but missed a slot previously!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T17:38:34-07:00","id":1204352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1204251#post1204251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Immaculate Order Preview*<br /> <br /> Wow. And the nominee for Best Fictional Religion goes to...</div> </div> </div> </div> Wow, that's incredibly high praise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1204273#post1204273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They\u2019re Disraeli conservative functionalists. Tolkien would approve. In fact I can even see popular Immaculate-approved fiction in the Realm that reads like Lord of the Rings - with a self-sacrificing humble commoner protagonist POV character bearing heroic burden among epic Dragon-Blooded heroes who are reliant on him.</div> </div> </div> </div> I actually included some more examination of Realm fiction in my draft for the chapter. Hopefully it makes it to the final product.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T17:46:53-07:00","id":1204356,"title":"","content":"The image of Immaculate monks going around the streets watching and judging people, trained to detect even minor hints of violating orthopraxy, puts me in mind of the Grammaton Clerics.<br /> <br /> \u200bI initially thought of the Dai Li, but they're a bit too shadowy and secretive.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, the material and its imagery stands on its own, I just like finding comparable visual reference points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T17:49:00-07:00","id":1204357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1204352#post1204352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Wow, that's incredibly high praise.<br /> <br /> I actually included some more examination of Realm fiction in my draft for the chapter. Hopefully it makes it to the final product.</div> </div> </div> </div>I take it you're the writer for this section? If you are, then you did a bang up job of writing up something evocative. Gave my imagination some fertile soil, so it serves its RPG purpose well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T18:01:31-07:00","id":1204363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1204352#post1204352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Wow, that's incredibly high praise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you mind commenting if the Intou heretics are just mentioned as a self-contained concept seed, or if they're something fleshed out in the book? I'm guessing the former since it doesn't have a page reference the way Prasad's Pure Way does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T18:21:00-07:00","id":1204366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1204357#post1204357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I take it you're the writer for this section? If you are, then you did a bang up job of writing up something evocative. Gave my imagination some fertile soil, so it serves its RPG purpose well.</div> </div> </div> </div> I appreciate you saying so. Thank you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1204363#post1204363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you mind commenting if the Intou heretics are just mentioned as a self-contained concept seed, or if they're something fleshed out in the book? I'm guessing the former since it doesn't have a page reference the way Prasad's Pure Way does.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't have the full text myself, and even if I did, the version I had wouldn't be up to date. I don't even have the most up-to-date text on this <i>chapter</i>, so the paragraphs on specific heresies were new to me. I think you're likely to get a glimpse of the Intou heresy in one of the upcoming Dragon-Blooded manuscript previews, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T18:28:09-07:00","id":1204372,"title":"","content":"<i>The Realm</i> doesn't elaborate on the Intou heresy, but I'm hoping an opportunity will arise in the setting book we're planning between <i>Lunars</i> and <i>Exigents</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T19:10:22-07:00","id":1204386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1204372#post1204372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>The Realm</i> doesn't elaborate on the Intou heresy, but I'm hoping an opportunity will arise in the setting book we're planning between <i>Lunars</i> and <i>Exigents</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gods &amp; Religions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T20:15:18-07:00","id":1204400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1204386#post1204386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gods &amp; Religions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that too, though we haven't written the pitch for that book yet.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T01:10:56-07:00","id":1204466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1204191#post1204191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might have missed it, but has the Dragon-blooded manuscript previews actually discussed the Immaculate Dragons in detail yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>In addition to what's in the core, the DB book seems to conflate the Immaculate Dragons and Elemental Dragons to a large degree, to the point where they use the Immaculate names for the Elemental Dragons. I don't know if this was how it was in previous editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T01:33:39-07:00","id":1204468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1204400#post1204400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, that too, though we haven't written the pitch for that book yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's not a book on gods and religions, what is the setting book you're planning between Lunars and Exigents?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T01:38:00-07:00","id":1204470,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that was the case in the old editions. The Immaculate Philosophy does conflate them, as do its adherants (the monks less than the laity).<br /> <br /> I should say, the names of the Immaculate Dragons <i>are</i> the same as the Elemental Dragons. Or rather, the Immaculate Dragons thought up by the Immaculates and Sidereals during the Shogunate were named after the Elemental Dragons, in order to benefit from the already-existing Dragon veneration of many Dragonblood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T03:22:55-07:00","id":1204488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1204466#post1204466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition to what's in the core, the DB book seems to conflate the Immaculate Dragons and Elemental Dragons to a large degree, to the point where they use the Immaculate names for the Elemental Dragons. I don't know if this was how it was in previous editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat's what Second Edition did, but where in Third have the Elemental Dragons been named at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T09:35:55-07:00","id":1204590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1204470#post1204470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should say, the names of the Immaculate Dragons <i>are</i> the same as the Elemental Dragons. Or rather, the Immaculate Dragons thought up by the Immaculates and Sidereals during the Shogunate were named after the Elemental Dragons, in order to benefit from the already-existing Dragon veneration of many Dragonblood.</div> </div> </div> </div> I had thought it was the reverse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T09:45:12-07:00","id":1204594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1204488#post1204488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThat's what Second Edition did, but where in Third have the Elemental Dragons been named at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I'm aware of? Even in the curretn DB book, it looks like the names are attributed to the Immaculate Dragons, but not hte Elemental Dragons themsleves, which as beings aren't relaly talked about much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T09:50:28-07:00","id":1204596,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Oh wow: I've only just looked at the update talking about developer ideas behind the outcastes, and I've got to say that I <i>really</i> like the design of Righteous River. It's stylized and distinctive, but in that verisimilitudous way that I like where it gives a mild impression of being grounded in realism.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's also nice to know that being an Immaculate monk doesn't need to mean that you aren't stylish. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T10:57:21-07:00","id":1204624,"title":"","content":"I'm wondering... if we get the T-shirts stretch goal, do we pay for T-shirts through the Kickstarter, or through the T-shirt manufacturer's website? If the former, I'll happily up my pledge now to cover a future spend. Is that how it's been handled before for similar stuff?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T11:29:36-07:00","id":1204635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1204624#post1204624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondering... if we get the T-shirts stretch goal, do we pay for T-shirts through the Kickstarter, or through the T-shirt manufacturer's website? If the former, I'll happily up my pledge now to cover a future spend. Is that how it's been handled before for similar stuff?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You go to our RedBubble store and buy a shirt from there. We put it at 0% markup, so we're not making anything from the sale*, you're just paying whatever RedBubble's costs are.<br /> <br /> *Unless you're also taking the opportunity to pick up one of our other fine products, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T12:41:19-07:00","id":1204650,"title":"","content":"So we're almost at the new bookmarks in the deluxe, which means more stretch goals should be forthcoming. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So if I have the count right then Prasad and the cadet houses still need to get their second expansion. After that what are you all hoping to see?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T12:51:27-07:00","id":1204653,"title":"","content":"1) all those sections to get another expansion<br /> <br /> 2) add martial arts styles to Heirs<br /> <br /> 3) i\u2019m assuming expanding the novella is in the cards<br /> <br /> 4) maybe get writeups for some relevant gods of the Isle, Prasad, etc?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T13:31:13-07:00","id":1204669,"title":"","content":"1) Charm cards. Those have been incredibly useful to my group and even if I just had a template where I could fill them in myself, they're just way better than a book or the line you get on a character sheet.<br /> <br /> 2) Cloth map addon. I can't have too many maps of Creation and we need a zoom of the Blessed Isle. Also I want more physical addons that I can use to raise my pledge to contribute more with a tangible reward.<br /> <br /> 3) I'll agree with glamourweaver with more Martial Arts. At least 1 or 2. <br /> <br /> 4) More generic (non-weapon/armor) Artifacts. Hearthstones. Arms gave us a great new take on these items and I want to see more, perhaps examples that are common among the Realm or Lookshy.<br /> <br /> 5) Artifact Weapons, Armor, and a Warstrider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T13:46:53-07:00","id":1204673,"title":"","content":"I really liked the paybump stretch goals from the Corebook KS. It seems like a nice sentiment, as I don\u2019t think RPG development pays very well in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T18:26:31-07:00","id":1204755,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't mind that kind of stretch goal either, though I'm not sure if Kickstarter likes stretch goals that are 'the money goes right into our personal pockets' or not. Has it been used in any of the other Onyx Path kickstarters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T18:28:48-07:00","id":1204756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1204755#post1204755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't mind that kind of stretch goal either, though I'm not sure if Kickstarter likes stretch goals that are 'the money goes right into our personal pockets' or not. Has it been used in any of the other Onyx Path kickstarters?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe original Exalted Kickstarted made giving the writers a bonus a stretch goal.<br /> <br /> \u200bStrictly speaking, it would not be what you're describing, because the writers and developers of this book aren't running the Kickstarter; Rich is. My impression is that he would not get any such money.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T10:07:13-07:00","id":1204896,"title":"","content":"New stretch goal at $221k is up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T10:39:06-07:00","id":1204908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1204896#post1204896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New stretch goal at $221k is up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;<b>REALM EXPANSION #1</b><span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">: War in the West \u2013 A section dealing with the impending war between House Peleps and House V\u2019neef </span></span></span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Huh, I did not see that coming. Neat!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T10:57:49-07:00","id":1204911,"title":"","content":"Damn, I wish those charm slots will sell. I have no doubt they will before the end, as people who haven\u2019t paid attention show up before the closing bell - but i\u2019m tempted to do something stupid like set up another Kickstarter account to buy another one...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T11:16:18-07:00","id":1204922,"title":"","content":"Have we had any clarification as to how the DB screen will differ (beyond artwork) from that offered as part of the Ex3 core Kickstarter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T11:37:20-07:00","id":1204925,"title":"","content":"I haven't seen anything, I imagine it may not very much though? As functionally mechanics are still the same, just the art is themed. Guess I have to wait to find out though, or make a post on the KS maybe about it :S.<br /> <br /> I asked for you so will see what they say ^^. Also need to get to 221k...that war in the west expansion looks like some little things being added to flesh it out! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13595-yawgrimas","user":"Yawgrimas","date":". 04-09-2018, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13595-yawgrimas","name":"Yawgrimas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T12:26:46-07:00","id":1204941,"title":"","content":"I must say that I'm really excited for the new stretch goal- the story hook of Peleps establishing their own Western Empire really got me- you go and play your little civil war, little kids. We are going to conquer the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T14:07:46-07:00","id":1204973,"title":"","content":"Additional stretchgoals added. Before the War in the West expansion, they\u2019ll be adding a new reward tier for more custom heirloom artifacts. After it they\u2019ll be adding more QS characters including Ragara and V\u2019neef themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T16:13:10-07:00","id":1205003,"title":"","content":"Oh man, custom artifacts are what will definitely get me to up my pledge!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T18:12:03-07:00","id":1205030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1204673#post1204673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really liked the paybump stretch goals from the Corebook KS. It seems like a nice sentiment, as I don\u2019t think RPG development pays very well in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those sorts of stretch goals tend to happen a fair bit further along in the KS than we are right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T18:13:23-07:00","id":1205032,"title":"","content":"I am kind of shocked that Karal Linwei wasn't already getting a QC write up, not like they have a plethora of more widely remembered characters to choose from when deciding who from Lookshy could get a QC write up in WFHW and whatever was going to be in the base dragon blooded companion. Guess that means we will mostly be getting Lookshy characters that didn't get any write ups in previous editions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T04:07:50-07:00","id":1205133,"title":"","content":"New Preview is up!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T04:44:40-07:00","id":1205140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205133#post1205133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Preview is up!</div> </div> </div> </div>And this time it is crunchy.<br /> <br /> Oh, there is fluff in the chapter fictions; showcasing some more nice slices of life for the signature kinship. Ah, also Mnemon gets some action with Novia ... blood and sorcery in Jiara!<br /> <br /> On to character creation, anima banners, traits, and charms. ... so many archery charms ... athletics, awareness, brawl, bureauocracy, craft, dodge, integrety, investigation, and... that's all for now. All? So much to digest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 04-10-2018, 08:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T05:16:03-07:00","id":1205145,"title":"","content":"Nearly 65 pages of Charms. As a quick reminder, Core had 60 pages for the same abilities (Archery -&gt; Investigation), so we're likely looking at no less than 150 pages.<br /> Man, this is going to be another hell of a doorstopper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3657-sagara","name":"Sagara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3657_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T05:57:10-07:00","id":1205154,"title":"","content":"I know most of you are skipping right ahead and reading the charms, and I can't hold that against anyone, but the thing that surprised me the most wasn't in the charm section, but in character creation... Dragon Blooded get 5 favored abilities... the same as Solars... I'll be completely honest... I did not see that one coming... I'm not complaining, I love the change, but oh boy, the character options it opens up!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T06:12:26-07:00","id":1205160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205154#post1205154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know most of you are skipping right ahead and reading the charms, and I can't hold that against anyone, but the thing that surprised me the most wasn't in the charm section, but in character creation... Dragon Blooded get 5 favored abilities... the same as Solars... I'll be completely honest... I did not see that one coming... I'm not complaining, I love the change, but oh boy, the character options it opens up!</div> </div> </div> </div>They can also get up to 18 Merits. They are pretty fancy.<br /> <br /> I'm still on Archery Charms at the moment, and I like most of what I read. The only thing I'm a bit torn on is that if feels like some of the Aspect anima powers aren't really balanced against each other. Some of them are REALLY good (like Earth's and Wood's anima flux) while others are a bit underwhelming (like Water's &quot;pay 3m for a non-Charm success to disengage&quot;). I'm overall glad that the anima powers are tuned down from 2E, but some are still vastly superior choices to others in most situations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T06:17:38-07:00","id":1205162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205154#post1205154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know most of you are skipping right ahead and reading the charms, and I can't hold that against anyone, but the thing that surprised me the most wasn't in the charm section, but in character creation... Dragon Blooded get 5 favored abilities... the same as Solars... I'll be completely honest... I did not see that one coming... I'm not complaining, I love the change, but oh boy, the character options it opens up!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I just did a quick count of pages, but am also reading in order. I haven't found a real penalty for DB's creation, except less flexibility in Aspect Abilities vs Solar Caste. roughly same amount of Attributes, Abilities and Charms, and there's actually an advantage Merit-wise.<br /> I'm guessing the real split is in the Charms' potency, and limitations in Sorcery, Martial Arts and Evocations. So in short, they're just as Exalted in their sheer natural ability, but they get a slightly less favorable powerset. Anyone's been tinkering with the Charms to confirm the power difference?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3657-sagara","name":"Sagara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3657_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T06:17:48-07:00","id":1205163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205154#post1205154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know most of you are skipping right ahead and reading the charms, and I can't hold that against anyone, but the thing that surprised me the most wasn't in the charm section, but in character creation... Dragon Blooded get 5 favored abilities... the same as Solars... I'll be completely honest... I did not see that one coming... I'm not complaining, I love the change, but oh boy, the character options it opens up!</div> </div> </div> </div>I came straight here as soon as I read that bit, because I wanted someone to assure me it wasn\u2019t a typo.<br /> <br /> It really will help with this idea that Aspect has less to do with individual personality and more to do with your parents. It encourages players to design characters with Aspects they wouldn\u2019t normally choose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T06:18:49-07:00","id":1205164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205154#post1205154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know most of you are skipping right ahead and reading the charms, and I can't hold that against anyone, but the thing that surprised me the most wasn't in the charm section, but in character creation... Dragon Blooded get 5 favored abilities... the same as Solars... I'll be completely honest... I did not see that one coming... I'm not complaining, I love the change, but oh boy, the character options it opens up!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The other interesting thing, from a homebrewer's perspective, is that Dragon-Blooded don't have the 'choose 5 of these 9 abilities as Aspect abilities'<br /> <br /> Also, hooray, breeding is no longer must buy!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T06:20:27-07:00","id":1205166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sagara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205145#post1205145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nearly 65 pages of Charms. As a quick reminder, Core had 60 pages for the same abilities (Archery -&gt; Investigation), so we're likely looking at no less than 150 pages.<br /> Man, this is going to be another hell of a doorstopper.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> OTOH, Dragon-Blooded Craft is a *helluva* smaller than Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T06:24:44-07:00","id":1205169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205160#post1205160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can also get up to 18 Merits. They are pretty fancy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes they can, but I wasn't surprised by them getting more Merits then Solars. They've gotten that since 1e, favored abilities though... they've been stuck @ 3 since the beginning, and I love that they are now more open to unique character concepts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm still on Archery Charms at the moment, and I like most of what I read. The only thing I'm a bit torn on is that if feels like some of the Aspect anima powers aren't really balanced against each other. Some of them are REALLY good (like Earth's and Wood's anima flux) while others are a bit underwhelming (like Water's &quot;pay 3m for a non-Charm success to disengage&quot;). I'm overall glad that the anima powers are tuned down from 2E, but some are still vastly superior choices to others in most situations. </div> </div> </div>You'll find that for each ability there is a dominant element, and 1-2 strong supporting elements, and the rest have only a handful of charms. Their entire charm set is designed that way. It allows them to have more powerful effects because of the limitations of Auras, and such.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T06:26:49-07:00","id":1205170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205166#post1205166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> OTOH, Dragon-Blooded Craft is a *helluva* smaller than Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So the Charm part is going to be even MORE immense? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, I really, REALLY want Glafira's sheet more than ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3657,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3657-sagara","user":"Sagara","date":". 04-10-2018, 09:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3657-sagara","name":"Sagara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3657_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T06:33:33-07:00","id":1205173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205154#post1205154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know most of you are skipping right ahead and reading the charms, and I can't hold that against anyone, but the thing that surprised me the most wasn't in the charm section, but in character creation... Dragon Blooded get 5 favored abilities... the same as Solars... I'll be completely honest... I did not see that one coming... I'm not complaining, I love the change, but oh boy, the character options it opens up!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, <i>right</i>, they only had 3 favoured in Ex2. Yes, <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">t</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">hey now have 5 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Aspect Abilities and 5 Favoured Abilities;\u200b and indeed <i>over all</i> t</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">he character creation </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">process for Essence 2 Dragonblooded is pretty much the same as for an Essence 1 Solar. Well, the Aspect Abilities are preselected by Aspect but they do get a few more specialties, merits, and bonus points to start with.</span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sagara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205162#post1205162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'm guessing the real split is in the Charms' potency, and limitations in Sorcery, Martial Arts and Evocations. So in short, they're just as Exalted in their sheer natural ability, but they get a slightly less favorable powerset. Anyone's been tinkering with the Charms to confirm the power difference?</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Only barely. A little less power for level, <i>maybe</i>, and there is a smaller mote pool to play with, but the Elemental Aura system looks promising and they do start at Essence 2 for every ability (versus having one supernal).</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 04-10-2018, 09:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T07:21:39-07:00","id":1205188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205163#post1205163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I came straight here as soon as I read that bit, because I wanted someone to assure me it wasn\u2019t a typo.<br /> <br /> It really will help with this idea that Aspect has less to do with individual personality and more to do with your parents. It encourages players to design characters with Aspects they wouldn\u2019t normally choose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I wanted to make a Water Aspected General, but I was afraid that the lack of Favored Abilities would make it so that I couldn't really pull it off, but now... So many directions that I can take every Aspect... I love this change!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T07:32:52-07:00","id":1205195,"title":"","content":"Ohhh goddammit; until I read the Charms, the forum is going to be insufferable!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T07:40:25-07:00","id":1205198,"title":"","content":"One limitation in dragon blooded charms comes from the aura mechanic. It boosts them, but also shuts off certain combos, because you can't combo an aura charm with a non-balanced aspect charm.<br /> <br /> To give an example from the preview, Unshakable Mountain Spine would be really good combined with the repurchase version of Grandmother Oak Exertion, but you can't use both at the same time because the former is an earth-aspect aura charm and the latter is a wood aspect charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T08:01:04-07:00","id":1205213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205198#post1205198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One limitation in dragon blooded charms comes from the aura mechanic. It boosts them, but also shuts off certain combos, because you can't combo an aura charm with a non-balanced aspect charm.<br /> <br /> To give an example from the preview, Unshakable Mountain Spine would be really good combined with the repurchase version of Grandmother Oak Exertion, but you can't use both at the same time because the former is an earth-aspect aura charm and the latter is a wood aspect charm.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, this, lower dice caps, and the lack of a Supernal ability, seem like big limiting factors for DB power compared to Solars, even with their starting stats/essence/merits/etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4115-flumpet38","name":"flumpet38","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T08:57:12-07:00","id":1205235,"title":"","content":"15 Custom Charm slots left (Sorcerer of the White Registry - $340)<br /> <br /> 10 Name an NPC slots (General of the Maelstrom Legion - $285)<br /> <br /> 6 pick a DB NPC to get a QC writeup left (1 Admiral of the Merchant Fleet - $375; 5 Admiral of the Fire Fleet - $425)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T09:04:41-07:00","id":1205241,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s a part of me that\u2019s sad that I missed the Panoply backer tier, but ...eh, what I really want is to get good enough at charm design so I can build my own and everything. While it might have been cool to force Vance to run with one of my concepts... even with design notes, I want Exigents more, I think.<br /> <br /> And making sure I get a DB charm I really wanted will be fun too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T09:05:27-07:00","id":1205242,"title":"","content":"Speaking of, who here got the Heirloom and Panoply tiers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T09:11:50-07:00","id":1205243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205166#post1205166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> OTOH, Dragon-Blooded Craft is a *helluva* smaller than Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank goodness for that. It seems they hit all the spots they need to as far as getting the dice bonuses needed for artifacts of 2 to 3 dots like they are supposed to without the bloat of the solar set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T09:27:02-07:00","id":1205248,"title":"","content":"I'm so happy Breeding is a social merit now. In my years of gaming I've grown to loathe things that provide a hard mechanical improvement but are meta-wise supposed to be few and far between (Breeding in DB and Werewolf, Virtues in 2E, etc)<br /> <br /> Also, Heart Eating Palm showing up in a chapter fiction is awesome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T09:32:31-07:00","id":1205254,"title":"","content":"I don't think a mote cost is necessary for Talents-to-Obols Refinement. That power could just as well simply be a permanent free effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T09:45:37-07:00","id":1205261,"title":"","content":"Found a typo.<br /> <br /> Firmament refers to the Heavens. The Earth is called the FUNDAMENT. As in \u201cfundamental\u201d and \u201cfoundational\u201d; the basic bedrock.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T10:37:19-07:00","id":1205287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205261#post1205261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Found a typo.<br /> <br /> Firmament refers to the Heavens. The Earth is called the FUNDAMENT. As in \u201cfundamental\u201d and \u201cfoundational\u201d; the basic bedrock.</div> </div> </div> </div>Save those for the Backer pdf, they won't track any reported errors until then","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T10:55:01-07:00","id":1205292,"title":"","content":"They kept the bonus points table consistent across splats... I feel like I owe somebody a big thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13326-aredin","name":"Aredin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T11:01:56-07:00","id":1205294,"title":"","content":"I don't understand the point of an Excellency keyword since it does absolutely nothing mechanically. Also just making you able to straight-up buy them seems like it's the same issue we've had two editions running of being a boring speedbump.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T11:08:03-07:00","id":1205297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kongurous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205294#post1205294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand the point of an Excellency keyword since it does absolutely nothing mechanically. Also just making you able to straight-up buy them seems like it's the same issue we've had two editions running of being a boring speedbump.</div> </div> </div> </div>Holden commented on this on rpg.net, having been involved in playtesting this before the developer changeover.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It did not work properly for DBs at <i>all</i> in playtesting. We found that people just leaned on the excellencies until their pools were empty and everything else about them ended up feeling really vestigial. Having a built-in &quot;fuck it, just driving the Essence bulldozer over this problem&quot; button feels <i>great</i> for Solars, but it made DBs just feel like cut-rate Solars. The more the DBs had to hustle to get their supernatural badass on, the better they felt in testing.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-10-2018, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T11:11:43-07:00","id":1205299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205297#post1205297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Holden commented on this on rpg.net, having been involved in playtesting this before the developer changeover.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, buying one charm sounds like a whole lot of hustle.<br /> <br /> Besides, you misunderstand what I'm suggesting. I'm not saying give them free access to excellencies like Solars. Rather, put dice adding effects onto other charms in the set, scatter them around, make it so you do have to work for hitting the full cap by investing and comboing the right charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T11:14:16-07:00","id":1205302,"title":"","content":"I'm surprised Spiral Academy has Presence on their Specialty list... I'd have thought Linguistics would fit better. Bureaucracy and Socialize are right on the money of course.<br /> <br /> Anyone want to help come up with the Specialty lists for the other Outcaste groups.... I'll start!<br /> <br /> Wanasaan: Integrity, Occult, Resistance<br /> <br /> <br /> Temple of the Reverent Whisper: Occult, Performance.... I'm not sure on the third. Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T11:21:28-07:00","id":1205305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kongurous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205299#post1205299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, buying one charm sounds like a whole lot of hustle.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's clearly not the &quot;hustle&quot; he was referring to. He was refering to how you can pick Excellencies to buy that fit your specific character concept, but you aren't starting with 10+ in addition to your Charms the way Solars do inherently, so you much less often have it as a crutch to lean on in play depending on the circumstance.<br /> <br /> As to your alternate suggestion, I need more time to read the charmset before I comment on that fully, but a quick glance seems to indicate that the Excellency Charms do indeed carry addition effects!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-10-2018, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T11:37:55-07:00","id":1205312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205305#post1205305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's clearly not the &quot;hustle&quot; he was referring to. He was refering to how you can pick Excellencies to buy that fit your specific character concept, but you aren't starting with 10+ in addition to your Charms the way Solars do inherently, so you much less often have it as a crutch to lean on in play depending on the circumstance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm talking to him elsewhere and he said I could post this: <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/VFVdVzE.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> As for them carrying additional effects, I know that, I read them. I kinda would have had to in order to even complain about this. That slightly sweetens the deal, but they're still bulk rate dice adders with a minor benny added, rather than the other way around, where I'd prefer &quot;NICE EFFECT YOU REALLY WANT also have an extra die.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T11:42:39-07:00","id":1205313,"title":"","content":"How would it be balanced to have more major effects and major dice adders in the same charm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T11:46:17-07:00","id":1205315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205313#post1205313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would it be balanced to have more major effects and major dice adders in the same charm?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think Kong means that you wouldn't have a complete excellency by itself, period. You'd have a numbre of charms, each adding 1-2 die, and by comboing them reach their dice limit. Personally, I prefer having the excellency+Quirk early, since excellencies are to me the defining trait of Exalted (next to expanding power sets).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T11:46:24-07:00","id":1205316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205313#post1205313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would it be balanced to have more major effects and major dice adders in the same charm?</div> </div> </div> </div>Please explain where in my words I proposed this, because I'm pretty sure what I said was &quot;NICE THING YOU REALLY WANT also have an extra die.&quot; As in, actually one extra die. 1. If you want to hit your dice cap, you need like 6 of these.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T11:47:07-07:00","id":1205317,"title":"","content":"Just a thought but I think the bigger issue may be the lack of actual/perceived benefit of charms outside of excellencies relative to the XP and mote cost. I am seeing a lot of charms both for Soiars and Dragonblooded that have such marginal benefits by themselves, are incredibly limited to rare situations, cost too many motes, will or heaven forbid initiative, are just too damn deep in the tree or some combination of these. It looks like the elemental nature of the ability trees has done a good job of flattening them (from the ones I've seen) but trying to sell anything that doesn't look like an excellency is gonna be rough.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>It did not work properly for DBs at </i><i>all</i><i> in playtesting. We found that people just leaned on the excellencies until their pools were empty and everything else about them ended up feeling really vestigial. <b>Having a built-in &quot;fuck it, just driving the Essence bulldozer over this problem&quot; button feels </b></i><b><i>great</i></b><i><b> for Solars, but it made DBs just feel like cut-rate Solars.</b> The more the DBs had to hustle to get their supernatural badass on, the better they felt in testing.</i><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Just to clarify, I'm trying to say this is a huge problem for both splats if the non-excellency charms aren't memorable enough to distinguish the two, whether it be by being frequently useful or just so awesome the raw impression of it sticks with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13326,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13326-aredin","user":"Aredin","date":". 04-10-2018, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13326-aredin","name":"Aredin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T11:56:42-07:00","id":1205320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kongurous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205316#post1205316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please explain where in my words I proposed this, because I'm pretty sure what I said was &quot;NICE THING YOU REALLY WANT also have an extra die.&quot; As in, actually one extra die. 1. If you want to hit your dice cap, you need like 6 of these.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I misunderstood what you were suggesting, Epee102 lay it out well, sorry for the miscommunication.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T12:11:23-07:00","id":1205325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205315#post1205315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think Kong means that you wouldn't have a complete excellency by itself, period. You'd have a numbre of charms, each adding 1-2 die, and by comboing them reach their dice limit. Personally, I prefer having the excellency+Quirk early, since excellencies are to me the defining trait of Exalted (next to expanding power sets).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the presentation of Solar Excellencies, as it just being a free thing you have as an option for most of your actions, helps you focus on the meat and potatoes of Solar Power. Like Thunder Bolt Attack Prana, Fivefold Bulwark Stance, or Reversal of Fortune.<br /> <br /> That said, folding in effects that could cost a Solar 3m (such as excellent strike) to a Dragon-Blooded's lower capped excellencies I think is going to make their &quot;Rollplay&quot; feel more interesting immediately. I've also always been a fan of having Dragon-Blooded be the splat with the most efficient, if lowest ceiling, excellency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13326-aredin","name":"Aredin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T12:34:04-07:00","id":1205329,"title":"","content":"The only potential problem I see with that would be you would then need to apply EFFECT YOU WANT on every roll in order to hit cap, which depending on how many charms you need to hit cap could kinda wash out their uses, because they'd need to be able to be used on every attack without much to do, otherwise you aren't able to hit cap often.<br /> <br /> Then you would need to have more charms that add 1 die than needed to hit cap, so that you could pick and choose.<br /> <br /> While this is a viable design, and I could see how that could be interesting for some people, having to sift through all of my powers just to get all the dice I want to throw at this sounds like it might slow down play to me.<br /> <br /> Another alternative would be having a couple different excellency type charms that don't give you full cap, but can only be used in certain situations... wait I just described Infernal excellencies. That is not a gameplay feature I would want farmed out to every character type, not that I don't think it works, just doesn't work for everything.<br /> <br /> TL;DR That idea has merits, but it's own set of issues. At the end of the day I like what we got.<br /> <br /> edit: for completionist sake, and to ensure I don't come off as strawmanning, if the alternative was &quot;EFFECT YOU WANT and NOW YOU HAVE UNLOCKED ONE MORE DIE ON YOUR EXCELLENCY BUT YOU DON'T HAVE TO USE THIS CHARM TO USE IT&quot; that is less tedious, but it puts a second progression roadblock to getting to your dicecap, the actual cap itself, and buying up the charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":1542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","user":"MoroseMorgan","date":". 04-10-2018, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T12:47:59-07:00","id":1205335,"title":"","content":"I'll probably just houserule the need to buy the excellencies as seperate charms out in my game and give them out for free on the same grounds solars get them. The way they did approach the excellency issue makes that approach extremly easy at the least, which is a plus in my book when it comes to design descisions that are bound to be controversial, such as this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T13:00:13-07:00","id":1205340,"title":"","content":"Also, still not really enthused by the addition of a keyword that doesn't actually do anything except add noise to the charm. Is it really that valuable of an addition to declare a charm is an excellency?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T13:06:37-07:00","id":1205344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kongurous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205340#post1205340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, still not really enthused by the addition of a keyword that doesn't actually do anything except add noise to the charm. Is it really that valuable of an addition to declare a charm is an excellency?</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC there were supposed to be effects that call out Excellency tagged charms specifically, so while it might not have saved wordcount on the excellency charms themselves, it was supposed to save wordcount on the other charms that invoke them.<br /> <br /> I'm not done with the preview yet, so I don't think I've seen any that use it, but that was what it was for.<br /> <br /> That said, I too am against unnecessary and circuitous keywords, especially when they seem to cause more confusion than they solve, with the recent question about Perilous as an example.<br /> <br /> edit: now that I think about it further, it might have been for Evocations, so that they can just say &quot;excellency&quot; instead of &quot;excellency and this specific DB charm.&quot;, but I'll keep reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":1542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","user":"MoroseMorgan","date":". 04-10-2018, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T13:09:28-07:00","id":1205346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sagara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205145#post1205145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nearly 65 pages of Charms. As a quick reminder, Core had 60 pages for the same abilities (Archery -&gt; Investigation), so we're likely looking at no less than 150 pages.<br /> Man, this is going to be another hell of a doorstopper.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know I'm 2 pages late on this, but bare in mind that pages in the manuscript do NOT equal pages in the finished book. Text will be smaller, formatted differently and laid out as such to fit more words on a page. 60 pages in the Manuscript will likely work out to something closer to 40 pages in the book. (Math pulled from the very distant memory I have of the similarly formatted playtest documents compared to the core book, so could be off, but the core concept is sound)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T13:35:31-07:00","id":1205356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kongurous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205340#post1205340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, still not really enthused by the addition of a keyword that doesn't actually do anything except add noise to the charm. Is it really that valuable of an addition to declare a charm is an excellency?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's value is entirely centered around ctrl+F","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13326-aredin","name":"Aredin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T13:44:41-07:00","id":1205358,"title":"","content":"There are a couple of solar charms that care about whether a charm is an excellency or not. The keyword is important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T13:48:33-07:00","id":1205359,"title":"","content":"Others can elaborate further, but when I got into playtesting the current slate of Charms, splitting the effects of an Excellency up into multiple Charms weakened the Dragon-Blooded and made them split an already painfully thin mote pool. It didn\u2019t add anything and the issue of before wasn\u2019t an issue in this Charmset. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kongurous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205340#post1205340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, still not really enthused by the addition of a keyword that doesn't actually do anything except add noise to the charm. Is it really that valuable of an addition to declare a charm is an excellency?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Several Solar Charms address interacting with Excellencies or Excellency-type magics; future Charms may do the same. This means you don\u2019t have to specify dice caps every time you talk about a Charm; it\u2019s just to the Excellency rating. <br /> <br /> Cheap and efficient diceadders are sort of a hallmark of the Exalted. Whether that curious aspect stays as a piece of design I don\u2019t know, but it\u2019s an interesting curio of design and one that speaks to an Exalt\u2019s primacy in the power tiers of the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T13:49:00-07:00","id":1205360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205346#post1205346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know I'm 2 pages late on this, but bare in mind that pages in the manuscript do NOT equal pages in the finished book. Text will be smaller, formatted differently and laid out as such to fit more words on a page. 60 pages in the Manuscript will likely work out to something closer to 40 pages in the book. (Math pulled from the very distant memory I have of the similarly formatted playtest documents compared to the core book, so could be off, but the core concept is sound)</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, and in fact I notice that, generally, the DB charms are written in a shorter way than the Solar charms were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T14:16:42-07:00","id":1205361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205360#post1205360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, and in fact I notice that, generally, the DB charms are written in a shorter way than the Solar charms were.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and also, as far as I went, they are much easier to read, similar to AotC. It's still a bit of a slog to read through, but not the nightmare than Core 3 was.<br /> Also, to quickly go back to the pagecount thing, it's actually the reason I compared sizes for Archery -&gt; Investigation for Core and WFhW, to get a rough estimate as to how long we can expect the DB Charm chapter to be. 150+ pages still sounds a reasonable ballpark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3657-sagara","name":"Sagara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3657_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T14:21:04-07:00","id":1205363,"title":"","content":"I'm finding myself underwhelmed by these Charms. Very little has jumped out at me as particularly impressive so far.<br /> <br /> The Shells-for-Silver/Blazing Hoard of Hesiesh combo is nice, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T15:40:06-07:00","id":1205395,"title":"","content":"The fire aspect dodge signature makes you explode.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T16:50:27-07:00","id":1205420,"title":"","content":"So, I decided to go through the Charms we have so far and count their number per Ability and Essence rating...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><u>Archery</u></span></b><br /> <b>E1:</b> 6<br /> <b>E2:</b> 4<br /> <b>E3:</b> 8<br /> <b>E4:</b> 1<br /> <b>E5:</b> 2<br /> <u><i>Total:</i></u><i> 21</i><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><u>Athletics</u></span></b><br /> <b>E1:</b> 7<br /> <b>E2:</b> 2<br /> <b>E3:</b> 6<br /> <b>E4:</b> 1<br /> <b>E5:</b> 1<br /> <u><i>Total:</i></u><i> 17 </i><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><u>Awareness</u></span></b><br /> <b>E1:</b> 4<br /> <b>E2:</b> 3<br /> <b>E3:</b> 9<br /> <b>E4:</b> 0<br /> <b>E5:</b> 1<br /> <u><i>Total:</i></u><i> 17 </i><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><u>Brawl</u></span></b><br /> <b>E1:</b> 6<br /> <b>E2:</b> 6<br /> <b>E3:</b> 9<br /> <b>E4:</b> 2<br /> <b>E5:</b> 1<br /> <u><i>Total:</i></u><i> 24</i><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><u>Bureaucracy</u></span></b><br /> <b>E1:</b> 4<br /> <b>E2:</b> 6<br /> <b>E3:</b> 11<br /> <b>E4:</b> 3<br /> <b>E5:</b> 0<br /> <u><i>Total:</i></u><i> 24 </i><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><u>Craft</u></span></b><br /> <b>E1:</b> 3<br /> <b>E2:</b> 7<br /> <b>E3:</b> 7<br /> <b>E4:</b> 0<br /> <b>E5:</b> 0<br /> <u><i>Total:</i></u><i> 17 </i><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><u>Dodge</u></span></b><br /> <b>E1:</b> 3<br /> <b>E2:</b> 3<br /> <b>E3:</b> 8<br /> <b>E4:</b> 1<br /> <b>E5:</b> 1<br /> <u><i>Total:</i></u><i> 16</i><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><u>Integrity</u></span></b><br /> <b>E1:</b> 4<br /> <b>E2:</b> 6<br /> <b>E3:</b> 7<br /> <b>E4:</b> 1<br /> <b>E5:</b> 0<br /> <u><i>Total:</i></u><i> 18</i><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><u>Investigation</u></span></b><br /> <b>E1:</b> 3<br /> <b>E2:</b> 5<br /> <b>E3:</b> 10<br /> <b>E4:</b> 1<br /> <b>E5:</b> 1<br /> <u><i>Total:</i></u><i> 20</i> </div> </div> </div>As expected, most of the Charms are concentrated at lower levels... except for Essence 3 since that's where the Signature Charms are. Which surprised me, but since each Ability has several and you can't take them all, it makes sense.<br /> <br /> I don't know where to find a count of Solar Charms for comparison, but going from memory, the size of the Dragon-Blooded trees is much more uniform than for Solars, which I like. There are very few Charms above Essence 3, which is a little disappointing. I do like how the trees tend to narrow towards a short path of mastery after Essence 3, though, and how you can get an extra Signature Charm at Essence 5 so that milestone is significant for everyone... I just wish at least some of the Abilities had one or two more Charms to round them out at the top.<br /> <br /> I think the Charm trees are smaller overall too, but I'm not sure by how much. While I liked having a lot of Charms to pick from for Solars, they could get pretty dense, and the Dragon-Blooded set looks like it will be much easier to absorb. That's a big positive, so I don't think I'll mind the relatively smaller selection too much.<br /> <br /> ...I haven't actually given the new Charms a proper read-through yet, though. I should do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/157-phoenix_kensai","name":"Phoenix_Kensai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar157_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T16:57:39-07:00","id":1205421,"title":"","content":"I really like the bottom heavy charm trees. Mostly because absent supernal abilities and considering just how much damn xp it takes to even reach essence 3, 95% of the time those charms are going to be in the hands of old NPCs anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T16:59:02-07:00","id":1205422,"title":"","content":"New stretch goal<br /> <br /> <b>At $231,000 in funding - HEIRS TO THE SHOGUNATE \u2013 LOOKSHY EXPANSION #3</b>: A section on the gentes and individual Lookshyans of note will be added to the Dragon-Blooded Companion PDF.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T19:46:32-07:00","id":1205444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205422#post1205422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New stretch goal<br /> <br /> <b>At $231,000 in funding - HEIRS TO THE SHOGUNATE \u2013 LOOKSHY EXPANSION #3</b>: A section on the gentes and individual Lookshyans of note will be added to the Dragon-Blooded Companion PDF.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think out of everything listed thus far, it's what I want to see most. I want to see Gentes be given the same attention that Dynastic houses have been.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13326-aredin","name":"Aredin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T00:16:25-07:00","id":1205481,"title":"","content":"Ok, I'm done with my first read of Charms and first impression is positive. A couple things I did note is how freaking complex the entire thing can be. While Solars were hard to digest due to the breadth of Charms available (and the meandering text), DBs have left me dazed by its depth. I mean, you got the Excellency Charms (okay, nothing too rough), then comes in talk about Cascades (par for the course), then Elemental Aspect (so far so good) that bleed into the concept of Aura.<br /> <br /> And that's when things get really complex to parse - It's clear there's a desire to create a flow to Charm use, with Aura Charms being big follow-ups to an &quot;upkeep phase&quot; to set yourself up. So you can split your charms by Ability, by Essence, but also importantly by Elemental Aspect and by Aura (At least to have a plan on how you intend to activate Arrow Raid Tempest). Add to THAT the Balanced keyword that allows a Charm to a) not disturb Aura, but b)still allows to build its specific Aura, and considering how making Charms we're likely to get, and it feels really necessary to have a long, deep thought before commiting to Charms, especially Aura Charms.<br /> <br /> To draw a parallel, it feels like DBs are going to be &quot;expert Exalts&quot;, not adviced for newer players without supervision. Or like noted above, they'll have to go for the more simple options of Martial Arts or Sorcery to avoid the whole Aura shting until they're ready to handle it. It leaves me wondering whether that's a design intent, and gets me thinking that maybe splitting Charms by Ability was not the best solution. Then again, splitting by Element isn't a great idea either, nor by Aura. Maybe a fully filterable database would help. Going back to Archery Water:<br /> <br /> &quot;Oooh so I got an archer, what's the cool Archery Charms? Oh, Arrow Rain Tempest looks cool! Wait, how am I supposed to have Water Aura? Oh I could use Death From Nowhere or Fang-of-the-Dephts. Oh, but I can use Unobtruscted Hunter's Aim too. Or Arrow Thorn. Wait, couldn't I use Water Brawl Charms one turn and start aiming for Arrow Rain the next? What is there in Brawl to use that's Water-compatible?&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm going to start something up focused purely on Attribute, Essence and Element, probably Excel to keep the technical low for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3657-sagara","name":"Sagara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3657_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T06:14:05-07:00","id":1205560,"title":"","content":"It is an extra layer of complexity to the db charmset, I agree. I have to see it in play to see how it flows.<br /> One thing I am sure: Colored border charm cards. Border indicates element (gray for neutral, wizards be damned). Balanced charms are half-element, half-gray. Aura charms have a badge to indicate that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T10:21:01-07:00","id":1205651,"title":"","content":"Given that they have actual schools for learning and using charms strategically, I can easily see them being the splat for having a low floor and a relatively high skill cap in potential when using coordinated attack/problem solving strategies.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13326-aredin","name":"Aredin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T10:42:03-07:00","id":1205665,"title":"","content":"You know, I've never been very fond of pyromancy as a power. It's incredibly common in fiction (whether used by protagonists, antagonists, or monsters), involves little more than slinging flames, is strong against a huge variety of beings (undead, plants, ice creatures, and also scary, in a very rational way, to animals and humans), and always conjures the same traits - red and orange colors, hot-blooded personalities, flames, fights, passion, etc. I'm much more drawn to air and earth as elements, being interpreted with more creativity, and maybe even more open to metaphorical or physical expressions rather than the very materialist and immediate nature of shit's burning yo.<br /> Now that's out of the way...<br /> ... having just backed the Kickstarter to see the previews, I love a bunch of things about Fire Aspects, from the aesthetics (fire is also smoke and ashes and... incense, now that's new and very welcome) to the aspected Charms (dodge explosions and violence-backed investigation and risky rewarding crafting and integrity-powered berserk and and) to a bunch of stuff and now I'm envisioning making a Fire-Aspected characters and what have you folks done to me.<br /> WHAT HAVE YOU DONE TO ME.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T10:50:42-07:00","id":1205673,"title":"","content":"You can track aura pretty easily using a D6. One side for each element, one for &quot;none&quot;.<br /> <br /> I mocked one up using bits of post-it notes but you can also paint one or just assign each value an element.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T11:30:40-07:00","id":1205692,"title":"","content":"It wasn't until I read the Brawl charm Crushing Avalanche Grasp that I realized I've been playing Grappling wrong this whole time. We've not been removing rounds of control from incoming attacks. Grappling feels <i>slightly </i>less godly powerful now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T12:05:27-07:00","id":1205702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205363#post1205363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm finding myself underwhelmed by these Charms. Very little has jumped out at me as particularly impressive so far.<br /> <br /> The Shells-for-Silver/Blazing Hoard of Hesiesh combo is nice, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue of having the lower-power Exalts is that, compared to Solars, their charms are likely to feel underwhelming.<br /> <br /> I found it a little like that myself... except that I've found the signature charms very interesting. They seem, generally, the most interesting (and wackiest) parts of a lot of the trees.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T12:05:27-07:00","id":1205703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205363#post1205363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm finding myself underwhelmed by these Charms. Very little has jumped out at me as particularly impressive so far.<br /> <br /> The Shells-for-Silver/Blazing Hoard of Hesiesh combo is nice, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue of having the lower-power Exalts is that, compared to Solars, their charms are likely to feel underwhelming.<br /> <br /> I found it a little like that myself... except that I've found the signature charms very interesting. They seem, generally, the most interesting (and wackiest) parts of a lot of the trees.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T12:21:04-07:00","id":1205706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205363#post1205363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm finding myself underwhelmed by these Charms. Very little has jumped out at me as particularly impressive so far.<br /> <br /> The Shells-for-Silver/Blazing Hoard of Hesiesh combo is nice, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well we knew that the gap between DBs and Solars will still be significant, although smaller in this edition. Its exactly there I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T13:49:30-07:00","id":1205741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205673#post1205673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can track aura pretty easily using a D6. One side for each element, one for &quot;none&quot;.<br /> <br /> I mocked one up using bits of post-it notes but you can also paint one or just assign each value an element.</div> </div> </div> </div>Supposing that was mostly aimed at my last comment (if not, well, apologies), I meant complex in the character creation phase. Now that I'm done with my Excell for Auras, I've come to realize that it might become a slight issue to activate the Air and Fire Brawl Signatures (as they require their Aura, something that no Brawl Charm can provide).<br /> <br /> So you could technically have Charms you're completely unable to activate. To as lesser extreme, you could have Charms that are hella hard to activate, requiring cross-ability planning (Setting up Air or Fire Aura via Dodge/Athletics/Archery). I would be *very* worried at leaving the DB book in a novice's hands, even more so than the Core book, and have him shoot himself in the foot.<br /> <br /> Now, once THAT hurdle is cleared, yeah, it's not *overly* complex to track and plan for during a fight. Which IS nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3657-sagara","name":"Sagara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3657_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T14:24:37-07:00","id":1205752,"title":"","content":"Definitely leaning toward letting PCs, and significant NPCs matched against the PCs in progression, have access to 1 signature Charm while still at Essence 2, to reflect being prodigies.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t want to hate off the coolest toys, but I also don\u2019t want to start at Essence 3, so unless there\u2019s some trap here i\u2019m missing, that seems like the best compromise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T14:43:30-07:00","id":1205761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackheartz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205706#post1205706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well we knew that the gap between DBs and Solars will still be significant, although smaller in this edition. Its exactly there I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that this will be the dominant (ubiquitous) take on the forums, but that's not what I'm seeing in the text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","name":"Equitable Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T14:46:58-07:00","id":1205762,"title":"","content":"Sorry about the near double-post, but I'm done with the worksheet. It's very bare-bones in a &quot;Jim, I'm a database manager, not a graphic designer&quot; way, and I still need a few answers to confirm some of my interpretation (of the texts), but it should give a rough idea as to what is what.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1GzFxtr8ACZnTPQboDuND6ViOOLXhfaS7LnVr0k4yeLQ/edit#gid=0\" target=\"_blank\">Here's the thing. PEACH and all that!</a><br /> <br /> Couple of things I noticed is that Aura is really only present in combat skills (which makes sense) and combat-applicable skills. Most of the Charms requiring Aura are actually fairly easy to set up inside their own skills, with a few outliers (looking at you, Air and Fire Brawl). One thing that's also going to be interesting is how Dodge being Fire-heavy will influence combat choices, since once you're commited to a specific Aura (say, Wood for an archer), you can't afford to activate Fire Dodge Charms without effing up your Aura. Thank the Dragons the Excellencies are all Balanced...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3657-sagara","name":"Sagara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3657_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T15:04:32-07:00","id":1205768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205761#post1205761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that this will be the dominant (ubiquitous) take on the forums, but that's not what I'm seeing in the text.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their key defenses don\u2019t stop working against opponents strong enough for said defenses to be needed against - that objectively makes Dragon-Blooded more powerful than they used to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T15:05:27-07:00","id":1205770,"title":"","content":"So looking through the new DB charms, how many building fires do you think get started because Hesieh's Discerning Tongue causes the poisoned thing in the DB's mouth to immediately catch fire before they spit it out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T15:08:56-07:00","id":1205773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aredin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205651#post1205651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that they have actual schools for learning and using charms strategically</div> </div> </div> </div>I would actually be very interested in how the Dragon-Blooded talk about and codify their essence-use techniques within the setting.<br /> <br /> Previously, I had assumed they approached them in the same way they did Martial Arts; you had savants and sifus who had dedicated their lives to understanding their Exaltations and how to draw forth its power, and they were heirs to centuries of savants and sifus who did the same thing. So, like, you'd get things like &quot;If you do these exercises, and meditate on the nature of your essence and your Exaltation, and align your essence in the proper ways, you will eventually learn to call it forth in the manner prescribed by our illustrious ancestors as the most puissant Charm known as the Become-the-Hammer technique. It is only through mastering this Charm that your essence will be enlightened sufficiently for you to attempt to express it in the ways prescribed as the Charms Pounding Surf Style or Water Dragon's Coils. Now punch this basket full of sand eight thousand times while meditating on the sutras I have taught you.&quot;<br /> <br /> But this isn't the case; the book goes out of its way to say &quot;Charms aren't codified techniques.&quot; And it's like... okay. If they're not codified techniques, how on earth do you even begin to teach them to people? MANY people at a time; Dragon-Blooded are educated in classroom settings. How do you measure their success and progress? How do you tell a struggling student &quot;no, that won't work; you need to do THIS instead.&quot; How do they talk about this stuff? How do the savants and sifus who delve into the mysteries of the Exaltation and the practical matters of educating the next generations of Princes in their use?<br /> <br /> We used to know that in prior editions, but now we do not and it bothers me.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T15:43:02-07:00","id":1205791,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure the schools teach people how to actually do the things their Abilities enable them to do, and their success is measured by their actual success in learning those things. You don't learn 3 War Charms at the House of Bells, you learn how to wage war, and the new ways your Essence helps you do that are manifestations of your excellence in that arena. Or something like that!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T17:45:01-07:00","id":1205840,"title":"","content":"What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23657_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23657\" data-vbnamecard=\"23657\">VioletDreamer</a> said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T17:52:38-07:00","id":1205844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205770#post1205770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So looking through the new DB charms, how many building fires do you think get started because Hesieh's Discerning Tongue causes the poisoned thing in the DB's mouth to immediately catch fire before they spit it out?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why DB's tend to build things out of stone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T17:55:11-07:00","id":1205847,"title":"","content":"I'm playing around with some houserules, because the &quot;Just Hatched&quot; rules don't really do what I'd want with school-aged campaign<br /> <br /> Recently Exalted tweens:<br /> <br /> - attributes 6/4/3<br /> - 15 ability dots<br /> - 2 specialties<br /> - 5 Merit dots<br /> - 4 Charms<br /> - Essence 1<br /> - 10 bonus points<br /> <br /> Late teens, 5 years or so into their education (if applicable):<br /> <br /> - attributes 7/5/3<br /> - 20 ability dots<br /> - 4 specialties (1 from school or background if applicable)<br /> - 7 Merit dots<br /> - 10 Charms (none at Essence 2 without spending bonus points)<br /> - Essence 2<br /> - 15 bonus points","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T18:29:34-07:00","id":1205856,"title":"","content":"Where does it say that schools teach Charms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T19:17:34-07:00","id":1205866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VioletDreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205791#post1205791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure the schools teach people how to actually do the things their Abilities enable them to do, and their success is measured by their actual success in learning those things. You don't learn 3 War Charms at the House of Bells, you learn how to wage war, and the new ways your Essence helps you do that are manifestations of your excellence in that arena. Or something like that!</div> </div> </div> </div>This carries with it the implication that learning to master your essence is a direct outgrowth of learning to do the thing in the same way mortals do, and to educate a Dragon-Blood to master and express their essence you just teach them to do the thing the way mortals do it and they'll pick up everything else a non-mortal can do on their own.<br /> <br /> And I mean, it is clearly true that Exalts can self-educate, that all Exalt types have a great deal of ability to figure out how to master their essence to do the thing without someone instructing them or helping them to do the thing. This has always been a thing, it's how the vast majority of Solars have always come into their power.<br /> <br /> But I'm not sure it makes sense that this is the ONLY way to learn to do the thing?<br /> <br /> Like... okay, to pick an ability at random. Craft. Let's say you want to build stuff. A worthy ambition for a Prince of the Earth, Pasiap would be proud of you. You begin to learn woodworking.<br /> <br /> You pick up the actual craft of woodworking relatively quickly, but you struggle with harmonizing your essence with it. Everyone else in the class can do that thing where they just... pick up a block of wood and carve it into what they want using their bare hands and their essence. You can't do this; you just break a lot of blocks in wood in half. You go to your sifu and say &quot;Sifu, I can carve this block of wood with knife, rasp, and plane in a skillful way; you yourself have nodded at my work and pronounced it acceptable. But I cannot express my essence to aid me in the way that you can and that my fellow Princes of the Earth can. You are my sifu; what am I doing wrong? How may I do better?&quot;<br /> <br /> It seems like the sifu should have an actual answer for them that's relevant to them <i>as an Exalt.</i> They should be able to identify the specific way the younger Exalt is attempting to express their essence and give them specific techniques and guidance that are relevant for them to be able to do the thing. The Dragon-Blooded care very much about education their next generation; so do the Sidereals, for that matter. It seems both logical and desirable that they'd have invested considerable resources into figuring out the best ways to do so that are relevant to the special things they can do <i>as an Exalt</i> that mortals cannot.<br /> <br /> Staying with Craft... Craft has Ephemeral Form Composition. Ephemeral Form Composition is very specifically just straight-up <i>magic</i>. You literally, not figuratively, turn your anima, something that, as an Exalt, you have unique control over, into a three-dimensional blueprint that you can manipulate using only your mind. No mortal is ever going to teach you how to do that, but it seems, I dunno, like it makes sense that your Exalted sifu ought to be able to teach you the technique through methods other than &quot;just... get real good at regular blueprint drawing and it'll come to you.&quot;<br /> <br /> This isn't just relevant to a classroom setting; the younger Exalts are going to look at their elders and see them perform miracles, and the elders are telling the younger ones that these miracles are their birthrights. The younger ones are gonna go &quot;Teach me how to do <i>that</i> one!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where does it say that schools teach Charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't directly, except for the Heptagram. (Learning Sorcery requires at least ONE Charm.) But the secondary schools exist for the purpose of education Dragon-Blooded Dynasts. Presumably they are... taught to express their essence at them, to master and control their might as Princes of the Earth.<br /> <br /> I don't think I'm out of line for making the assumption.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T19:34:32-07:00","id":1205873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205866#post1205866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't directly, except for the Heptagram. (Learning Sorcery requires at least ONE Charm.) But the secondary schools exist for the purpose of education Dragon-Blooded Dynasts. Presumably they are... taught to express their essence at them, to master and control their might as Princes of the Earth.<br /> <br /> I don't think I'm out of line for making the assumption.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Heptagram doesn't teach a Charm, it tries to teach you sorcery. That's an important distinction that's more consistent with the other material. Exalted and unexalted both learn sorcery with the incidental expression of that on the game's mechanical end being a Charm and a Merit.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I think for your other point that their education doesn't really work that way? And that given the way charms are described and how the core set is not exhaustive that there's an idea that the Chosen express their excellence in myriad ways. The manifested excellence of the group in the classroom would probably take on half a dozen different forms abstractly, and it wouldn't be about how to acquire HIS mastery or HER mastery, but simply about unlocking your own potential through your excellence, and whatever they come away with is true to them, or some kind of thing like that.<br /> <br /> But I also think that if that kid <i>really wants </i>to learn how to do that thing that his friend did, he'll probably just gain that capability or something like it ultimately, and the Secondary Schools don't push for it.<br /> <br /> I'm sure if it really mattered and they felt like it, they could probably articulate this process, but I understand how it really might not be that important.<br /> <br /> I think the important thing to just keep in your head is that these schools are teaching Dragon-Blooded how to excel in real things like actually winning a war. The Charms are game widgets that abstractly represent their essence further buoying that real endeavor. I don't think the deed is parsed seperately from the person who does it.<br /> <br /> EX. Your Sworn Kinship has a member aligned with the blessed element of Mela who can whisper commands to her soldiers on the winds. That's a valuable skill, but not one coerced from her Essence, it's an outgrowth of her personal excellence. Others with similar capabilities are seen the same way. This is not a thing people do, it's a thing that Tepet Nisana does. <br /> <br /> I recognize that this is kind of a rabbit hole though, so I guess I'll just say that's what I imagine to be a potential way to understand the way third edition is approaching this sort of thing. I'm largely of the opinion that it doesn't really matter.<br /> <br /> The House of Bells teaches you how to wage war, knowing fully that you will display your own personal excellence and that will bring you victory. They can't control for how that is expressed, and don't. If you are excellent at war, your essence will demonstrate excellence in warfare. How that looks varies for each of the Princes of the Earth.<br /> <br /> It kind of reminds me of reading about certain schools of painting in ancient China actually!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":23657,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","user":"VioletDreamer","date":". 04-11-2018, 10:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T20:26:19-07:00","id":1205894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205866#post1205866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't directly, except for the Heptagram. (Learning Sorcery requires at least ONE Charm.) But the secondary schools exist for the purpose of education Dragon-Blooded Dynasts. Presumably they are... taught to express their essence at them, to master and control their might as Princes of the Earth.<br /> <br /> I don't think I'm out of line for making the assumption.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's safe to assume dragon-blooded learn charms in school.<br /> But it's incorrect to assume the school teaches charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> The charms are well codified for the <i>players</i>. While a charm always does the same thing, and can be more or less recognized by an appropriate expert, it might not be how it's expressed in-setting. Even the same charm can appear as different things just by being used in different contexts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T21:32:16-07:00","id":1205908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VioletDreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205873#post1205873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: I think for your other point that their education doesn't really work that way?</div> </div> </div> </div>A strong possibility, but if it doesn't I really want to know <i>how</i> it works, in the same way I can understand how, say, Martial Arts training would work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the important thing to just keep in your head is that these schools are teaching Dragon-Blooded how to excel in real things like actually winning a war. The Charms are game widgets that abstractly represent their essence further buoying that real endeavor. </div> </div> </div>I don't think this is the case. The effects that Charms have on the world are very, VERY concretely described in many cases. They don't seem like abstractions at all.<br /> <br /> If they were, speaking only for myself, I would kind of really fucking hate that. I understand that we're dealing with fictional kung-fu magic superhumans here who do not have real-world analogues and so true understanding of them will always elude us. But like... I don't want the cool-ass magic shit that they do and that they are to be weird abstractions. I want to know that when they're doing the thing, it's the thing I think they're doing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think the deed is parsed seperately from the person who does it. </div> </div> </div>Well, you can never wholly separate any deed from the person who does it, but also, most things that people do aren't weirdly unique to them even for truly exceptional people.<br /> <br /> Almost nobody can execute a jump shot like LeBron James does, and in that sense his jump shot is a unique deed that cannot be parsed separately from him. But the basic mechanics of how to improve your own capability to execute a jump shot are well understood, because people have invested a shit-ton of time and energy into understanding how to make the human body do that, and that has resulted in exercises and techniques that will allow you to execute your own jump shot. It won't be the jump shot of LeBron James, but it will still be, recognizably, a jump shot.<br /> <br /> This applies even to things that are abstractly creative. You're never gonna be Picasso; his work was uniquely his in a way even stronger and more personal than what a skilled athlete does. You cannot be taught his unique genius.<br /> <br /> But you <i>can</i> be taught his <i>technique</i>. That's been studied and analyzed and dissected, as have the techniques of the other great artists. In teaching you those techniques, they can teach you to draw forth your own unique excellence. The paintings you create will not be Picasso's paintings, but they will still be paintings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EX. Your Sworn Kinship has a member aligned with the blessed element of Mela who can whisper commands to her soldiers on the winds. That's a valuable skill, but not one coerced from her Essence, it's an outgrowth of her personal excellence. </div> </div> </div>It's both, isn't it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Others with similar capabilities are seen the same way. This is not a thing people do, it's a thing that Tepet Nisana does. </div> </div> </div>Presumably other people will very much want to do those things. Tepet Nisana may even want to teach her thing she does to other people; that's a thing. Some people are all &quot;I can do the thing! The thing is awesome. I want to teach other people to do it as well!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's safe to assume dragon-blooded learn charms in school.<br /> But it's incorrect to assume the school teaches charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>This implies that any mastery over their essence (or whatever terminology you want to use for &quot;a Charm&quot;) a Dragon-Blooded learns at school basically happened by accident and without guidance from their teachers. I'm... not sure that's the case, and I'm definitely sure I wouldn't WANT it to be the case.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T22:09:27-07:00","id":1205919,"title":"","content":"Things are nuanced. Dragon Blooded are Ability Based Exalts, the fact that they learn their Abilities at school is a way to stimulate their Essence, they instruct and push their students and each student expresses their Elemental Nature in a personalized way. Each Dragon-Blooded is an elemental demigod urging to imprint the world with their mark. The same lesson can coax a Dodge Charm for one Student and a Resistance one for another. People have the same mechanical Charm, but the aesthetics in world could be very different.<br /> <br /> The teachers teach the Abilities, and the students learn and develop their Elemental Essence in a directed, but not controlled way. The school doesn't pride itself that every graduate can use &quot;Hopping Firecracker Evasion&quot;. They pride themselves in teaching elite evasion skills, with which their students may awaken a certain potential they have in their Exaltation.<br /> <br /> Nothing keeps you from using Charms are Techniques reality in your games though, it is just not how the 3rd setting is presented. But whatever rocks your boat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T22:39:52-07:00","id":1205932,"title":"","content":"I always assumed that while charms <i>in general</i> are not techniques, there are techniques that are charms. For example, the Actually a Doombot charm is not a technique, it's a narrative effect stating that there was a doombot there all along. You aren't suddenly replaced by a doombot with doombot replacement jutsu. On the other hand, this whispering commands to soldiers on the winds? Totally a technique that you could learn, if you put your mind to it. Most charms exist somewhere in the middle, like excellencies or other dice tricks, which are just &quot;I do the thing better.&quot; There's a million different ways you could be doing things better, but we just lump them all into excellencies and things like Excellent Strike (sorry for using Solar charms, haven't read the previews yet even though I have them).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1581-tonberrian","name":"tonberrian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T22:51:01-07:00","id":1205941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tonberrian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205932#post1205932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always assumed that while charms <i>in general</i> are not techniques, there are techniques that are charms. For example, the Actually a Doombot charm is not a technique, it's a narrative effect stating that there was a doombot there all along. You aren't suddenly replaced by a doombot with doombot replacement jutsu. On the other hand, this whispering commands to soldiers on the winds? Totally a technique that you could learn, if you put your mind to it. Most charms exist somewhere in the middle, like excellencies or other dice tricks, which are just &quot;I do the thing better.&quot; There's a million different ways you could be doing things better, but we just lump them all into excellencies and things like Excellent Strike (sorry for using Solar charms, haven't read the previews yet even though I have them).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd generally agree this is true, except I disagree with the assumption that IN-UNIVERSE any Solar has the ability to learn any given Solar charm based discrete power if they try hard enough, or same for Dragon-Blooded and their techniques, etc. Some people have inherent talents different than others. No amount of practice would let Heracles play music like Orpheus. As a player you can buy any Charm you want and build your character up with xp however you want, but that's because you have control over their narrative that they don't in-universe. So no institution can standardize what Charms they train, hence there not being a defined list of Charms that House of Bells graduates wield. They train in combat and strategy and tactics, and their powers manifest along those lines based on their own essence and personalities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T01:44:06-07:00","id":1205965,"title":"","content":"I'm reminded of the episode of Steven Universe where Steven is trying to figure out how to summon his shield. He asks the gems how they summon their weapons, and all three of them give him a different answer.<br /> <br /> I suspect it's a similar situation for Glorious Solar Saber and other &quot;technique&quot; charms. There's a known thing exalts can do, but how they do it varies slightly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T09:34:37-07:00","id":1206047,"title":"","content":"These are some great posts on how to frame it, guys!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T10:16:36-07:00","id":1206062,"title":"","content":"<b> At $233,000 in funding - NEW ADD ON</b> - A cloth map of the Blessed Isle and a cloth map of Creation will be offered as an Add On for $80 each, or both for $150, and can be added to any Reward Tier that includes a deluxe hardcover version of <b>Dragon-Blooded: What Fire Has Wrought</b>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>At $240,000 in funding - HEIRS TO THE SHOGUNATE \u2013 REALM EXPANSION #2:</b> Secondary Schools - materials to run games set in the secondary schools will be added to the Dragon-Blooded Companion PDF.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 04-12-2018, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T10:29:13-07:00","id":1206069,"title":"","content":"Huh. With the latest update providing a larger picture depicting a found egg choosing between the razor and the coin, I notice that its representation of the former is a narrow-bladed, folding handle straight razor, as was developed in Europe in the 17th century.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhereas I've always pictured the razor offered to represent accepting the Immaculate Order as being the older, simpler, fixed handle razor consisting of a semi-circular or square blade, as might be seen used by Aang in The Last Airbender.<br /> <br /> \u200b[image]http://media.giphy.com/media/r1Btb4pm7lfTG/giphy.gif[/image]<br /> <br /> \u200bApart from the resonance between the images, I always found the notion of the simpler razor to be more fitting to the austerity of the Immaculate Order, and that the simple shape had a nice symmetry with the coin.<br /> <br /> Am I overthinking it a bit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T10:49:39-07:00","id":1206077,"title":"","content":"Okay, meaning no disrespect Murcushio, you're saying lengthy points that I feel a need to make a singular, focused response to, so if I quote and respond to a single line, it's because I feel as though the key point can be represented there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205908#post1205908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This implies that any mastery over their essence (or whatever terminology you want to use for &quot;a Charm&quot;) a Dragon-Blooded learns at school basically happened by accident and without guidance from their teachers. I'm... not sure that's the case, and I'm definitely sure I wouldn't WANT it to be the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the approach to take is not that the instruction of teachers is irrelevant, but that it does not reference the Charms specifically and individually.<br /> <br /> \u200bA Dragon Blood who has received instruction in cultivating and harnessing their Essence comes out of it with, say, four Charms. None of those Charms were described by name in the training (although some of the more obvious or iconic ones, such as being able to send your words to somebody far away, may have been seen distinctly, just not with a flowery name for it), but they are the mechanical representation of the results of the training. It probably represents it even more strongly in the very fact that the use of skill by the Dragon Blooded becomes something that is expressed in mystical power; the kind of training you received in youth is why you'll be able to continuously develop Charms across your lifetime.<br /> <br /> \u200bThis is a thing that exists below the resolution of mechanics, because it really wouldn't be fun to say that an outcaste character who received no formal instruction from anybody is mechanically inferior at learning or using Charms. It's mostly a thing to characterize the culture of the Scarlet Dynasty and background of characters therein.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, the secondary schools are not environments in which you assemble classes of students repeatedly practicing Wingardium Leviosa.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhich is not what they've ever been. Apart from the Heptagram, the basic principle has always been that they're where the Dynasts go to get the equivalent of an Ivy League quality education in skills relevant to being on top of the world.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhich is also not a thing that can really be represented in these mechanics, beyond specialties and justification for the facts that can be declared with Lore or otherwise.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe important thing about the secondary schools is in how they characterize the Scarlet Dynasty as something that does not play fast and loose with whether or not those involved will be actually qualified to lead armies or run the world from a purely technical standing, and the associated expenses. And even apart from how the system is not nearly nuanced enough to represent the differences this might have to anybody else who came about their dots in War or Bureaucracy and the like, it doesn't really need to. That's not where the dramatic thrust of the gameplay is, and even people in real life who have received Ivy League education have been outperformed by people who came from less prestigious institutions.<br /> <br /> \u200bEDIT: I propose that another manner in which their education might directly relate to the Charms they develop is in the notion that Charms can often emerge from the application of skills under adversity, and the kind of environment you get in a Realm secondary school is at least as adverse (if a good deal safer) then what you'll get in practical experience adventuring in the Threshold. When you attend the House of Bells and learn a Melee Charm to cause your weapon to give off blinding sparks as somebody parries it, it isn't because your teacher brought you into a training room and gave you some kind of mental blueprint over how the Charm worked, and then had you practice it a hundred times on a training dummy, it's because your Exalted Essence (that you're imperceptibly aware of and feel control over due to the spiritual exercises and mystical instruction referring to your Essence as a whole rather than your Charms individually) finally managed to express itself in the midst of trying to excel in yet another live weapons exercise. It's not an incantation that you were taught and tried repeatedly, it's a moment of the skills you're using and the environment you're in clicking, and your power flows out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 04-12-2018, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T10:52:29-07:00","id":1206081,"title":"","content":"I would say that, even if they can't directly teach charms, the teachers must have methods that help you unlock your own potential and provoke epiphanies that might help you unlock that last little thing you need to figure out how to do a thing. Possibly they use koans and aphorisms.<br /> <br /> Alternately, I think you can assume that some charms are techniques like tonberrian suggests and assume that at least some of that knowledge can be conveyed from one DB to another, much like Iroh could teach Zuko how to deflect lightning. This doesn't mean it will work, much like Iroh couldn't teach Zuko to create lightning, but you can try.<br /> <br /> Actually, using Avatar might be a good idea. While the various teachers in the series give you tips and help and suggest that you need to widen your stance or whatever, ultimately, it's you doing the thing and there are aspects of it that you really can't teach directly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T11:14:24-07:00","id":1206091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1206081#post1206081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, using Avatar might be a good idea. While the various teachers in the series give you tips and help and suggest that you need to widen your stance or whatever, ultimately, it's you doing the thing and there are aspects of it that you really can't teach directly.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat actually reminds me of another part of it; there is the occasional specific, named and codified move that is applied, but it's evident that Bending training does not consist solely of being taught a library of these techniques, and that actual fighting consists of a lot of varied and improvised applications.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe central thing in training in Bending arts that we see tends to be conveying the mindset and spiritual foundation of the Bending. The main thing that Aang learns from Toph isn't 1000 different ways to manipulate rocks and soil, but the need to be solid and unmoving.<br /> <br /> \u200bI imagine that in any references to the likes of the Cloister of Wisdom teaching you about your Essence, what you'll mostly get is... the kinds of things that came up in the Aspect descriptions. Sure, your Aspect already gives you a lot of that mindset, but if you're taught to effectively recognise it, articulate it, and live in alignment with it, then the Charms that are expressions of it will emerge as appropriate.<br /> <br /> \u200bResistance, Integrity and their Charms aren't exactly recognised as distinct things in the setting, but if an Earth Aspect gets taught to understand their strengths in being a solid pillar against which they should let challenges break, then in the occasions where they face challenges (which they definitely will in those schools) and stand firm against them, then those things <i>shall</i> break against them.<br /> <br /> \u200bI imagine that even Ephemeral Form Composition is the kind of thing that doesn't arise from having been taught a specific way to manipulate Essence into the form of a blueprint so much as it comes from somebody having that perspective on structures, materials, Essence and the world that Mnemon did when she looked out over Jiara.<br /> <br /> \u200bHmm, come to think of it, one thing that might benefit a Dragon Blood being taught about Essence is the rudiments of the mindset of the other Aspects, since they'll probably need that if they want to learn Charms with an element not their own.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor that matter, speaking of Mnemon, that chapter fiction in general might be instructive. I'd say that the manner in which Mnemon learnt how to survive being stabbed and slashed a dozen times from a rain of daggers was being taught how to be the kind of person who would face down a rain of daggers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T11:27:35-07:00","id":1206099,"title":"","content":"It might help that in real life there's not even really such a thing as a discreet technique. Like if you're learning how to box and throw punches you don't sit there trying again and again until you cross some threshold and suddenly your jabs are just as good as anyone else's. Exalted is a game so it's difficult to represent it like that though. <br /> <br /> That doesn't mean that certain techniques can't have names in setting, again in real life you've got a ton of different named techniques for everything from fighting to parkour, but being able to throw a wind blade is more of a big sloppy sliding scale than casting a spell in DnD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T11:51:48-07:00","id":1206108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205761#post1205761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that this will be the dominant (ubiquitous) take on the forums, but that's not what I'm seeing in the text.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But what do you see in the text? Do you think that the gap is too big or what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T12:12:19-07:00","id":1206124,"title":"","content":"Consider that the vast majority of time spent learning to do something is time spent almost-but-not-quite doing the thing you want to do. Consider also that everything another person might do in front of me is something that I can theoretically, with enough time, training, and talent, do at least semi-competently. In observing, I can begin to theorize how it's done because every human capability is one of my capabilities, barring physical barriers to success.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo every person with Dragon-Blooded essence can understand on some level what it would take to, say, set their whispers to drift upon the wind. Many can probably <i>almost</i>\u200b do it, the way that mortals might almost be able to whistle (&quot;I just need to practice until I get the right lip-shape.&quot;). \u200bAnd even once a person learns to whistle, they all learn to do it differently. I don't know how to whistle with the piercing strength that my grandfather had, and my mouth may just not be built to do it, but I can whistle my own way.<br /> <br /> \u200bAll that wibbly-wobbly stuff is below the level of mechanical resolution. <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That space is where stunts and anima and signs of breeding live. If dogs were making a Human: The Thumbening RPG, they might well write a &quot;whistling&quot; Charm and debate what it's like for humans to do or learn this impossible-for-dogs thing, because they don't have the parts needed, the same way we don't have the right essence. But the answer's the same either way: anything we have the capability to do, we can observe, comprehend, practice, and master.<br /> <br /> \u200bEdit: Ninja'd by the good doctor.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T12:32:13-07:00","id":1206128,"title":"","content":"-Bursts in-<br /> IM SORRY, DID THAT UPDATE HAVE THE FACE SNAKED AS AN IMAGE?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T12:46:58-07:00","id":1206133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1206128#post1206128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DID THAT UPDATE HAVE THE FACE SNAKED AS AN IMAGE?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bNono, that's clearly a faced snake. Easy mistake to make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T13:52:29-07:00","id":1206153,"title":"","content":"Catching up on Previews, and just got to the outcaste, and I just had to pop in to mention how much I loved the outcaste name &quot;Heady Monsoon&quot;.<br /> <br /> That's just such a good name. Even if I don't use that NPC, I will be using that name at some point.<br /> <br /> Edit: I really hope that art was inspired by, and intended to stoke, the confusion around the term &quot;face-snaked&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T16:32:04-07:00","id":1206194,"title":"","content":"I like most of the Dragon-Blooded Charms I've seen so far, but one I'm not sure about is Hesieh's Discerning Tongue. I like the idea, but letting characters detect poison before consuming it seems like something a Storyteller might want to let characters do by default, and the Charm's existence kind of makes it seem like you shouldn't - and if you do, it raises the question of how that should work and exactly how the Charm makes you better at it.<br /> <br /> It's not <i>too</i> bad. The concept is cool, the automatic Essence 3 upgrade could be nice, and it's reasonable to say that without it, you're likely to consume some poison before you realize it's there. But the Charm has clearly defined mechanics while any mortal capabilities it enhances do not, as far as I can remember, and that kind of bugs me.<br /> <br /> Maybe that's just me, I don't know.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/157-phoenix_kensai","name":"Phoenix_Kensai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar157_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T16:39:03-07:00","id":1206195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phoenix_Kensai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1206194#post1206194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like most of the Dragon-Blooded Charms I've seen so far, but one I'm not sure about is Hesieh's Discerning Tongue. I like the idea, but letting characters detect poison before consuming it seems like something a Storyteller might want to let characters do by default, and the Charm's existence kind of makes it seem like you shouldn't - and if you do, it raises the question of how that should work and exactly how the Charm makes you better at it.<br /> <br /> It's not <i>too</i> bad. The concept is cool, the automatic Essence 3 upgrade could be nice, and it's reasonable to say that without it, you're likely to consume some poison before you realize it's there. But the Charm has clearly defined mechanics while any mortal capabilities it enhances do not, as far as I can remember, and that kind of bugs me.<br /> <br /> Maybe that's just me, I don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div>My 2 cents is that you should probably consider it in terms of the myriad of poisons that are not particularly detectable. I suspect it's easy for a GM to say you can do a perception + awareness at a ridiculous difficulty that's unlikely to succeed and this charm lets you subvert that. But if poisons were easily detectable they wouldn't be used! In general, the devs seem unwilling to define discrete mortal mechanics for mundane things, preferring GMs to come up with what makes sense for them. That's not always appealing, but it does seem to fit the direction of a lot of this stuff.<br /> <br /> Again, my 2 cents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T18:39:08-07:00","id":1206219,"title":"","content":"I wonder if I'm the only one kinda hoping Trauma Bear makes an appearance on the artwork at some point...<br /> ...I don't think an animal-loving person of Vance's grade is gonna want the poor bear to suffer anymore, though XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":868,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","user":"danelsan","date":". 04-12-2018, 09:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T20:36:22-07:00","id":1206259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1205965#post1205965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm reminded of the episode of Steven Universe where Steven is trying to figure out how to summon his shield. He asks the gems how they summon their weapons, and all three of them give him a different answer.<br /> <br /> I suspect it's a similar situation for Glorious Solar Saber and other &quot;technique&quot; charms. There's a known thing exalts can do, but how they do it varies slightly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to dismiss your point, but it's also worth noting that future episodes reveal reasons for why the process is different for each of them.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Gems like Amethyst were made to fight, so her weapon comes instinctually to her without real effort. Gems like Pearl weren't meant to fight at all, and it took her a long time and a lot of effort to figure out how to form a weapon. Garnet is a fusion of a footsoldier Ruby and an aristocractic Sapphire; the gauntlets are Ruby's easy-to-summon weapon, but refined by Sapphire's assistance.<br /> <br /> In Exalted mechanical terms, Pearl needed higher minimums, more XP, and possibly more non-combat Charm prerequisites to arrive at her spear, whereas Amethyst got her whip as a base-level Charm with low minimums and favored costs, and Garnet is using two different sets of Charms from which she made connected advanced Charms.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T20:40:01-07:00","id":1206260,"title":"","content":"Anyway, my major source of frustration is that the last preview didn't include Dragon-Blooded Melee.<br /> <br /> I'm ITCHING to look into ways Dragon-Blooded Melee Charms can interact with artifact Melee weapons.<br /> <br /> In particular, I still want to take a stab at Raven Branwen's multi-blade sword from <i>RWBY</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T23:06:37-07:00","id":1206295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1206069#post1206069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. With the latest update providing a larger picture depicting a found egg choosing between the razor and the coin, I notice that its representation of the former is a narrow-bladed, folding handle straight razor, as was developed in Europe in the 17th century.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhereas I've always pictured the razor offered to represent accepting the Immaculate Order as being the older, simpler, fixed handle razor consisting of a semi-circular or square blade, as might be seen used by Aang in The Last Airbender.<br /> <br /> \u200b[image]http://media.giphy.com/media/r1Btb4pm7lfTG/giphy.gif[/image]<br /> <br /> \u200bApart from the resonance between the images, I always found the notion of the simpler razor to be more fitting to the austerity of the Immaculate Order, and that the simple shape had a nice symmetry with the coin.<br /> <br /> Am I overthinking it a bit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you\u2019re kind of overthinking it. Minton wrote an art note saying \u201cDraw a razor,\u201d that\u2019s the razor that came to mind to the artist and therefore the kind of razor the artist drew, and then in the revision process, for whatever reason nobody went \u201cHmm, that seems anachronistic, we ought to have the artist change it.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T23:16:42-07:00","id":1206297,"title":"","content":"<br /> Meh its Exalted, we've got a country with airships because they dug them out of ruins. Would honestly not surprise me for the design to be an old thing handed down or something that came out of specific desires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":".  Realized I probably didn't need the quote. 04-13-2018, 02:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T23:19:50-07:00","id":1206299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1206297#post1206297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh its Exalted, we've got a country with airships because they dug them out of ruins. Would honestly not surprise me for the design to be an old thing handed down or something that came out of specific desires.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean it can be, but the older razor would look cooler, so lets go with that one instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T01:11:31-07:00","id":1206336,"title":"","content":"Hah, you know what's really cool? You can use Virtuous Negation Defense to reflexively defend other with dodge, and then use Safety Among Enemies to redirect that attack. I think anyway. Which means that if some Abyssal is swinging a grand daiklave at your hearthmate you can push them out of the way, catch the blade, and redirect it in a spinning slash towards his own horde of zombies in one smooth motion.<br /> <br /> Afterwards as a reflexive action you then reach into your robe, pull out a pair of sunglasses, pop them on your face and give a cheeky smile. (I imagine this got cut from the official charm text space and clarity)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T03:57:34-07:00","id":1206362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1206295#post1206295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, you\u2019re kind of overthinking it. Minton wrote an art note saying \u201cDraw a razor,\u201d that\u2019s the razor that came to mind to the artist and therefore the kind of razor the artist drew, and then in the revision process, for whatever reason nobody went \u201cHmm, that seems anachronistic, we ought to have the artist change it.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSo just like Janest's outfit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 04-13-2018, 07:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T06:58:52-07:00","id":1206415,"title":"","content":"Forest Witch Expansion 3 added as a stretchgoal (their factions and some individual members).<br /> <br /> Hopefully we\u2019ll see Outcaste Expansion 3 soon. More Prasad and Cadet Houses will be nice, but they\u2019re lower priority since they\u2019re getting coverage in the Realm book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T11:26:23-07:00","id":1206536,"title":"","content":"Wonder how many more stretch goals we will manage to reach now that they seem to be spacing them out a bit more? Pretty sure we will definitely manage the current two at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T11:49:09-07:00","id":1206546,"title":"","content":"We\u2019ll hit a fair number more, especially when we speed up again in the last few days.<br /> <br /> Vance hinted today that a full preview of the Realm text might be in the cards if we keep up a good pace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T12:14:32-07:00","id":1206571,"title":"","content":"Map is available as an add-on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T12:23:23-07:00","id":1206573,"title":"","content":"Damn, I really hope those custom charms sell... They should publically push them again after the next text update when we have the whole charmset so people can identify whatever they feel they want that\u2019s missing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T12:32:42-07:00","id":1206580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1206546#post1206546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We\u2019ll hit a fair number more, especially when we speed up again in the last few days.<br /> <br /> Vance hinted today that a full preview of the Realm text might be in the cards if we keep up a good pace.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True, I forgot that there tends to be a last minute rush at the end. Maybe we can manage to hit 300K, would be pretty impressive since its safe to say the series hasn't gotten back the hype it had during the core book kickstarter. But that should be changing now that we finally have consistently released new material again.<br /> <br /> That would be a nice preview bonus","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T12:41:07-07:00","id":1206584,"title":"","content":"I mean there\u2019s still some work to do to rebuild the following - but a supplement was never going to to make as much as the core. It\u2019s doing quite well all things considered.<br /> <br /> Unless I\u2019m mistaken on the timing, I think the official approval from White Wolf/Paradox to proceed with Lunars is a good sign they were pleased with the response from Backers as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-13-2018, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T12:43:36-07:00","id":1206590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1206580#post1206580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, I forgot that there tends to be a last minute rush at the end. Maybe we can manage to hit 300K, would be pretty impressive since its safe to say the series hasn't gotten back the hype it had during the core book kickstarter. But that should be changing now that we finally have consistently released new material again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. How much of it is that, and how much is the fact corebooks generally do better than supplements, we don't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T14:25:07-07:00","id":1206654,"title":"","content":"Mind, given the prominence of the Terrestrial Exalted in the setting, more than a few people have expressed the sentiment that a book detailing them is essential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T14:56:56-07:00","id":1206672,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I would argue that they are just as essential as solars given their current dominance of so much of the world and how many of them there are compared to any other exalt type in the setting. Depending on how many exalts there are in the new splats like the exigents they might outnumber all the other types put together. Of course its all up to the story teller what you run into and they aren't obligated to put them in just because they are the most common place, but generally speaking they are so numerous and have so much potential to be part of any organization thanks to outcaste exaltations creating free agents they are a very likely antagonist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T15:52:51-07:00","id":1206700,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d argue that the Dragon-Blooded are potentially more essential to the game than the Solar Exalted, and that one of the major reasons why the Solar Exalted need to be published first is that, if the Dragon-Blooded were first, it would be really hard to see the Solar Exalted as anything other than Anathema.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T16:35:20-07:00","id":1206722,"title":"","content":"I agree they\u2019re essential to the setting, but that doesn\u2019t change the inherent dynamic that exists between any corebook and a supplement, where the book that requires the other to be playable will sell less than the required book, since it can only sell to people who have the core, but the core can sell without the supplement. Set and sub-set.<br /> <br /> I mean, I suppose there\u2019s the piracy factor, but I don\u2019t see a lot of that demo paying for supplements when they\u2019re willing to pirate the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T18:07:34-07:00","id":1206746,"title":"","content":"Well also the corebook is basically needed by anyone who wants to play the game. A splat though is only needed by players interested in playing that splat, or the ST who feels they'd need information from it. Like most of my group hasn't expressed interest in playing as DBs* consequently the book isn't that useful to them and they don't feel the need to get it. I run the game, so this is full of really helpful information and potential for glorious challenges.<br /> <br /> *One day that may change, but it probably won't be during the kickstarter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 04-13-2018, 09:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T19:09:29-07:00","id":1206759,"title":"","content":"The Kickstarter is literally closing on my birthday, so I went ahead and got myself another custom charm.<br /> <br /> If there\u2019s a rush on the remaining slots at the end, and people who want one don\u2019t get one, I\u2019ll give one up. But as it stands they\u2019re just sitting there so screw it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T00:54:42-07:00","id":1206809,"title":"","content":"Man, imagine how easy churning out the maps would be with the Distaff and Craftsman Needs No Tools. &gt;.&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T12:25:29-07:00","id":1206980,"title":"","content":"I'm liking this latest preview of the Realm. A growing desert is a pretty good way to give an impression of change over time, and there are some vivid characters there, such as the shrivelled up head gods, the newly arrived dragon (very Earthsea/Flat Earth), and the eccentric and occasionally mutant monks.<br /> <br /> Ohhh shit... yeah, from this point on, my mental image of Hualli shall be Kass the Rito bard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"col