://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/157-phoenix_kensai","name":"Phoenix_Kensai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar157_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T10:02:22-07:00","id":1208046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phoenix_Kensai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1208029#post1208029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Performance excellency allows the Dragon-Blooded to ignore the penalty for targeting multiple characters with social influence, but Performance already does that (according to the sidebar under Solar Performance Charms in the core, at least), right? Is there some benefit to that I'm missing, or is it a mistake?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's Solar Performance Charms only.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T10:37:36-07:00","id":1208056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1208046#post1208046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's Solar Performance Charms only.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Oh, I see now that it specifically says &quot;Solar Performance Charms&quot;. Thanks for the answer.<br /> <br /> It might be a while before I have time to read through all the new Charms, but after last week's preview and what I've seen of the new one, I want to say I like what I've read so far. The text is clear and concise, the balance looks good at a glance (for what little that counts), and I'm rarely left wondering how a Charm works or why I would want it after a quick read-through, which was a common problem with Solar Charms. Dragon-Blooded were never my favorite of the Exalted, but this book is making me want to play one, and they're definitely the type I'd pick for introducing new players to the system.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">(Until we get Lunars and Sidereals, anyway.)</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/157-phoenix_kensai","name":"Phoenix_Kensai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar157_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T10:38:15-07:00","id":1208057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phoenix_Kensai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1208056#post1208056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...Oh, I see now that it specifically says &quot;Solar Performance Charms&quot;. Thanks for the answer.<br /> <br /> It might be a while before I have time to read through all the new Charms, but after last week's preview and what I've seen of the new one, I want to say I like what I've read so far. The text is clear and concise, the balance looks good at a glance (for what little that counts), and I'm rarely left wondering how a Charm works or why I would want it after a quick read-through, which was a common problem with Solar Charms. Dragon-Blooded were never my favorite of the Exalted, but this book is making me want to play one, and they're definitely the type I'd pick for introducing new players to the system.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">(Until we get Lunars and Sidereals, anyway.)</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad to hear it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T10:41:04-07:00","id":1208059,"title":"","content":"Does that mean if a Solar makes a performance roll against a group without using any charms, she takes the penalty?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T10:51:58-07:00","id":1208064,"title":"","content":"Yeah I\u2019m really impressed by how many charms are just one sentence of fluff, one of crunch, moving on. I\u2019m also really liking the powers I\u2019m seeing here. They\u2019re interesting and for the most part don\u2019t combo very well so you don\u2019t need to worry too much about that, except when they\u2019re pretty explicitly designed to combo. I\u2019m also loving that you start at essence 2, clears up a lot of space for charms to be in for chargen and I\u2019m really looking forward to properly utilizing some of the lower powered antagonists. <br /> <br /> At least until the players get to E4-5, then they\u2019re looking pretty stacked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T12:42:19-07:00","id":1208111,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's a small thing, but I'm really happy to see Dragon-Blooded Resistance Charms that enhance their endurance in ways unrelated to damage and poison, like Untiring Earth Meditation (questions about fatigue penalties aside). They might not be as broadly useful as combat Charms, but I was always disappointed that Solar Charms didn't explore that design space.<br /> <br /> That goes more generally for the other Abilities, too. I felt that Solar Charms were sometimes too focused on a theme that wasn't central to their Ability, limiting their appeal for characters that weren't built around that. The Dragon-Blooded Charmset seems to have a broader variety of effects overall, despite its smaller size, and I like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/157-phoenix_kensai","name":"Phoenix_Kensai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar157_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T14:36:02-07:00","id":1208183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1208064#post1208064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I\u2019m really impressed by how many charms are just one sentence of fluff, one of crunch, moving on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dear god, this.<br /> <br /> The level of clarity and precision in these Charms blows those in the core out of the water. Everyone involved stepped their game HELLA up.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T14:41:57-07:00","id":1208186,"title":"","content":"One of the things I am really liking about the charms is how they encourage divergent play based upon the charms you pick. For instance, a wood based archery build to me feels really different than if you focus air archery charms. I am also loving their solution to DBs only having one sorcerous ritual for mote generation (in comparison to a solar\u2019s 3).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T16:21:57-07:00","id":1208227,"title":"","content":"Novella #2 achieved. Cadet House Expansion #2 at 275k!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T17:49:08-07:00","id":1208257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1208186#post1208186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am also loving their solution to DBs only having one sorcerous ritual for mote generation (in comparison to a solar\u2019s 3).</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the sorcery Charm, but I'm not convinced it's a replacement for access to their sorcerous path's two other rituals.<br /> <br /> Rather, it seems like a nice compensation for not getting any new sorcerous toys at Essence 3 or beyond the way other Exalted do.<br /> <br /> <br /> Over all, though, I'm amazed and thrilled by the Dragon-Blooded Charmset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T19:22:50-07:00","id":1208287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1208257#post1208257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the sorcery Charm, but I'm not convinced it's a replacement for access to their sorcerous path's two other rituals.<br /> <br /> Rather, it seems like a nice compensation for not getting any new sorcerous toys at Essence 3 or beyond the way other Exalted do.<br /> <br /> <br /> Over all, though, I'm amazed and thrilled by the Dragon-Blooded Charmset.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s more of where it fits and function it serves, primarily as an avenue for generating SMs, most shaping rituals generate between 1-5 sorcerous motes per action, which is inline with with Puissance which generates either 1 or 3 additional sorcerous notes per round. Further the use of the aura mechanic is inline with the kinds of variables that are normally used for shaping rituals. Just my two cents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T23:00:18-07:00","id":1208331,"title":"","content":"So, in order to help figure out DB builds and tactics, I've started a spreadsheet.<br /> <br /> I've got the names of every DB charm in there and spaces to note what element it is and places to flag the new keywords and everything.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1LUZ_ub0LW60-Q5Xf0z3LPTLIgPbwT5USj-re8Pa5LFs/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> I only have the info filled out for Archery so far, but I'll try to continue adding more in. I also made it editable by anyone with that link, should people wish to help. If you do wish to help, please use the way Archery was done and formatted as a guide.<br /> <br /> Once done, sort and filter operations should make it easy to find, say, all the Non-Aura Starting Water charms or all the Signature charms with No Prereqs, and help you figure out how best to go for a particular DB build.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T23:57:21-07:00","id":1208346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1208331#post1208331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in order to help figure out DB builds and tactics, I've started a spreadsheet.<br /> <br /> I've got the names of every DB charm in there and spaces to note what element it is and places to flag the new keywords and everything.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1LUZ_ub0LW60-Q5Xf0z3LPTLIgPbwT5USj-re8Pa5LFs/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> I only have the info filled out for Archery so far, but I'll try to continue adding more in. I also made it editable by anyone with that link, should people wish to help. If you do wish to help, please use the way Archery was done and formatted as a guide.<br /> <br /> Once done, sort and filter operations should make it easy to find, say, all the Non-Aura Starting Water charms or all the Signature charms with No Prereqs, and help you figure out how best to go for a particular DB build.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Hey! I tried something similar last week, and I'd love to give a hand - I'll see if I can fit a couple hours later today.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1GzFxtr8ACZnTPQboDuND6ViOOLXhfaS7LnVr0k4yeLQ/edit#gid=0\" target=\"_blank\">Here's the thing for comparaison's sake!</a> (Yours looks way cooler, BTW)<br /> <br /> First, don't be afraid to pilfer anything you want from mine. Next, I had a few questions regarding your end objectives.<br /> <br /> A) How are you going to represent Charms that allow to expend Aura when upgraded, like <span style=\"color:#000000\">Drawing Lightning Style</span>? Maybe a new value in the columns &quot;In Aura Bonus&quot; and &quot;Expends Aura&quot; to express how and upgrade exists? It would actually be sleeker than my cumbersome &quot;Aura Upgrade&quot; field.<br /> <br /> B) Similarly, how are you going to represent Charms with various Elemental version (like <span style=\"color:#000000\">Cloud-Piercing Focus) and differenciate with multi-aspected Charms like </span> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Death From Nowhere?<br /> <br /> C) Lastly, and more critically, Say I wanna use your tool to decide which Charm I could use to be in Water Aura using Archery to prepare for Arrow Rain Tempest. I can easily see Death From Nowhere and and Fang-of-the-Depths, but I'd need to also check the Balanced Charms in another column, which means I'd need to filter twice. This is actually the one thing I'm proud about in my version - why not mention that a Charm is Balanced INSIDE the various elements? You save a column in width, don't clutter up your table too much and have a one-click tool to create combo lists.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3657,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3657-sagara","user":"Sagara","date":".  Damn formatting... 04-18-2018, 03:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3657-sagara","name":"Sagara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3657_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T08:31:15-07:00","id":1208459,"title":"","content":"I tend to use the sort operation more than the filter, so that\u2019s why it\u2019s set up like it is, just to make it easy to sort by each column. I think it\u2019ll work better with a seperate column for balanced. That said, I hadn\u2019t really considered how to differentiate charms with repurchase effects and or multi element charms vs ones with multiple versions.<br /> <br /> If you wanna try messing with the formatting a bit more, you could save a copy of the file, adjust it, and put it back up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T13:32:31-07:00","id":1208553,"title":"","content":"Right now, I'm thinking first finishing up my version and probably pick up a couple formatting ideas on your side, and then I'll copy/paste all the easy info into yours.<br /> <br /> I get the gist of your approach, but I can't quickly think up an idea that could integrate both our strenghts, so I think two &quot;competing&quot; works might be a better start, and maybe the solution will make itself evident in usage.<br /> Still, I've got a couple ideas how to easily fill up your columns where our approach differ, so once that first phase's done, I'll probably make a copy and see if I can help finish up yours as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3657-sagara","name":"Sagara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3657_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T13:36:13-07:00","id":1208555,"title":"","content":"Sounds good. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T12:33:52-07:00","id":1208977,"title":"","content":"So, someone suggested tracking current Aura with a six sided die, which I think is pretty clever.<br /> <br /> And then I found out that people make six-siders with a different color on each side.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.rainbowresource.com/proddtl.php?id=047536&amp;gclid=Cj0KCQjw_ODWBRCTARIsAE2_EvXEiF7kjhTjp0zHaVDpjjYYa3mcDd-CLFznNIzhOdEr9vUKs8f1j1kaAhKJEALw_wcB\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/hdtsjhzsw/image/upload/s--2ku5t5_8--/q_auto:low/c_fit,w_265,h_265/qal2oznerac3dad3vbl0.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.rainbowresource.com/proddtl.php?id=047536&amp;gclid=Cj0KCQjw_ODWBRCTARIsAE2_EvXEiF7kjhTjp0zHaVDpjjYYa3mcDd-CLFznNIzhOdEr9vUKs8f1j1kaAhKJEALw_wcB\" target=\"_blank\"> Single-Spot Six-Colored Die </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.rainbowresource.com/proddtl.php?id=047536&amp;gclid=Cj0KCQjw_ODWBRCTARIsAE2_EvXEiF7kjhTjp0zHaVDpjjYYa3mcDd-CLFznNIzhOdEr9vUKs8f1j1kaAhKJEALw_wcB\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.rainbowresource.com/proddtl.php?id=047536&amp;gclid=Cj0KCQjw_ODWBRCTARIsAE2_EvXEiF7kjhTjp0zHaVDpjjYYa3mcDd-CLFznNIzhOdEr9vUKs8f1j1kaAhKJEALw_wcB </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Instead of rolling 1 through 6, how about rolling blue? Or purple? This 20mm, six-sided square die features a large colored \"spot\" on each side, in the following colors: blue, black, purple, green, red, and yellow. Invent your own games, quiz young children on their colors, or swap them with your regular dice to add variety next family game night! Sold individually. Six sides shown for detail. ~ Lisa </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It\u2019s not perfect, because they have purple and yellow, but no white side. Still, if you were willing to take some white-out or something to one of the two wrong sides or get an entirely blank die and set of paints, you could have a nice aura tracker die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T12:39:54-07:00","id":1208980,"title":"","content":"Realm Civil War section achieved. At 285k (10k after the Cadet House Expansion at 275k) they add chapter fiction to the front of each chapter in Heirs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T12:50:44-07:00","id":1208983,"title":"","content":"After reading more Charms and running some quick comparisons, I'm getting the impression that Dragon-Blooded aren't actually far behind Solars in average successes for any given Ability. It might take the Dragon-Blooded more investment to get there, and they might be more limited in when and how often they can use their full potential, but if a Solar and Dragon-Blooded are directly competing in their area of specialty, the Solar has a significant risk of losing any individual roll-off.<br /> <br /> I wonder if I'm right on this, not being an expert on either Charmset, and (if so) if that was a design goal for the Dragon-Blooded Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/157-phoenix_kensai","name":"Phoenix_Kensai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar157_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T15:28:09-07:00","id":1209031,"title":"","content":"Based on the design notes given in the most recent Kickstarter Update, I think that was a design goal actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T15:35:52-07:00","id":1209034,"title":"","content":"Another one seems to be encouraging Dragon-Blooded to generalize more than Solars.<br /> <br /> Solar Abilities have very deep Charm trees, where Terrestrial ones are relatively shallow. Even so, without a Supernal Ability, a Terrestrial can\u2019t reach the penultimate Charms of anything (including their second Signature Charm in the Ability) until they\u2019re actually Essence 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T16:13:09-07:00","id":1209042,"title":"","content":"Also DBs being 150xp out from essence 3 means you\u2019re going to pick up a lot of charms before your availability opens up more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T17:10:37-07:00","id":1209057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1209034#post1209034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another one seems to be encouraging Dragon-Blooded to generalize more than Solars.<br /> <br /> Solar Abilities have very deep Charm trees, where Terrestrial ones are relatively shallow. Even so, without a Supernal Ability, a Terrestrial can\u2019t reach the penultimate Charms of anything (including their second Signature Charm in the Ability) until they\u2019re actually Essence 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Elemental Aura and Signature charms mechanics in particular seem to suggest &quot;Hey, look, you don't have to buy every charm in an ability. In fact, you can't. So just get the ones you want!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T17:16:57-07:00","id":1209062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1209057#post1209057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Elemental Aura and Signature charms mechanics in particular seem to suggest &quot;Hey, look, you don't have to buy every charm in an ability. In fact, you can't. So just get the ones you want!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At the same time, I wish the trees had more charms, specifically because the xp cost on advancement requires a lot of investment while you're spinning your wheels on Essence 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T17:21:09-07:00","id":1209063,"title":"","content":"&quot;Penultimate&quot; is <i>next</i>-to-last.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T18:01:25-07:00","id":1209077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1209062#post1209062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> At the same time, I wish the trees had more charms, specifically because the xp cost on advancement requires a lot of investment while you're spinning your wheels on Essence 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>150 XP is roughly 18 charms, combined with char gen that\u2019s only a total of 33 charms. Spread across 10 aspect/favored abilities that\u2019s roughly at most 3 charms per Ability. Now while we know that people probably won\u2019t be delving into every aspect/favored, there will be sufficient that I think you could get charms in like 7-8 abilities, opening up much more varied styles of play. If anything the bigger concern I have is differentiation in non-combat settings for my players, but I suspect that as long as we all meet and hash out their concepts together it should be ok.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T18:12:07-07:00","id":1209079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1209063#post1209063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Penultimate&quot; is <i>next</i>-to-last.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and the printed pinnacle Charms aren't necessarily the end of those trees; just the official ones.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1209077#post1209077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If anything the bigger concern I have is differentiation in non-combat settings for my players, but I suspect that as long as we all meet and hash out their concepts together it should be ok.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely want Terrestrial Brawl to include sand-bending, since it's so similar to Currents Sweep to Sea and Smashing Tidal Wave.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, I don't think Earth Dragon Style will let you kick up a stone wall to block ranged attacks, so we need to find a place for that in the Charmset, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T18:33:39-07:00","id":1209083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1209079#post1209079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, and the printed pinnacle Charms aren't necessarily the end of those trees; just the official ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please don't. The <i>capacity</i> to have someone behind me in line does not change the fact that I'm the last one in line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T19:10:05-07:00","id":1209090,"title":"","content":"For those who have gotten a second major tier reward, how hard is it to set up another Kickstarter account?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T19:13:53-07:00","id":1209092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1209090#post1209090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For those who have gotten a second major tier reward, how hard is it to set up another Kickstarter account?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not remotely difficult. You just need a different email address. You can use the same credit card and everything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T06:08:50-07:00","id":1209208,"title":"","content":"Edit: never mind","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-20-2018, 09:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T06:20:04-07:00","id":1209215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1209208#post1209208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: never mind</div> </div> </div> </div>So, based on what you've seen in the KS previews, are you excited to see what the dev team has in store for Lunars? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Because I'm excited. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Also curious for your input in my Lore thread if you don't mind.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-20-2018, 09:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T08:23:20-07:00","id":1209259,"title":"","content":"I already trusted that Lunars would function and not suck.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m being cautiously optimistic about whether Lunars will deliver even half of the Wow Factor of the new Dragon-Blooded. <br /> <br /> I\u2019ll take a look at your lore thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-20-2018, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T11:30:26-07:00","id":1209335,"title":"","content":"Ah, good; with the latest update, we've got a full roster of pictures of the signature characters.<br /> <br /> \u200bI already said what I like about Righteous River, and I think all of the designs are pretty good, but for the moment I'll limit myself to Left Hand Chalima. What I like in her is how she's a more stocky, rounded looking woman, especially as a subversion of what I would often expect in a Fire Aspect. Also her overcoat looks nice, and I like how her firewand is sufficiently stylized to make it look more impressive to me than a flintlock pistol, without being over the top.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T12:59:56-07:00","id":1209360,"title":"","content":"Minor nitpick: Yushoto Mathar's name has been misspelled as &quot;Yushuto Mathar&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T16:36:47-07:00","id":1209451,"title":"","content":"So if i\u2019m not mistaken about the signature characters....<br /> <br /> Air - Dynast Sorcerer<br /> Earth - Found Egg in the Legions<br /> Fire - Outcaste<br /> Water - Immaculate (unclear if Found-Egg or Dynast with dropped family name)<br /> Wood - Lookshyan","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T18:00:32-07:00","id":1209462,"title":"","content":"If it's in the text I missed it. What's Realm law on when a slave Exalts as Dragon-Blooded? I assume they're automatically freed and then treated like a commoner Found Egg (Razor or Coin)... but I'm guessing the former owner is entitled to compensation? Is the new Dragon-Blooded considered in debt to them, or do the Legions, Order, or Empress just pay them the cost of the mortal slave they lost, or what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T22:09:45-07:00","id":1209511,"title":"","content":"(My responses don't speak for the developers.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1209462#post1209462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's in the text I missed it. What's Realm law on when a slave Exalts as Dragon-Blooded? I assume they're automatically freed and then treated like a commoner Found Egg (Razor or Coin)... but I'm guessing the former owner is entitled to compensation? Is the new Dragon-Blooded considered in debt to them, or do the Legions, Order, or Empress just pay them the cost of the mortal slave they lost, or what?</div> </div> </div> </div>Who would dare put a price on a mild inconvenience caused by a miraculous decree of the Elemental Dragons? Who would have the temerity to claim any ownership whatsoever upon the newest Prince of the Earth, even in their absence? And who would be foolish enough to view an Exalt as a lost slave instead of a potential adoptee (formal or informal)?<br /> <br /> The Scarlet Dynasty is legalistic, but their faith decrees that Exaltation as a Dragon-Blooded is an Elemental Dragon-backed statement about the Exalt's rightful place in society. It would be sacrilegious to make a claim as petty as slave ownership in the face of that.<br /> <br /> The <i>really interesting</i> question is: who does the slave owner have to bribe to claim that the new Exalt is part of their bloodline?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T22:40:28-07:00","id":1209519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1209511#post1209511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(My responses don't speak for the developers.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Who would dare put a price on a mild inconvenience caused by a miraculous decree of the Elemental Dragons? Who would have the temerity to claim any ownership whatsoever upon the newest Prince of the Earth, even in their absence? And who would be foolish enough to view an Exalt as a lost slave instead of a potential adoptee (formal or informal)?<br /> <br /> The Scarlet Dynasty is legalistic, but their faith decrees that Exaltation as a Dragon-Blooded is an Elemental Dragon-backed statement about the Exalt's rightful place in society. It would be sacrilegious to make a claim as petty as slave ownership in the face of that.<br /> <br /> The <i>really interesting</i> question is: who does the slave owner have to bribe to claim that the new Exalt is part of their bloodline?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not convinced - look at the precedent of how Patrician Houses are compensated for the adoption of Dragon-Blooded by Great Houses, and how they can then be held liable if the Dragon-Blooded turns out to be a disappointment.<br /> <br /> The basis here isn't asserting ownership of a Dragon-Blooded (at least not more so than a house &quot;owns&quot; their scions), its being compensated for their mortal slave, lost to Exaltation.<br /> <br /> Edit: Dex raises an interesting point! I assumed at fist that a slave who Exalted as Dragon-Blooded would be treated as a commoner lost egg, and thus pick between the razor and coin. But it's possible that if they're owned by a Dynast, that Dynast's House might have adoption rights! Or if they were Patrician owned, there might be the option of Dynastic adoption with the Patrician house being compensated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-21-2018, 02:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T07:27:13-07:00","id":1209616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1209519#post1209519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not convinced - look at the precedent of how Patrician Houses are compensated for the adoption of Dragon-Blooded by Great Houses, and how they can then be held liable if the Dragon-Blooded turns out to be a disappointment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying that Dragon-Blooded are priceless, but that it would be insulting and petty to obsess over the mere cost of a slave compared to your new (possibly strained!) relationship with a Dragon-Blood. And even if you were enough of a Scrooge to think about it, the Realm has no obligation to compensate you for property lost to a clear act of the Elemental Dragons.<br /> <br /> Someone's probably tried to claim it, but I suspect they got a brutally polite denial from the tax assessor about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T08:20:22-07:00","id":1209636,"title":"","content":"So it's basically like in the United States, if one's slave is discovered to be somebody that was actually free, with corroborating documentation?<br /> <br /> \u200bAt least, that was the impression I got from 12 Years a Slave; that part of why Benedict Cumberbatch's character won't hear anything of Solomon Northup being a freeman is because he's still making payments for him, and when Solomon walks off with his friend carrying his identity papers, Michael Fassbender's character gets no compensation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1209511#post1209511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <i>really interesting</i> question is: who does the slave owner have to bribe to claim that the new Exalt is part of their bloodline?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHmm, I was wondering about the question of whether a Dynast would <i>want</i> to, but considering the barriers to adopting commoner or foreign outcastes, I suppose that they might actually be expected to. That and it represents the rare opportunity in which a Dynast or patrician might be the first one to note the person Exalting, and in circumstances private enough where it might not be reported to a prefectural official that could pass it to the Imperial Service*.<br /> <br /> \u200bBuuuut it also does strike me as a circumstance that would go beyond just bribery and forging records. Isn't the social circle of a Dynast or patrician going to be well aware that they have not had a child for the past 9-20 years? Even if there's a claim that the child was kept completely isolated and home-schooled for that period, it seems to me that a lot of people who might try it will have been publically living in a manner that will indicate that such wasn't the case.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt seems like the kind of thing in which you'd need to pay for the silence of a <i>lot</i> of people, or else just rely on the hope that everybody in your social circle will politely ignore the fact that it's basically impossible for you to have had a child in that time. Or hell, what if you <i>did</i>?<br /> <br /> \u200bUnless it's a question of claiming that they're part of your bloodline in the sense of being an Exalted child of your mortal fifth cousin six times removed that none of your friends have met but who very politely offered their one Exalted scion to a household better suited to handling their needs?<br /> <br /> \u200b* Note to self on other circumstances in which that might happen: a Dynast on a hunting trip deep in the wilderness who happens upon some poaching peasant children, one of whom Exalts (raises ominous questions about what might be done with the other ones). A Dynast woman having been around the Threshold for long enough that when she happens upon some foreign outcaste, she can plausibly claim that the child had been hers and with her the whole time, and she's only just returning with them now that they've Exalted.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T08:21:38-07:00","id":1209637,"title":"","content":"Some new limitted tiers opened up in case folks missed them and some of the previous ones are still available:<br /> <br /> $285 General of the Maelstrom Legion: Get your character name into the Companion or upcoming book. 6/10 left.<br /> <br /> $305 Archimandrite of the Immaculate Order: Copy of the Exalted 3e core's deluxe edition in case you want one along along wiht DBs. 14/150 left.<br /> <br /> $340 Sorcerer of the White Register: Custom Dragon-Blooded Charm. 12/20 left.<br /> <br /> $425 Admiral of the Fire Fleet: Pick a canonical character for the devs to put in the Companion or upcoming book as a QC. 5/5 left.<br /> <br /> $475 Honored Elder of a Great House: Character illustration in the Companion or another upcoming book. 6/6 left","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T09:33:04-07:00","id":1209662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1209462#post1209462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's in the text I missed it. What's Realm law on when a slave Exalts as Dragon-Blooded? I assume they're automatically freed and then treated like a commoner Found Egg (Razor or Coin)...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's correct; it's explicitly covered in the text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1209462#post1209462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but I'm guessing the former owner is entitled to compensation? Is the new Dragon-Blooded considered in debt to them, or do the Legions, Order, or Empress just pay them the cost of the mortal slave they lost, or what?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unsure; we didn't cover it in the text, and I don't see any coverage in <i>Exalted: the Outcaste</i>. I'm not sure whether the former owner is compensated. The outcaste is not indebted to her former owner; I'm not sure why one might think she should be. Her obligations are solely to the Empress.<br /> <br /> Note that slaves on the Blessed Isle may only be owned by the Dragon-Blooded, whose stipends make any such compensation nominal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T09:37:32-07:00","id":1209664,"title":"","content":"Thanks Eric!<br /> <br /> In other news, QC signature characters achieved. Prasad Expansion #2 added as stretchgoal at 295k.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T10:06:56-07:00","id":1209678,"title":"","content":"Oooo... new Caul preview!<br /> <br /> I wonder if Sh\u2019a Oka is what he seems (a specific elder Lunar who is either really good at faking his death or has some kind of resurrection power), or if it\u2019s a mantle. Perhaps his form is one that a Lunar of the Caul can somehow adopt to their form library, so there\u2019s always a Sh\u2019a Oka when the time calls for him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T12:07:41-07:00","id":1209722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1209662#post1209662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that slaves on the Blessed Isle may only be owned by the Dragon-Blooded, whose stipends make any such compensation nominal.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case, I take it slaves are generally only used as servants on the Isle? They\u2019re not used as a labor force for agriculture/industry?<br /> <br /> That would make sense with the (compared to oppressed populations in the Threshold) beneficial status the Realm extends Isle commoners - you don\u2019t want imported slaves putting them out of work.<br /> <br /> Any slave plantations would be in satrapies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T12:25:04-07:00","id":1209729,"title":"","content":"James Bell just commented on the Kickstarter that the 335k stretchgoal would be to add Warstriders to Heirs.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a long shot but it\u2019s possible if the end of campaign surge picks up early enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T12:30:44-07:00","id":1209733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1209722#post1209722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In that case, I take it slaves are generally only used as servants on the Isle? They\u2019re not used as a labor force for agriculture/industry?<br /> <br /> That would make sense with the (compared to oppressed populations in the Threshold) beneficial status the Realm extends Isle commoners - you don\u2019t want imported slaves putting them out of work.<br /> <br /> Any slave plantations would be in satrapies?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dragon-Blooded may assign slaves to mortal overseers on the Isle, including manual labor. But the Dragon-Blood remains the owner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T12:42:11-07:00","id":1209737,"title":"","content":"295k stretch goal is the second Prasad expansion, including the Dragon Clans and notable Prasadi NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T12:46:28-07:00","id":1209742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1209451#post1209451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if i\u2019m not mistaken about the signature characters....<br /> <br /> Air - Dynast Sorcerer<br /> Earth - Found Egg in the Legions<br /> Fire - Outcaste<br /> Water - Immaculate (unclear if Found-Egg or Dynast with dropped family name)<br /> Wood - Lookshyan</div> </div> </div> </div>From the opening fic:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Swift was a lost egg who\u2019d taken the coin; she couldn\u2019t be more than a dozen years into her service. River might have asked if Swift wished she\u2019d taken the razor instead, but, well. That wouldn\u2019t necessarily have kept her away from this disaster. River herself was proof of that. </div> </div> </div>I'd take that as indication that River is herself a lost egg who took the razor. That would also fit with the new signatures representing each potential origin for your Terrestrial characters (Prasadi and Forest Witches excepted).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T12:55:54-07:00","id":1209747,"title":"","content":"Do we know anything about Left Hand yet? Just occurred to me they could be a Forest Witch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T13:43:54-07:00","id":1209766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ascension</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1209742#post1209742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd take that as indication that River is herself a lost egg who took the razor. That would also fit with the new signatures representing each potential origin for your Terrestrial characters (Prasadi and Forest Witches excepted).</div> </div> </div> </div>River is a Ledaal who joined the Immaculate Order.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1209747#post1209747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we know anything about Left Hand yet? Just occurred to me they could be a Forest Witch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chalima is an outcaste from the Scavenger Lands. She's not affiliated with a larger outcaste group or lineage.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T14:14:43-07:00","id":1209776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1209722#post1209722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They\u2019re not used as a labor force for agriculture/industry?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI would suppose that the kinds of agriculture engaged in by House Cynis are more likely to be done by slaves<br /> <br /> \u200bI think that may go for the Houses in general, if there's still a background to the Realm of the Empress having wanted to limit the power that Dynasts held over the peasantry. So it might be that Dynast estates produce luxury foodstuffs worked by slaves, while the peasants are providing the more bulk food and raw materials for the cities and armies.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T18:20:38-07:00","id":1209844,"title":"","content":"The Caul is neat. It plays nicely into some of my own ideas about the mythology of the origins of the Dragon Blooded. I can also see some benefits to the idea that it was absent for a big chunk of history. I also like the described potential of the pilgrimage as a political tool; possibly for periods in which adopted daughters of the Empress had the strength of their bloodline elevated a bit to remove the uncertainty from some desired appointments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T18:25:05-07:00","id":1209845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1209636#post1209636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bBuuuut it also does strike me as a circumstance that would go beyond just bribery and forging records. Isn't the social circle of a Dynast or patrician going to be well aware that they have not had a child for the past 9-20 years? Even if there's a claim that the child was kept completely isolated and home-schooled for that period, it seems to me that a lot of people who might try it will have been publically living in a manner that will indicate that such wasn't the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mistakes happen, whether we're talking about &quot;oops I misfiled something, here have a talent of jade&quot; or &quot;oops I had an affair, how embarrassing, guess I gotta claim the kid.&quot; Sometimes it's convenient to claim a mistake where there was none.<br /> <br /> It's also illustrative to recall the &quot;hide a pillow under your robe for six months&quot; school of chicanery introduced in 1st Edition. A bit of &quot;everyone politely pretends the timeline makes sense&quot; can save a lot of embarrassment and money in the long run. At the very least, your Great House has a vested interest in pretending things were always this way. And if you're part of a patrician household, doubly so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T18:51:54-07:00","id":1209850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1209845#post1209845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mistakes happen, whether we're talking about &amp;quot;oops I misfiled something, here have a talent of jade&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;oops I had an affair, how embarrassing, guess I gotta claim the kid.&amp;quot; Sometimes it's convenient to claim a mistake where there was none.</div> </div> </div> </div>Claiming the child from an affair isn\u2019t a right men have in the Realm. Children share the legal social status/alignment of their mother regardless of who the father is. That\u2019s why the pillow-trick is a thing - so Dynasts can lay claim to a husband\u2019s bastards they would otherwise lose to the Razor or Coin if they Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T18:55:40-07:00","id":1209853,"title":"","content":"I wonder if we'll get any details about the other four shrines on the Caul. Or the hidden city/shrine the Dragon-Blooded want to reach.<br /> <br /> The Earth shrine has an interesting effect upon the land around it. It would be nice to know what the other shrines do, and how the Lunar Exalted might be making use of them.<br /> <br /> Also, I find it amusing that the port-city is the home of the Earth shrine rather than the Water one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T19:03:22-07:00","id":1209856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1209850#post1209850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Claiming the child from an affair isn\u2019t a right men have in the Realm. Children share the legal social status/alignment of their mother regardless of who the father is. That\u2019s why the pillow-trick is a thing - so Dynasts can lay claim to a husband\u2019s bastards they would otherwise lose to the Razor or Coin if they Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right! I misremembered some details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T19:05:03-07:00","id":1209858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1209853#post1209853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if we'll get any details about the other four shrines on the Caul. Or the hidden city/shrine the Dragon-Blooded want to reach.<br /> <br /> The Earth shrine has an interesting effect upon the land around it. It would be nice to know what the other shrines do, and how the Lunar Exalted might be making use of them.<br /> <br /> Also, I find it amusing that the port-city is the home of the Earth shrine rather than the Water one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, the complete pilgrimage route is in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T20:23:39-07:00","id":1209877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1209845#post1209845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also illustrative to recall the &quot;hide a pillow under your robe for six months&quot; school of chicanery introduced in 1st Edition. A bit of &quot;everyone politely pretends the timeline makes sense&quot; can save a lot of embarrassment and money in the long run. At the very least, your Great House has a vested interest in pretending things were always this way. And if you're part of a patrician household, doubly so.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat makes sense if you intend to raise a child whose parentage denotes a possibility of Exalting from birth, but less so if one is trying to claim that a slave who I'm presuming has Exalted somewhere around their mid-teens is your own child, whether the Dynast trying to pull that off is a man or woman.<br /> <br /> \u200bHey, while there are writers answering some questions in this thread: disregarding the religious attitude, what's the legal status of gods or elementals having the children of Dynastic men in the Realm? Are they assumed to have any legal claim to them, say, akin to patricians, or does the Immaculate Order come around insisting that the violation of divine order needs to be redressed by surrendering them to the Assessors?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 04-21-2018, 11:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T21:26:54-07:00","id":1209892,"title":"","content":"The bittersweet thing about stretch goals, no matter what there is probably going to be something super sweet we are told could have been only to not get it (unless there is a last second super surge of a several thousand dollars that leaves no time to put up further goals, but that seems really unlikely).<br /> <br /> Anyway, loved the stuff on the Caul. I am guessing that people that die without dramatically turning to dust starve to death or something like that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T22:29:50-07:00","id":1209907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1209858#post1209858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, the complete pilgrimage route is in there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very exciting. <br /> <br /> Will there be any advice for how to judge if a particular DB is &quot;worthy&quot; of a temple's blessing?<br /> <br /> How about any advice as regards the security of the temples, in case a PC group wanted to try for an illicit pilgrimage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T23:18:01-07:00","id":1209922,"title":"","content":"Worthiness for the pilgrimage seems like the kind of thing that would be ST fiat like it is if any kid you have in a game that time skips around enough that starts to be relevant gets to exalt as a dragon blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T06:58:01-07:00","id":1210009,"title":"","content":"Whenever the writing doesn't specify the criteria of &quot;worthiness&quot;, it's always the ST and/or player's call.<br /> <br /> Just like for Exaltation. There are no official criteria for who a god feels is worthy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T17:00:51-07:00","id":1210186,"title":"","content":"Hit 275K to get the cadet house expansion","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T18:34:22-07:00","id":1210210,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">After the Prasad #2 expansion, there's a paybump for the writers at 300k, and 2 page player handouts at 305k.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T18:40:22-07:00","id":1210213,"title":"","content":"I had already set 300K as the minimum I wanted to see it get for some reason I can't remember but that is another really good reason to manage to get it. Unfortunately my wallet can't handle giving more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T18:41:46-07:00","id":1210214,"title":"","content":"I have no doubt we'll hit 300k. The rate of increase is already picking up a bit, and it will SURGE with the 48 hour notice goes out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T04:44:52-07:00","id":1210366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1210213#post1210213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had already set 300K as the minimum I wanted to see it get for some reason I can't remember but that is another really good reason to manage to get it. Unfortunately my wallet can't handle giving more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if it doesn't hit 300k, are you comfortable with not having the book because it didn't hit a number that didn't even add a reward you would want to get?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T05:42:20-07:00","id":1210378,"title":"","content":"$300k is happening. It's $335k that's up in the air.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1210366#post1210366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, if it doesn't hit 300k, are you comfortable with not having the book because it didn't hit a number that didn't even add a reward you would want to get?</div> </div> </div> </div>... What? What does this have to do with what Mizu said at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T09:44:11-07:00","id":1210465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1210366#post1210366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, if it doesn't hit 300k, are you comfortable with not having the book because it didn't hit a number that didn't even add a reward you would want to get?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to clarify, are you asking if I was planning on cancelling my pledge and not getting the stuff if it looked like it wasn't going to hit 300K? If so then no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T10:33:08-07:00","id":1210483,"title":"","content":"I think that for being the first Ex3 Kickstarter after the Core, it has done very well. Shows the resilience of the IP's fanbase.<br /> <br /> The Core Kickstarter was somewhat disastrous in the &quot;instill confidence&quot; department. And many people throughout other mediums have said that they would look into how OP handles the DB Kickstarter before even considering backing OP Kickstaters (let alone Ex3 Kickstarters).<br /> <br /> So even if we don\u00b4t reach 300k (500%) which I hope we do (specially for the pay bump), I think the balance is very positive and the future trends to bright for future fatsplats (Lunars, soon, hopefully).<br /> <br /> Ex3 needs steam, the current team is working towards it. The work they are putting out is great. And while I don't think we can consider that the line has hit it's stride, if Lunars come soon enough, I will consider that it has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T17:50:04-07:00","id":1210702,"title":"","content":"I have a slight point of confusion on the latest added stretch goal, when they say it will be in color they mean the physical copies right? Seems odd that they would have the PDFs not be in color given all the colored art previews.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"