row-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what do people think about what we did with the fiction this time 'round?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it. Very nice to have a narrative through line that lets us see lots of things.<br /> <br /> I was surprised when we had a random monk in front of the MA chapter, given that River was a Sig. Finding out that she was an apostate and married was a fun surprise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T12:30:17-07:00","id":1211099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1211085#post1211085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'd have to ask the Kickstarter backers who went for the &amp;quot;bring back a canonical 1e/2e character as a Quick Character&amp;quot; reward tier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that one might be \u201cfun\u201d for future installments.<br /> <br /> Will future Kickstarters have a \u201cdelete this past character from the current book\u201d reward tier?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T12:39:18-07:00","id":1211103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1211099#post1211099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will future Kickstarters have a \u201cdelete this past character from the current book\u201d reward tier?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">10char</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T12:41:20-07:00","id":1211105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1211094#post1211094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like it. Very nice to have a narrative through line that lets us see lots of things.<br /> <br /> I was surprised when we had a random monk in front of the MA chapter, given that River was a Sig. Finding out that she was an apostate and married was a fun surprise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that she didn't leave the Immaculate Order because she was disillusioned with the Order or the Philosophy. She left because she fell in love and felt that pursuing a relationship meant more to her than membership in the Order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T13:35:14-07:00","id":1211129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1211085#post1211085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'd have to ask the Kickstarter backers who went for the &quot;bring back a canonical 1e/2e character as a Quick Character&quot; reward tier.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I thought about this'n, but then I remembered that Tepet Elana was backdoored in during the Empress' chapter fiction, and all was right with the world again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T15:55:45-07:00","id":1211192,"title":"","content":"Prasad expansion achieved. Should we get to 325k, there's a second expansion on the War in the West.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T18:11:12-07:00","id":1211246,"title":"","content":"So, is Mnemon now officially mother/grandmother/great grandmother/etc of the year by dynast standards? Provided they don't rock the boat of course, but dynastic standards aren't very high in that regard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T18:25:52-07:00","id":1211250,"title":"","content":"I'm not really clear on why the Wanasaan have a sorcery initiation... I mean... I guess they weren't going to provide necromancy early just for them. But it's not like sorcery is involved with their setting niche at all. Regular Occult Charms cover it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T19:33:29-07:00","id":1211267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1211246#post1211246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, is Mnemon now officially mother/grandmother/great grandmother/etc of the year by dynast standards? Provided they don't rock the boat of course, but dynastic standards aren't very high in that regard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems unlikely. There are likely to be plenty of Dynastic parents who treat their kids in roughly the same manner she does. Using the carrot rather than the stick to get what they want out of their children.<br /> <br /> The writeup is... intriguingly silent on how Mnemon treats scions of her bloodline who defy her will, after she generously lavished so much time and attention on them. I have a hard time imagining someone who is known to hate compromising and holds grudges for a long time reacts well to that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T19:48:17-07:00","id":1211269,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about it and I think I figured out why the Heirloom bonus generally felt underwhelming to me. Granted, I was expecting something like the weapon either only working for scions of a given house or that it would have a unique higher essence evocation that only unlocked for that house or something like that, but &quot;You automatically unlock the first evocation free if you're of the blood-line I like&quot; is actually pretty nice. However, there are enough artifacts that already grant any resonant wielder their first Evocation for free, that it doesn't really feel particularly special for that to generally be the Heirloom bonus.<br /> <br /> The artifacts are quite cool in general, I loved their stories ( &quot;Attempted Bribery&quot; ), but ...I dunno, I'd want a secret technique or something that only unlocked for my House. <br /> <br /> To be fair, Imprimatur's bonus of +1 to max Renown for Nellens and Perdurant Vault's access to a city that's potentially full of house secrets and wonders, both kinda work for me. I guess I kinda feel like Traverse the Secret City should only awaken for members of House Ragara and maybe the Nellens bonus to max renown should be bigger or have an upgrade charm, but both of those feel like unique bonuses that allow members of that house to really get more out of the artifact than anyone else can, literally in Nellen's case and figuratively in Ragara's case.<br /> <br /> (I figure that any Ragara that left something in there for a future wielder would have left records for them and defenses, just in case the shield was lost or stolen. So, anyone who invades the vault without access to the Ragara records should be in for some nasty surprises.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T19:54:45-07:00","id":1211270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1211267#post1211267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seems unlikely. There are likely to be plenty of Dynastic parents who treat their kids in roughly the same manner she does. Using the carrot rather than the stick to get what they want out of their children.<br /> <br /> The writeup is... intriguingly silent on how Mnemon treats scions of her bloodline who defy her will, after she generously lavished so much time and attention on them. I have a hard time imagining someone who is known to hate compromising and holds grudges for a long time reacts well to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly wish she'd had someone loving she could trust to help her avoid becoming paranoid all those years ago. Granted, her older brother WAS trying to kill her and I'm not sure she'd have made it to where she is now WITHOUT becoming paranoid, but..... It just kind of hurts to know that she always has this wall up and there's a part of her that's always searching the area for danger, because she won't ever let herself get hurt or be helpless ever again. <br /> <br /> I kinda wish she and V'Neef could reconcile, because I could imagine that V'Neef might be able to be that person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T20:03:17-07:00","id":1211275,"title":"","content":"The cooler we made the house-specific magic shticks, the more it felt like we were funneling people toward having to use them, thereby enforcing stereotypical house characters, and the more it felt like we were at risk of accidentally giving one or two houses shticks the Internet at large would fixated on as substandard, thereby condemning them to being seen by the fanbase as \u201cthe suck house\u201d for the remainder of the edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T21:04:48-07:00","id":1211282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1211275#post1211275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The cooler we made the house-specific magic shticks, the more it felt like we were funneling people toward having to use them, thereby enforcing stereotypical house characters, and the more it felt like we were at risk of accidentally giving one or two houses shticks the Internet at large would fixated on as substandard, thereby condemning them to being seen by the fanbase as \u201cthe suck house\u201d for the remainder of the edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. As long as I can say that the heirloom bonus of artifacts I create is more substantial, I'll get over my disappointment, because the artifacts in the book are still very cool. Calumny was someone answering my desire for an Ultimately Useful Tube with evocations, Perdurant Vault is several kinds of cool, I love the backstories on Daring Venture and Sea's Verdict (and the way it crumbles and everything), and everything else was pretty awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T21:05:11-07:00","id":1211283,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but look at the scale she does it on. That seems like a tremendous amount of effort on her part given all the other balls she has to juggle just to hand out some carrots instead of letting others ingratiate them to the house. She also did things like try to save her siblings and give monuments to the ones that weren't saved. That is a lot of acting to do (especially since she is envious of V'neef for nailing mother's charisma when she can't do that) as opposed to just ever so slightly letting her guard down around some family. I mean it is still plausible I guess, maybe family is just easier to fool because they let <b>their</b> guard down for their sister/whatever generation removed ancestor she is and buy her terrible acting. One big act she is doing in the 'enlightened self-interest' genre and she is also a massive control freak that can't stand to let someone else handle all the carrot waving because they might get it wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T21:15:01-07:00","id":1211286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1211270#post1211270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I honestly wish she'd had someone loving she could trust to help her avoid becoming paranoid all those years ago. Granted, her older brother WAS trying to kill her and I'm not sure she'd have made it to where she is now WITHOUT becoming paranoid, but..... It just kind of hurts to know that she always has this wall up and there's a part of her that's always searching the area for danger, because she won't ever let herself get hurt or be helpless ever again.<br /> <br /> I kinda wish she and V'Neef could reconcile, because I could imagine that V'Neef might be able to be that person.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly, I'd kind of wondered about that exact point given my first introduction was.... 2E Mnemon, but more and more of the 3E presentation was intriguing me. This writeup's kind of cemented the image of Mnemon as damaged in an incredibly functional way, and the image of my Earth Aspect just kind of making helping the grandmother that helped her through her early life so much a big social goal is just kind of great. Given V'neef's only a &quot;minor&quot; level of resentment, it'll be interesting to see how that shakes out in game. Does &quot;help Mnemon reconnect with her family that aren't assholes like Ragara&quot; count as a legendary social goal? :lol:","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1817-opmegs","name":"OpMegs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1817_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T21:19:11-07:00","id":1211287,"title":"","content":"While I understand the desire for the heirloom bennies to be bit more pronounced, I personnaly didn't find the absence thereof so disappointing because what we got was so evocative, pardon the pun.<br /> <br /> The idea of a family artifact really doesn't work too well outside of longstanding DB families, given the small pool of people that can use artifacts. And I have to say I really loved some of the artifacts. The stories attached to them really felt like family histories, that I then could be a part of and carry on. These house artifacts almost work so well to define the houses that I wish they were in Chapter 2 instead of their own chapter.<br /> <br /> I particularly found the Ledaal artifact played off the house beautifully, not to mention the clever twist about the lightning bolt looking like dragon's teeth, so Immaculates wouldn't even bat an eye at it.<br /> <br /> It's like getting your grandfathers car that he drove when he asked your grandmother to go steady, but then also used to run over the unholy killer attacking kids at Lovers lane, so the car is now imbued with sacred power to destroy demons, and it is your sixteenth birthday don't scratch it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T22:11:13-07:00","id":1211295,"title":"","content":"disregard, sleeping pills made me loopy quicker then I thought","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 04-25-2018, 01:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T22:18:50-07:00","id":1211296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1209079#post1209079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, and the printed pinnacle Charms aren't necessarily the end of those trees; just the official ones.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I definitely want Terrestrial Brawl to include sand-bending, since it's so similar to Currents Sweep to Sea and Smashing Tidal Wave.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, I don't think Earth Dragon Style will let you kick up a stone wall to block ranged attacks, so we need to find a place for that in the Charmset, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>A couple of the artifacts have upgrade charms that basically reskin existing DB charms with a new Element. Maybe a set of White Jade Smashfists that do sand-bending are in order?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T02:19:00-07:00","id":1211329,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1211303#post1211303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sea's Verdict's first evocation, From the Depths, interacts with the Aura mechanic. I didn't think artifacts were allowed to do that, so is that a typo, or did I misunderstand things?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is an acceptable exception. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That evocation is gated behind a Dragonblooded charm prerequisite. Playing nicely with the Dragonblooded' toys should be <i>encouraged </i>for those.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Also, Sea's Verdict has </span></span></span><i>its own anima banner</i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">. This is ice coolness.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 04-25-2018, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T11:22:43-07:00","id":1211476,"title":"","content":"We've hit 305k! <br /> <br /> There's quite a few Custom Charm and NPC tiers left in there. If those sold out we'd almost certainly hit the next few stretch goals!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10995-abakus","name":"Abakus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T11:37:00-07:00","id":1211484,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I want the warstrider one. Wish that one was sooner","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10745-nosleeves","name":"nosleeves","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T13:32:10-07:00","id":1211538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OpMegs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1211286#post1211286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does &quot;help Mnemon reconnect with her family that aren't assholes like Ragara&quot; count as a legendary social goal? :lol:</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be VERY hesitant of romanticizing Mnemon. You don't become the head of a Great House and cultivate the sort of powerbase it has for centuries without being something of an asshole yourself; even Cathak Cainan, who presents as a morally upright Realm patriot, wasn't above shanking dramatically weakening the Realm in order to shank House Tepet when the chance arose.<br /> <br /> (Sidebar: this super frustrated me about Cathak's writeup. Those are supposed to be neutral and present true information, not an idealized self-image, and Cainan's went on and on and on about what a big patriot he was and how into duty and honor he was and I just kept thinking &quot;am I supposed to fucking buy this six chapters after I read about how they tripped House Tepet and then starting kicking them in the ribs when they were down, jeopardizing the Realm's interests in the face of the greatest Solar empire-builder since the First Age?&quot;)<br /> <br /> Anyway. Mnemon hasn't held onto her position by having a secret soft center. Mnemon is hard as nails and she is absolutely as likely to try murdering her way to the Throne as Ragara is.<br /> <br /> I do wonder how genuine and flexible her faith was. In prior editions she was absolutely willing to, say, invite Abyssals into the Realm to treat with her.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T15:50:44-07:00","id":1211598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1211538#post1211538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">am I supposed to fucking buy this six chapters after I read about how they tripped House Tepet and then starting kicking them in the ribs when they were down, jeopardizing the Realm's interests in the face of the greatest Solar empire-builder since the First Age?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. <br /> <br /> When you ask a Dragon-Blooded, &quot;What's best for the Realm?&quot;, the answer is not likely to be one that seems consistent with the priorities of an unbiased omniscient robot.<br /> <br /> After all, House Tepet was something he could see, feel, and plan for; the same is not true of the Solar Exalted returning <i>en masse</i> from their moldering graves. It's entirely reasonable for a Dragon-Blooded at the time to answer that the greatest threat facing the Realm in the immediate future is House Tepet trying to step in and take over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-25-2018, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T16:34:12-07:00","id":1211606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1211538#post1211538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would be VERY hesitant of romanticizing Mnemon. You don't become the head of a Great House and cultivate the sort of powerbase it has for centuries without being something of an asshole yourself; even Cathak Cainan, who presents as a morally upright Realm patriot, wasn't above shanking dramatically weakening the Realm in order to shank House Tepet when the chance arose.<br /> <br /> (Sidebar: this super frustrated me about Cathak's writeup. Those are supposed to be neutral and present true information, not an idealized self-image, and Cainan's went on and on and on about what a big patriot he was and how into duty and honor he was and I just kept thinking &quot;am I supposed to fucking buy this six chapters after I read about how they tripped House Tepet and then starting kicking them in the ribs when they were down, jeopardizing the Realm's interests in the face of the greatest Solar empire-builder since the First Age?&quot;)<br /> <br /> Anyway. Mnemon hasn't held onto her position by having a secret soft center. Mnemon is hard as nails and she is absolutely as likely to try murdering her way to the Throne as Ragara is.<br /> <br /> I do wonder how genuine and flexible her faith was. In prior editions she was absolutely willing to, say, invite Abyssals into the Realm to treat with her.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly can't chuck so many stones at the Realm for being myopic given I know full well my own lifestyle is only possible because people are getting screwed over in some other country and haven't really done anything at all about it. I guess at least I can claim 'out of sight out of mind' while a lot of them are directly involved into grinding foreigners under their boot to get resources for house and country.<br /> <br /> <br /> On more awesome notes, at 335K we get two warstrider write ups (one belonging to the Realm the other belonging to Lookshy). Come on we can totally make it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 04-25-2018, 10:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T17:01:01-07:00","id":1211610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1211598#post1211598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you ask a Dragon-Blooded, &quot;What's best for the Realm?&quot;, the answer is not likely to be one that seems consistent with the priorities of an unbiased omniscient robot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was under the impression that the various informational writeups were meant to at least attempt to be unbiased and objection, tho.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's entirely reasonable for a Dragon-Blooded at the time to answer that the greatest threat facing the Realm in the immediate future is House Tepet trying to step in and take over. </div> </div> </div>This isn't made explicit, tho, nor does it square with the presentation of Cathak Cainan as being super into duty and honor; abrogating your responsibilities to support your fellow Dynasts against the Anathema in exchange for short-term political gain is neither dutiful nor honorable.<br /> <br /> For that matter, this doesn't even fit House Cathak's motivations in a realpolitik sense, as elsewhere they're on record as going &quot;we'll support whoever looks like they've basically already got it locked in.&quot; Why would they care if that were House Tepet?<br /> <br /> This has always been a problem with Cathak Cainan, not just in this edition. In my opinion, we could either use some wordcount devoted to how House Cathak squares this circle internally, OR the Cathak legions should have been replaced by the Sesus legions when it comes to which Great House was supposed to march in support of the Tepet's against the Bull and instead decided to pull the rug out.<br /> <br /> Because so much of the wordcount devoted to him is all about how he's this dutiful, honorable guy who isn't going to try and seize the throne himself because he knows he's too old and he just wants to serve the Realm and how he treats friends and foes with honor and dignity. And like... great! Reconcile that with the Bull of the North, please! People are complicated. Expose and discuss this complexity! How does he feel about this hypocrisy? DOES he view it as hypocrisy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":4742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","user":"Murcushio","date":". 04-25-2018, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T19:14:42-07:00","id":1211649,"title":"","content":"Just thought I'd point out, still some of those special limited reward tiers left. Like getting to choose one dragon blooded from a past edition besides the Scarlet Empress for a quick character write up or name a character new to the canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T03:36:03-07:00","id":1211726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1211538#post1211538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do wonder how genuine and flexible her faith was. In prior editions she was absolutely willing to, say, invite Abyssals into the Realm to treat with her.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that was one of the bigger mistakes they made with Mnemon and the notion of a Realm civil war as a whole.<br /> <br /> It makes the character look really stupid to players who know what the Deathlords are all about (i.e basically anyone literate, it's in their fucking name) creates a plot seed for &quot;Turns out the outcome of the Realm Civil War was a ... ... ... <b>DEATHLORD PLOT!!!</b>&quot; turning it from Game of Thrones into a Saturday Morning Cartoon. <br /> It's also taking something that one of the less advantaged houses could be considering to tip the scales out of genuine fear they'll be purged if they don't and giving it to Mnemon.<br /> <br /> Yeah, it'll all pan out if the stuff with the Abyssals is really part of her plan to prepare for her mother's return like how 2nd edition spun it but now we have ... ... ... <b>YOZI PLOT!!!</b> which isn't any better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T03:48:04-07:00","id":1211730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1211610#post1211610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has always been a problem with Cathak Cainan, not just in this edition. In my opinion, we could either use some wordcount devoted to how House Cathak squares this circle internally, OR the Cathak legions should have been replaced by the Sesus legions when it comes to which Great House was supposed to march in support of the Tepet's against the Bull and instead decided to pull the rug out.</div> </div> </div> </div>This actually does get addressed in The Realm, as I recall, but the gist of it is that being a super honorable patriot means being super honorable and patriotic to the greatest machine for oppressing and pillaging jade out of the world, personified in the form of a half-deified overworked demigod. Cainan's not a moron and he's capable of doing shitty things, he just has to reconcile them first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T09:16:45-07:00","id":1211840,"title":"","content":"So, we didn't quiiiite hit that last stretch goal. Would it be possible to get one warstrider anyway? Instead of two?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T09:21:06-07:00","id":1211843,"title":"","content":"Do we know anything about the previous Tepet Matriarch? I\u2019m assuming they died fighting the Bull?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T09:42:41-07:00","id":1211855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1211726#post1211726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that was one of the bigger mistakes they made with Mnemon and the notion of a Realm civil war as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Honestly, 1E and 2E Mnemon is one of the three or four house leaders I can <i>absolutely</i> see being willing to try using Anathema to achieve her own ends.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It makes the character look really stupid to players who know what the Deathlords are all about (i.e basically anyone literate, it's in their fucking name) </div> </div> </div>Er... plenty of very intelligent people have made deals with forces that are inimical to their own long-term goals because they believed they could obtain short-term advantage from it and then outmaneuver them in the long run. This does not make them stupid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> creates a plot seed for &quot;Turns out the outcome of the Realm Civil War was a ... ... ... <b>DEATHLORD PLOT!!!</b>&quot; turning it from Game of Thrones into a Saturday Morning Cartoon. </div> </div> </div>Why wouldn't the Deathlords, especially Mask, who just bulldozed a satrapy, try and meddle in the Realm Civil War? This utterly makes sense. It's entirely in their interests to try. Why is this a bad plot seed for Storytellers to run with if they want to, and discard it as a minor irrelevancy (&quot;In this game, Mnemon made a one-time deal to get her hands on some soulsteel, outmaneuveing Mask, who was really hoping for more. That's it&quot;) when they don't?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's also taking something that one of the less advantaged houses could be considering to tip the scales out of genuine fear they'll be purged if they don't and giving it to Mnemon. </div> </div> </div>Now THIS is a compelling argument to me. Mnemon had a LOT of wordcount dedicated to her machinations in prior editions. Some of it was pretty great! The people writing her stuff often wrote her interestingly, and this created a kind of cycle where more people wanted to get in on someone they found super cool.<br /> <br /> But it also meant that a ton of stuff got laid across Mnemon's shoulders and some of that love could have been spread around. In the current edition, treating with the Deathlords to try and get a little bit of their mojo is something that... hmm. House Ragara, obviously. House Iselsi, maybe House Sesus. Potentially a couple others.<br /> <br /> Mnemon actually seems less likely to do it because in 3E she's taken such a strong &quot;you don't get to fuck with the Realm, that makes you my enemy&quot; stance she was willing to weaken her houses position in a potential civil war in order to make the point by re-conquering Jiara.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T10:03:39-07:00","id":1211865,"title":"","content":"Ahh, what conversations have taken place while I've been focused on my analysis of the book?<br /> <br /> Hmm, too much argument for my blood. Even if Mnemon is one of my favoured revisions in this go around.<br /> <br /> What else is there...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1211843#post1211843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we know anything about the previous Tepet Matriarch? I\u2019m assuming they died fighting the Bull?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat's said in the House's write up, yes. She's also mentioned in Arada's chapter fiction, as having been one of his Hearth mates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T10:24:10-07:00","id":1211876,"title":"","content":"Perhaps there\u2019s some reason Cainan rationalized that she needed to be out of the running for Empress \u201cfor the good of the Realm.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T10:24:59-07:00","id":1211877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1211855#post1211855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? Honestly, 1E and 2E Mnemon is one of the three or four house leaders I can <i>absolutely</i> see being willing to try using Anathema to achieve her own ends.</div> </div> </div> </div> 100%. It doesn't matter what you could see other House Leaders doing, that bridge was canonically crossed by Mnemon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Er... plenty of very intelligent people have made deals with forces that are inimical to their own long-term goals because they believed they could obtain short-term advantage from it and then outmaneuver them in the long run. This does not make them stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Semantics. This was published after Exalted; the Abyssals, players and Storytellers knew she was in way over her head dealing with a Deathlord directly and it undeniably shaped how they used her.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why wouldn't the Deathlords, especially Mask, who just bulldozed a satrapy, try and meddle in the Realm Civil War? This utterly makes sense. It's entirely in their interests to try. Why is this a bad plot seed for Storytellers to run with if they want to, and discard it as a minor irrelevancy (&quot;In this game, Mnemon made a one-time deal to get her hands on some soulsteel, outmaneuveing Mask, who was really hoping for more. That's it&quot;) when they don't?</div> </div> </div> </div> It's a bad plot seed because Storytellers felt bound to it and once the Anathema become involved in the Realm civil war it's very easy for it to become all about them.<br /> <br /> I also think a secret deal between major NPCs that the players know about because they read a particular source book is inherently shite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T10:28:54-07:00","id":1211880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1211876#post1211876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps there\u2019s some reason Cainan rationalized that she needed to be out of the running for Empress \u201cfor the good of the Realm.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>On that note, I've always envisioned Cathak Urima as his pragmatic shoulder devil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 04-26-2018, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T10:29:30-07:00","id":1211881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1211876#post1211876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps there\u2019s some reason Cainan rationalized that she needed to be out of the running for Empress \u201cfor the good of the Realm.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI could see a depiction in which Cainan thought that House Tepet being hobbled was a desired outcome, but never expected some of its more powerful members to actually fall at the head of their legions even against several Anathema (not that you'd get him to admit it was an unforeseen outcome and possibly detrimental).<br /> <br /> \u200bOn the other hand, lacking their matriarch means that the current leadership is divided against itself. It might be that she was never seen as a candidate for Empress (she might not have even wanted it), but if the House has to fall then it's better to go in pieces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T10:58:49-07:00","id":1211893,"title":"","content":"I must reiterate the bitter sweetness of kickstarter stretch goals, so very close to getting those warstrider write ups that could have been. But at least we got tons of other fun stuff, wonder how long that book is going to end up being after all those stretch goals were met? Same size as Arms and The Realm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T11:04:41-07:00","id":1211897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1211893#post1211893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must reiterate the bitter sweetness of kickstarter stretch goals, so very close to getting those warstrider write ups that could have been. But at least we got tons of other fun stuff, wonder how long that book is going to end up being after all those stretch goals were met? Same size as Arms and The Realm?</div> </div> </div> </div>Longer than either, at least by my current rough estimation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T11:27:23-07:00","id":1211906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1211881#post1211881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI could see a depiction in which Cainan thought that House Tepet being hobbled was a desired outcome, but never expected some of its more powerful members to actually fall at the head of their legions even against several Anathema (not that you'd get him to admit it was an unforeseen outcome and possibly detrimental).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To continue the never-ending Game of Thrones comparisons, no one expected Geoffrey to kill Ned Stark","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T11:31:17-07:00","id":1211907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1211015#post1211015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, who can guess what purpose they'll serve as a bunch of Quick Characters in the average Exalted game?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYou bastard! Are we going to have to ask every single Wyld Hunt if they have an adorable family to go home to?!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T11:56:54-07:00","id":1211918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1211907#post1211907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bYou bastard! Are we going to have to ask every single Wyld Hunt if they have an adorable family to go home to?!</div> </div> </div> </div>The second &quot;Wyld Hunt&quot; my players ran into was the children of the PCs in a previous DB game and several of the players were in both games. So far they've managed to take the DBs prisoner and are trying to befriend them, but who knows what will happen in the long run?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T14:03:00-07:00","id":1211968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1210999#post1210999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can\u2019t wait to read about that super prison and why the Realm would take Anathema alive!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd imagine a Solar safely (?) under lock and key in the Imperial Manse is preferable to one killed, with the resultant new one popping up in a random unexpected location and stirring up trouble before the Wyld Hunt can find them.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T14:09:53-07:00","id":1211974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1211968#post1211968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd imagine a Solar safely (?) under lock and key in the Imperial Manse is preferable to one killed, with the resultant new one popping up in a random unexpected location and stirring up trouble before the Wyld Hunt can find them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Now that it\u2019s been clairified the escape was from the Imperial Manse, I tho k it\u2019s safe to say they were kept their for the personal mystic experimentation of the Empress.<br /> <br /> I was thinking though of that new Dragon-Blooded super-max that\u2019s going to be detailed in the Realm book. It\u2019s a fascinating hook, but i\u2019m still not clear on why the Realm would bother with a super-max. I guess because related Dynasts would take offense at executing their kin?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T14:50:59-07:00","id":1211998,"title":"","content":"Probably both. It doesn't take a genius to realise that locking anathema up alive means you have to spend far less resources and manpower playing whack-a-mole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T15:17:13-07:00","id":1212013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1211974#post1211974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now that it\u2019s been clairified the escape was from the Imperial Manse, I tho k it\u2019s safe to say they were kept their for the personal mystic experimentation of the Empress.<br /> <br /> I was thinking though of that new Dragon-Blooded super-max that\u2019s going to be detailed in the Realm book. It\u2019s a fascinating hook, but i\u2019m still not clear on why the Realm would bother with a super-max. I guess because related Dynasts would take offense at executing their kin?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because sometimes you need a stiffer penalty than a fine but a less severe penalty than death, maybe? <br /> <br /> Or maybe the Empress has plans for you, but she wants to soften you up first?<br /> <br /> Or maybe you ARE going to be executed, but for whatever reason you aren\u2019t allowed to be executed YET?<br /> <br /> Or maybe you know things and, once other people know them, you\u2019ll be placed somewhere else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 04-26-2018, 06:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T15:44:56-07:00","id":1212024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1212013#post1212013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because sometimes you need a stiffer penalty than a fine but a less severe penalty than death, maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in the ancient societies the Realmis based on generally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T18:03:58-07:00","id":1212087,"title":"","content":"Thinking back over some things:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1211538#post1211538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would be VERY hesitant of romanticizing Mnemon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that Mnemon needs to be romanticized to warrent somebody in her House having positive motivations towards her. There's still apparently a background of her having been nice to them in addition to harsh discipline, and I'd imagine that many grow up with values that cause them to view her formidable qualities with admiration. <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't become the head of a Great House and cultivate the sort of powerbase it has for centuries without being something of an asshole yourself</div> </div> </div> </div>But you also don't often achieve it without managing to cultivate some positive relationships, and that's an element that the new write-up placed emphasis on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway. Mnemon hasn't held onto her position by having a secret soft center.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the mistake here is looking at it as a dichotomy, rather than elements that can complement each other. I mean, it's there in the write-up; to her scions she can offer wisdom and comfort, she's counselled nervous children, lavishes affection on those whom she takes as lovers, and in private is known for generosity, good humour and deep devotion to the national ideology.<br /> <br /> \u200bMind, I would argue that it's a false dichotomy to regard such things as necessarily constituting softness. She doesn't need to be somebody that has a secret soft centre, or any less ruthless, to still be genuinely loving and capable of handing out affection and positive reinforcement. I've known or known of people whose general demeanour was rather harsh even in private, even with people that they liked, and it wasn't an obstacle to being able to engage in positive interpersonal interaction.<br /> <br /> \u200bHmm, note to self; take cues for her sense of humour from Lilith from Frasier.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mnemon is hard as nails and she is absolutely as likely to try murdering her way to the Throne as Ragara is.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI don't know; from this write-up, I can't see willingness to murder basically everybody, with an allowance to employ some especially underhanded means.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat being said, I would presume that even if Mnemon's resentment towards V'neef is currently a Minor thing, I would assume that it might be a bit difficult for a scion of her House to convince her to give it up. Not because it matters a lot to her, but because of how she regards her own position in the House; I can see her as being galled by the presumption of a scion who would try influencing her priorities like that, although I'd need to review how that might play out in rules beyond applying that Defining Tie to her Resolve.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T18:07:49-07:00","id":1212090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1212024#post1212024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not in the ancient societies the Realmis based on generally.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bNoo they did. That just usually took the form of a period of being subjected to hard labour, rather than being confined to a specific building.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T20:51:10-07:00","id":1212133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1212090#post1212090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bNoo they did. That just usually took the form of a period of being subjected to hard labour, rather than being confined to a specific building.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's markedly different though - &quot;society&quot; is still getting a &quot;use&quot; out of the enslaved convict*. Also in many cases that was an extension of the &quot;fine&quot;, option - with slavery being the result of being fined into debt.<br /> <br /> *dear lord please understand I'm not defending said system - convict slavery is an abomination that remains a bedrock part of the US prison industrial complex masquerading as a justice system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T22:08:14-07:00","id":1212153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1211877#post1211877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Semantics. This was published after Exalted; the Abyssals, players and Storytellers knew she was in way over her head dealing with a Deathlord directly and it undeniably shaped how they used her.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay? Yes? This is a problem?<br /> <br /> Every Storyteller and player who has read the splatbooks and the setting books knows a SHIT TON MORE about the secret, hidden truths of Creation and the true motivations of major setting figures than even very well-informed NPCs. This always shaped how they used those NPCs, as it should have done! That's... not actually a bad thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's a bad plot seed because Storytellers felt bound to it </div> </div> </div>&quot;Some Storytellers are very bad at their job&quot; isn't a problem the game should design around. &quot;Mnemon has entered into negotiations with a Deathlord over... something&quot; is an extremely vague plot seed that is both easily inconsequential or easily very consequential.<br /> <br /> I believe Jenna Moran once said explicitly something along the lines of &quot;Chejop Kejak is meant to be useful as a powerful and effective antagonist, but if you can't figure out a way to do that without breaking your game because you only conceive of things he'll do that will just make your players miserable and the game unfun, <i>don't use him</i>.&quot; (I'm paraphrasing.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and once the Anathema become involved in the Realm civil war it's very easy for it to become all about them. </div> </div> </div>Anathema are already involved in it in 3E. That's in the cores chapter fiction, in fact, there are Anathema building power bases on the Blessed Isle and totes getting involved.<br /> <br /> And what, precisely, is wrong with that? In a Solar game why SHOULDN'T Anathema be involved in the Realm Civil War? One of the most popular kind of Solars are Dynasts, in fact. Heck, even in a Dragon-Blooded game there's both in-setting and out-of-setting justification for Anathema becoming involved, because Solars and Lunars do not stop existing just because the Realm is fighting amongst itself. If you're running a DB game and don't want the Solars and Lunars involved in the Realm meltdown, you can plausibly keep them away, but if you DO want them involved the game should, and it very explicitly does, provide avenues for that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also think a secret deal between major NPCs that the players know about because they read a particular source book is inherently shite. </div> </div> </div>That's literally Chejop Kejak and the Empresses entire relationship; a secret deal between major NPCs that the players know about because they read a particular sourcebook.<br /> <br /> In fact that's... that's a TON of Sidereal stuff. And other stuff as well. Sesus Nagezzar's entire &quot;I am secretly a giant super-patriot and am single-handedly stabilizing the threshold&quot; thing is something players only know because they read a particular sourcebook. Secret deals between major NPCs are a big big part of the setting!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T22:21:39-07:00","id":1212156,"title":"","content":"Thanks for taking the time, Neall.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1211730#post1211730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This actually does get addressed in The Realm,</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, excellent! Thank you for setting my mind at ease.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> as I recall, but the gist of it is that being a super honorable patriot means being super honorable and patriotic to the greatest machine for oppressing and pillaging jade out of the world, personified in the form of a half-deified overworked demigod. </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, no question. I just... when discussing the morality and ethics of people within the Realm I usually assume we're discussing them within the broad cultural consensus OF the Realm unless explicitly stated otherwise. That just seems like a logical time-saver to me.<br /> <br /> The Realm, like all societies, has inherent contradictions between &quot;these are the values we say we uphold and value&quot; and &quot;these are the things that powerful, respected people can actually get away with and remain respected even though they violate the stated values.&quot;<br /> <br /> Like... it seems to me if you provided a roomful of Dynasts with convincing evidence that a sister murdered her brother to secure her line of succession, they'd likely feel compelled to condemn that act publicly because it goes against their societies stated values of honor, morality, law, and upright family relations even though some of them know that the REAL crime in question here is that she got <i>caught.</i><br /> <br /> But it also seems to me if you provided them with evidence that a Great House was deliberately impoverishing a satrapy to live high on the hog, they'd stare at you blankly waiting for the point to come, because in their lexicon it is honorable, moral, and legal to do this, because they're a superior class of being from a superior nation, and inferior people from an inferior nation, who were clearly born there because they weren't karmically worthy of being born into the Realm, SHOULD be impoverished so the Realm can live large. It doesn't violate either their unspoken values or their purported values, so there's no contradiction in play there.<br /> <br /> (I could be completely misreading this, of course.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cainan's not a moron and he's capable of doing shitty things, he just has to reconcile them first. </div> </div> </div>Right. I don't dispute this. I just think that the Tepet thing, plus continuing to put the boot into them after the fact, is a huge enough thing that wordcount should be spent on it. It's the sort of contradiction that someone who actually tries to live by the Realm's stated values, and it is a BIG PART of Cainan's character that he tries to do this, would seem to need to very much justify and reconcile themselves to.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T22:24:50-07:00","id":1212158,"title":"","content":"For my custom heirloom artifact, I'm wrestling now between a Green Jade Grimscythe and Blue Jade War Fans (or possibly paired Blue &amp; Red Jade War Fans).<br /> <br /> Though part of me would like to see armor heirlooms since none of the examples in WFHW are armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-27-2018, 01:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T23:20:41-07:00","id":1212162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1211918#post1211918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The second &amp;quot;Wyld Hunt&amp;quot; my players ran into was the children of the PCs in a previous DB game and several of the players were in both games. So far they've managed to take the DBs prisoner and are trying to befriend them, but who knows what will happen in the long run?</div> </div> </div> </div>You are a monster and can I play with you please","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T04:17:29-07:00","id":1212207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1212153#post1212153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;Mnemon has entered into negotiations with a Deathlord over... something&quot; is an extremely vague plot seed that is both easily inconsequential or easily very consequential.</div> </div> </div> </div>...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspect Book Earth page 4</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cI want military aid waiting when the Great Houses go to war,\u201d Mnemon began.Her eyes were hungry and far away. \u201cI want you to keep the Seventh Legion from interfering with that war.\u201d She focused once more on Sorrow\u2019s body, sensing the wash of unclean Essence blazing from within. \u201cI want spells,\u201d she finished.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm done debating you over this.<br /> <br /> For the benefit of anyone who doesn't have Aspect Book Earth it's the opening story which goes on for four pages, that's our extremely vague plot seed. I don't think every line should be scrutinised out of fear that someone\u2019s going to latch onto it and ruin everyone else\u2019s fun but this was clearly given weight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 04-27-2018, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T08:57:56-07:00","id":1212311,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m thinking about \u201cBender\u201d DBs this morning. Obviously the Immaculate Styles are a big part of that idea, but my mind kept coming back to Elemental Bolt. <br /> <br /> A DB who fights with that as their primary weapon seems like they\u2019re going to run out of motes VERY quickly since it eats up most of your respiration before enhancement and defensive charms, and yet a part of me wants that to be a viable combat style. On the other hand, an essentially Natural-tagged ranged weapon with tags like Disarming and Smashing that you can equip as a scenelong charm seems like it might be a problem. <br /> <br /> Did I miss a charm that would let you use this charm as your primary weapon? Or is it\u2019s non-sustainable mote cost necessary to balance its flexibility?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10995-abakus","name":"Abakus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T09:24:25-07:00","id":1212323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1212207#post1212207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> <br /> Yeah, I'm done debating you over this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, hmm. I'd legitimately forgotten about that. I was wrong! I remembered their meeting ending with the Abyssal coming up out of the water and then a fade. I clearly fucked that up.<br /> <br /> That's definitely way more weight than that should have had, then. &quot;Mnemon negotiating with the Deathlords for... something&quot; is a decent thing to drop in. &quot;Mnemon specifically wanting some spells&quot; is starting to push it a bit but is okay; a Dynast bartering with dark powers for (what they hope) will be a one-time deal is also cool. But if they're going to try and get a full-up military alliance with a Deathlord, that needs to be very very carefully considered from a meta perspective. There's narrative space for that, but it is fraught, and it probably shouldn't have been given to Mnemon specifically. (Although perhaps at the time nobody foresaw that Mnemon was going to get All The Wordcount, which is a bit of a planning failure.)<br /> <br /> I don't think this undermines the core thrusts of my arguments, tho. Especially since you made blanket statements that condemn common writing practices and enormous swathes of the setting outright. There's noting wrong with condemning enormous swathes of the setting, people have been making (sometimes cogent, sometimes not) criticisms about things like Malfeas, the Lunars, the Sidereals, in a widespread way for ages, but I don't think &quot;a secret deal between major NPCs that the players know about because they read a particular source book is inherently shite&quot; and &quot;Storytellers will feel bound to plot seeds&quot; are so self-evidently correct they can just be deployed without justification; those two statements alone invalidate enormous amounts of commonly used and effective setting design.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T09:43:21-07:00","id":1212330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Abakus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1212311#post1212311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m thinking about \u201cBender\u201d DBs this morning. Obviously the Immaculate Styles are a big part of that idea, but my mind kept coming back to Elemental Bolt. <br /> <br /> A DB who fights with that as their primary weapon seems like they\u2019re going to run out of motes VERY quickly since it eats up most of your respiration before enhancement and defensive charms, and yet a part of me wants that to be a viable combat style. On the other hand, an essentially Natural-tagged ranged weapon with tags like Disarming and Smashing that you can equip as a scenelong charm seems like it might be a problem. <br /> <br /> Did I miss a charm that would let you use this charm as your primary weapon? Or is it\u2019s non-sustainable mote cost necessary to balance its flexibility?</div> </div> </div> </div>Check out Persistant Hornet Attack in the thrown tree.<br /> <br /> EDIT: although eve with that you\u2019re only breaking even with a willpower loss at two turns, so it\u2019s only for long fights. Otherwise I think the enhancements make it not such a raw deal, getting double 10s on damage for 4 mores isn\u2019t great, but it\u2019s orobably fine considering the flexibility of also making it poison or smashing or what have you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 04-27-2018, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T10:35:24-07:00","id":1212351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1212323#post1212323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think this undermines the core thrusts of my arguments, tho.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm sure there will be discussions about how the gameline handles secrets and how the spectre of metaplot can impact people's games. But even if this thread is reaching the end of it's natural life due to the end of the kickstarter, on principle I'm not going to risk surrendering what little future it has left over to Deathlords or the Reclamation. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T12:26:53-07:00","id":1212383,"title":"","content":"On the subject of Mnemon negotiating with the Mask of Winters:<br /> <br /> \u200bIn its own context, I actually liked that, and did not feel as though it compromised the character of Mnemon or the importance of the civil war. I kind of feel as though the Deathlords should more often be treated as people with whom one can conduct diplomatic relations with in a manner that doesn't constitute being corrupted by them, and even in cases where people can be ideologically opposed to them. I feel as though there is plenty of room in the setting for alliances that are in the short-term, between people that would otherwise be enemies, and where nobody has any illusions about how long it can last (although where the follow-up isn't necessarily another war; soft power has its applications). In the machinations of the Realm civil war, I think there definitely should be somebody who would want to court the ruler of Thorns for supplies, aid, intelligence, or keeping Lookshy off their back. There should also be people courting Lookshy for the same (with the added benefit of keeping the Mask of Winters off of them). And the other side of the table is measuring their own costs and benefits, and what powers in the Realm would be to their advantage.<br /> <br /> \u200bI don't think the title of Deathlord should be an obstacle to this, whether it be something understood as meaning a lord of the dead, and <i>even if</i> one recognises that they're talking to somebody who intends for the end of all life.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe real world has had alliances between Nazis and communists, in spite of both having ideologies very openly demanding the destruction of the other.<br /> <br /> \u200bAt the same time, I acknowledge that the surrounding context in which that chapter fiction first appeared was... I presume after the point where the publications started leaning towards the Deathlords being the all consuming Big Bads of the setting, which made an application of somebody pragmatically making a short-term alliance with one of them problematic. Not entirely irreconcilable, but weighted. I'm not really trying to argue here, just feel prompted to lay out my own thoughts.<br /> <br /> \u200bI look at Mnemon as she's written now as somebody whose convictions are of the kind in which even a pragmatic alliance with a Deathlord would be unconscionable. Mind, that's not the same as meaning that she wouldn't do it, just that I imagine it would be a harder sell to her, and an action that she would feel a measure of disgust about rather than &quot;mwahaha, I am getting ahead and I'm going to screw over this bastard in the end&quot;. I don't strictly think that this shift in portrayal is redressing a short-coming in how she was written previously, I just happen to find it a lot more compelling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T14:15:20-07:00","id":1212418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1212383#post1212383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bIn its own context, I actually liked that, and did not feel as though it compromised the character of Mnemon or the importance of the civil war. I kind of feel as though the Deathlords should more often be treated as people with whom one can conduct diplomatic relations with in a manner that doesn't constitute being corrupted by them, and even in cases where people can be ideologically opposed to them. I feel as though there is plenty of room in the setting for alliances that are in the short-term, between people that would otherwise be enemies, and where nobody has any illusions about how long it can last (although where the follow-up isn't necessarily another war; soft power has its applications). In the machinations of the Realm civil war, I think there definitely should be somebody who would want to court the ruler of Thorns for supplies, aid, intelligence, or keeping Lookshy off their back. There should also be people courting Lookshy for the same (with the added benefit of keeping the Mask of Winters off of them). And the other side of the table is measuring their own costs and benefits, and what powers in the Realm would be to their advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isator, when you're right you're right. This echoes my own thoughts almost exactly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bAt the same time, I acknowledge that the surrounding context in which that chapter fiction first appeared was... I presume after the point where the publications started leaning towards the Deathlords being the all consuming Big Bads of the setting, which made an application of somebody pragmatically making a short-term alliance with one of them problematic. Not entirely irreconcilable, but weighted. I'm not really trying to argue here, just feel prompted to lay out my own thoughts. </div> </div> </div>Kinda-sorta. Aspect Book: Earth came out in '04. Exalted: The Abyssals was a year old at that point, and Sidereals had also been published, but we were still in 1E. The Deathlords were not really yet the all-consuming terror monsters they'd later become, but they were getting there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bI look at Mnemon as she's written now as somebody whose convictions are of the kind in which even a pragmatic alliance with a Deathlord would be unconscionable. </div> </div> </div>Something I really really love about new Mnemon is that while she clearly is very much her mother's daughter, she isn't just &quot;Big Red only younger.&quot;<br /> <br /> Because you really got the impression in both prior editions that she wasn't just LIKE her mother, she essentially WAS her mother. This Mnemon is more complicated than that.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T18:27:54-07:00","id":1212507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1212418#post1212418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isator, when you're right you're right. This echoes my own thoughts almost exactly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Kinda-sorta. Aspect Book: Earth came out in '04. Exalted: The Abyssals was a year old at that point, and Sidereals had also been published, but we were still in 1E. The Deathlords were not really yet the all-consuming terror monsters they'd later become, but they were getting there.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>2004 was when Autochtonians was being written, so they were already there - we just didn't get to see it until the Engines of Extinction turned everything into the First and Forsaken Lion Show, with a little help from the Book of Bone and Ebony. the Abyssal book also didn't give much of an impression of Deathlords as people, but that might just have been my reading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T02:41:44-07:00","id":1212572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1212383#post1212383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI don't think the title of Deathlord should be an obstacle to this, whether it be something understood as meaning a lord of the dead, and <i>even if</i> one recognises that they're talking to somebody who intends for the end of all life.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe real world has had alliances between Nazis and communists, in spite of both having ideologies very openly demanding the destruction of the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>My comment about the title Deathlord is that it carries expectations rooted deep in the fantasy genre. As such, having someone form an alliance with one is less like a historical event and more like a piece of historical fiction.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T18:18:10-07:00","id":1212865,"title":"","content":"Hmm, a quick skim through the pdf doesn't find me my favorite Ragara, Myrrun. Where is the martial arts grandmaster and soon-to-be essence crater?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T18:33:19-07:00","id":1212873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1212865#post1212865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, a quick skim through the pdf doesn't find me my favorite Ragara, Myrrun. Where is the martial arts grandmaster and soon-to-be essence crater?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIt suddenly occurs to me that the different approach to the martial arts might kind of preclude that narrative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T18:37:26-07:00","id":1212879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1212865#post1212865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, a quick skim through the pdf doesn't find me my favorite Ragara, Myrrun. Where is the martial arts grandmaster and soon-to-be essence crater?</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's my guess as to why, just a guess;<br /> <br /> \u200bNow that there aren't separate celestial and terrestrial martial arts his achievement of being an elemental grandmaster doesn't have the same impact. He's not functioning in a higher plane than the other DB's. Also we haven't yet seen any Sidereal arts and I have some doubt that their mechanics been nailed down with certainty. As a result the discussion of teaching a DB Sidereal arts lacks much of the context it had when Myrrun was introduced in first edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T18:56:46-07:00","id":1212886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1212873#post1212873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bIt suddenly occurs to me that the different approach to the martial arts might kind of preclude that narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, we already know that SMA are still gated beyond the reach of most exalts (I mean, even <i>solars</i> have so much trouble reaching it they have to learn it directly from a sidereal since only they know it well enough to explain it in a way they can manage to understand) and they will presumably be awesome enough to be worth using so no reason to not have someone who is futilely trying to grasp mastery that is beyond his potential (and who might explode from trying it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T19:03:41-07:00","id":1212888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1212873#post1212873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bIt suddenly occurs to me that the different approach to the martial arts might kind of preclude that narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>You two are right, of course. I was hoping he'd keep his status by dint of &quot;Youngest multi-dragon style Grandmaster&quot; and maybe Sidereal Martial Arts are as hard to learn as shapeshifting is for anyone who isn't a Lunar, but we'll see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T21:18:09-07:00","id":1212925,"title":"","content":"He also wasn't likely included since there's like 50+ named characters in jus thte Aspect Book personalities alone and in the grand scheme of things, he's probably a less useful NPC for most games than the ones we got.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T06:33:31-07:00","id":1213037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1212865#post1212865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, a quick skim through the pdf doesn't find me my favorite Ragara, Myrrun. Where is the martial arts grandmaster and soon-to-be essence crater?</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the feeling that Ragara Myrrun would've changed a lot if he'd returned in this book. The problem he's had for the last two editions is that he hasn't felt like a person in his own right, he seems to want things because Anys Syn wants them.<br /> <br /> There's interesting things that could be done with the basic details cast in a new light, especially in light of the fact that we've moved away from &quot;all my spiritual convictions are just mumbo jumbo the Sidereals made up! lol!&quot; like maybe he's got this little heresy going in the back of his mind where she's the Sixth Immaculate Dragon who brought the fighting styles into the world before hiding her own existence from history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T06:42:18-07:00","id":1213042,"title":"","content":"Now I imagine a mortified Anys Syn learning that she has been declared the new Scarlet Empress and trying to explain how this happened to Chejop Kejak.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T03:15:53-07:00","id":1213719,"title":"","content":"Does anyone have any idea when we'll be asked about add-ons? I'm now worried I've missed something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T04:15:00-07:00","id":1213730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1213719#post1213719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone have any idea when we'll be asked about add-ons? I'm now worried I've missed something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Surveys'll probably go out towards the end of the month.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T10:45:37-07:00","id":1214216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1213719#post1213719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone have any idea when we'll be asked about add-ons? I'm now worried I've missed something.</div> </div> </div> </div>They\u2019re using Backerkit now, so you\u2019ll be able to add things on after the fact using their shopping cart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T12:50:19-07:00","id":1214271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1212865#post1212865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, a quick skim through the pdf doesn't find me my favorite Ragara, Myrrun. Where is the martial arts grandmaster and soon-to-be essence crater?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, they could be the canon QC that somebody brings in from previous editions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T23:23:47-07:00","id":1214434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1214216#post1214216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They\u2019re using Backerkit now, so you\u2019ll be able to add things on after the fact using their shopping cart.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is this shopping cart? I can only see an option to view my pledge. Is this different from the survey <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"51\" data-vbnamecard=\"51\">marin</a> mentioned?<br /> <br /> Apologies for the confusion, but I'm not grokking the terminology everyone's using at this point, and it almost feels like there should be options somewhere, but there are none.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T00:00:37-07:00","id":1214447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1214434#post1214434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is this shopping cart? I can only see an option to view my pledge. Is this different from the survey <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"51\" data-vbnamecard=\"51\">marin</a> mentioned?<br /> <br /> Apologies for the confusion, but I'm not grokking the terminology everyone's using at this point, and it almost feels like there should be options somewhere, but there are none.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not up yet. Onyx Path are going to eventually send out an email asking DB backers to fill out a survey on Backerkit (whether there're reward tiers you'd like to see in future Kickstarters, what name you want to have in the backers list, etc.). It'll allow you to change your pledge and add things you missed in the KS, as BrilliantRain says,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T21:17:31-07:00","id":1214902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1214434#post1214434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is this shopping cart? I can only see an option to view my pledge. Is this different from the survey <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"51\" data-vbnamecard=\"51\">marin</a> mentioned?<br /> <br /> Apologies for the confusion, but I'm not grokking the terminology everyone's using at this point, and it almost feels like there should be options somewhere, but there are none.</div> </div> </div> </div>BackerKit goes live later. It's a different website.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought-for-exalted-3/posts/2172218\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects.../posts/2172218</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>4. BACKERKIT SURVEYS</b> Once BackerKit says I'm good to go, I will send out a survey to all backers. This is why confirming your e-mail is important! The survey will list the reward tier you've chosen, confirm all of the rewards associated with that reward tier, and confirm your total pledge amount. I expect Surveys to go out 3-4 weeks into May.<br /> If you opted to include any Add-On rewards to your pledge, this is the point where you will select them. BackerKit will deduct the cost of your reward tier (+shipping) from your total pledge and show you how much you have to allocate for add-on purchases. You simply select the ones you want and proceed. From that point forward, those add-ons will be included in your list of rewards.<br /> During the Survey period, you can also also choose to increase your reward tier. If you've managed to get a tax refund and decide it's time to trade up to get two copies of the book or include another add-on, you can do so at this time. Note, you will not be able to reduce your reward tier selection, only increase.<br /> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T21:28:50-07:00","id":1214907,"title":"","content":"Use Larceny\u2019s Window-in-the-Door Technique to spy through a wall or the hull of a ship. Take aim. <br /> <br /> Use Sea\u2019s Verdict\u2019s Hull-Breaking Tsunami Swipe to blow a hole through that barrier while also attacking your target on the other side.<br /> <br /> (Does Mischievous Wind Grasp work the same when the other side of the barrier is filled with water rather than air?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T20:08:51-07:00","id":1216451,"title":"","content":"From my understanding the legions being split up between the great houses is new to this edition, which seems like a stroke of genius, I've found.<br /> <br /> So I've been playing the mobile remaster/port of the excellent 90s tactical RPG Romance of the Three Kingdoms: The Legend of Cao Cao, and was finding a bunch of DB/Realm inspiration. I was filling in gaps of my ROTK knowledge, when I found this portion of the wiki particularly poignant-<br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">In 188, Emperor Ling accepted a memorial from </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liu_Yan_(Han_dynasty_warlord)\" target=\"_blank\">Liu Yan</a><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> suggesting he grant direct administrative power over feudal provinces and direct command of regional military to local governors, as well as promoting them in rank and filling such positions with members of the Liu family or court officials. This move made </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zhou_(country_subdivision)\" target=\"_blank\">provinces</a><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> (</span></span></span><i>zhou</i><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">) official administrative units, and although they had power to combat rebellions, the later intragovernmental chaos allowed these local governors to easily rule independently of the central government.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Really helps set up for the coming Civil War.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T20:38:41-07:00","id":1216460,"title":"","content":"The thing is less that it's new this edition, and it's new that we know how they were split up, and how there was a ban on houses save Cathak, Sesus, and Tepet from fielding any.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T04:43:41-07:00","id":1216571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1216451#post1216451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From my understanding the legions being split up between the great houses is new to this edition</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bNah, that's been there since the First Edition core book. It might be a more consistent detail of the Realm than the nature of the Great Houses is.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T04:55:14-07:00","id":1216576,"title":"","content":"Looking over this again. It bugs me a little that so many charms have excellency prerequisites I'd have thought dice/success adders would have been something players could've been trusted to get in their own time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T07:16:02-07:00","id":1216630,"title":"","content":"Well, there ya go. I read every second ed book and didn't remember that being a thing, or at least being as spelled out. So I guess the kudos just goes back to GBG, and also Vance/Neal for making sure it was prominent.<br /> <br /> Looking through historic evidence while prepping for a Realm game that would play into Civil War and I found myself on the wikipedia page for Failed State and State Collapse. Sobering read at 2 in the morning.<br /> <br /> Just makes me even more excited for the Deliberative government details in The Realm.<br /> <br /> Could just be a case of my apparent 2ed DB amnesia, but was the machinations of the Deliberative expounded on in a previous edition source I could rifle through to sate my curiosity, and also help me better identify new material?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T09:27:13-07:00","id":1217019,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The comment elsewhere on somebody somehow managing to find the Dragon Blooded Charms so unsatisfying that they only want Martial Arts and Evocations had me imagining a character that actually did that, and how they would be looked upon by their fellows. I'm seeing somebody looked down upon with the most severe kind of contempt, for squandering and disregarding the holy power that flows through their own veins, the legacy of their ancestors and the sacred Dragons, bestowed upon their unworthy selves.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T15:53:42-07:00","id":1217168,"title":"","content":"People often forget how spoilt PCs are with their ability to choose and customise backgrounds/merits.<br /> It's pretty great to imagine a Solar finding the weapon of their previous incarnation noting it's not a Form weapon of their preferred Martial Art and tossing it over their shoulder like its trash or a young Dynastic child demanding their exaltation gifts be artifacts designed to their specifications and not some hand-me-down crap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T16:58:07-07:00","id":1217190,"title":"","content":"Isator, careful now, seems like that's a roundabout way to get this thread us back (obliquely) to the perennial &quot;Are martial arts Charms a 'thing' in setting?&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T17:24:44-07:00","id":1217203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1217190#post1217190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isator, careful now, seems like that's a roundabout way to get this thread us back (obliquely) to the perennial &quot;Are martial arts Charms a 'thing' in setting?&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't entirely understand this sentence.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless...<br /> <br /> \u200bCould somebody link me to any fan projects to update the Dragon Blooded Charms to Third Edition? I would be interested in seeing how they contrast with the new cascades.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T21:55:29-07:00","id":1217267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/881714-a-clutch-of-dragons-hub-thread\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/881714-a-clutch-of-dragons-hub-thread\"> A Clutch of Dragons: Hub Thread - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/881714-a-clutch-of-dragons-hub-thread\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/881714-a-clutch-of-dragons-hub-thread </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I don't really want to spam the forum by posting a new thread every time I finish an Ability, so I'm just going to keep them all here and update the first post. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Re: evocation/MA only character, it wouldn't necessarily be too crazy. We do have the Solar NPC who was all about the evocations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T00:09:38-07:00","id":1217285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1217203#post1217203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't entirely understand this sentence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Martial arts charms aren't a differentiated concept in setting, then why see a Dragonblooded who uses them as different from a user of native Charms? If Martial arts charms are *just* Dragonblooded pouring their power through martial arts, then why would in setting characters see a Dragonblood who does so as socially different from one who pours their power through melee? Why would in setting characters have any more scorn for them than a comparable Solar? (Though this is getting into the exact forum discussions I thought would be a played out tangent already <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T02:20:26-07:00","id":1217303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1217285#post1217285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Martial arts charms aren't a differentiated concept in setting, then why see a Dragonblooded who uses them as different from a user of native Charms? If Martial arts charms are *just* Dragonblooded pouring their power through martial arts, then why would in setting characters see a Dragonblood who does so as socially different from one who pours their power through melee? Why would in setting characters have any more scorn for them than a comparable Solar? (Though this is getting into the exact forum discussions I thought would be a played out tangent already <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).</div> </div> </div> </div>Martial Arts <i>styles</i> are a recognisable thing in the setting. <br /> <br /> The distinctive movements, form weapons, and stances are identifiable. The charms represent an exalted awesomising those movements.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T03:38:21-07:00","id":1217322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1217303#post1217303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Martial Arts <i>styles</i> are a recognisable thing in the setting.<br /> <br /> The distinctive movements, form weapons, and stances are identifiable. The charms represent an exalted awesomising those movements.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ghosthead specifically talks about Charms. There should be no way to judge somebody to be throwing away their divinity for having MA Charms instead of Melee, or expressing your divinity through communion with an object of power, specially a family heirloom.<br /> <br /> Mortals can't do any of that, so any of those expressions are probably seem as exercising your divine inheritance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T03:56:14-07:00","id":1217323,"title":"","content":"I think it sort of comes back to how &quot;charms aren't things&quot; is mostly, but not <i>entirely</i> true. There are certain techniques and powers that charms permit that can clearly be pointed out as things in-setting. Of course, generally speaking essence use is a kind of personal, instinctive thing, so two people using the same charm might not actually do it the same way, but I think Martial Arts are a bit of an exception to this.<br /> <br /> Martial Arts are a way exalted have found to channel essence in a defined, repeatable way that other exalted can emulate. They still think of it in terms of katas and stances, but those katas and stances are not just about moving your body correctly. They're also about moving your <i>essence</i> correctly. So the charms are things, but that thing is simply an aspect of another thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T04:25:02-07:00","id":1217328,"title":"","content":"Well, that could be true for some Charms and not for others, even in Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> And, more to the heart of the discussion, Dragon Blooded are still Ability based Exalts, and Martial Arts is an ability, therefore showing your power through them should not be seen as squandering your talents nor cause you to suffer from any ostracism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T04:44:25-07:00","id":1217334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1217322#post1217322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There should be no way to judge somebody to be throwing away their divinity for having MA Charms instead of Melee, or expressing your divinity through communion with an object of power, specially a family heirloom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon Blooded have the Aura.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T04:58:51-07:00","id":1217336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1217334#post1217334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dragon Blooded have the Aura.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aura is only visible when flaring. It is a detail in a show of power.<br /> <br /> You think someone is going to walk up to a master of Mantis Style, or the bearer who mastered Horizon Cleaver and say:<br /> <br /> &quot;I notice that when your anima flares, it doesn't flare in a certain way! You are running away from your spiritual gifts and spitting on the eyes of the Dragons! You pitiable lout!&quot;<br /> <br /> ?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T05:42:36-07:00","id":1217347,"title":"","content":"Tbh, I think the idea that you're going to find a Dragonblood who didn't even develop an excellency in school is so vanishingly rare that I doubt there's any culturally-mandated way of dealing with it... if you could even tell, which you probably can't really, feasibly. A Fire Aspect flaring iconically and a Fire Aspect in Fire Aura flaring iconically do, I think, look the same (not 100% sure on that).<br /> <br /> But I can't really see a DB Tiger Stylist not having Become the Hammer, and thus frequently entering water aura, or a DB wielding Gorgon not having Stoking Bonfire Style and thus frequently entering fire aura.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's hypothetically possible, but surely it's so vanishingly rare for a woman with a magic sword who uses it every day and has unlocked its greatest magical secrets to have not learned the most basic instinct for using channelling her own essence into swordsmanship, that society is just going to be confused as to why you'd do that.<br /> <br /> I guess if said character went round saying &quot;the power of the Dragon's blood is so rubbish that I'd rather learn to unleash the power in this Anathema-forged weapon of Wyld-silver than use my innate Draconic power even a little&quot; then people might find it blasphemous. And idiotic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-10-2018, 08:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T05:51:46-07:00","id":1217352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1217347#post1217347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tbh, I think the idea that you're going to find a Dragonblood who didn't even develop an excellency in school is so vanishingly rare that I doubt there's any culturally-mandated way of dealing with it... if you could even tell, which you probably can't really, feasibly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agreed. 10char","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T05:59:41-07:00","id":1217353,"title":"","content":"I can\u2019t imagine why a dedicated Dragon-Blooded Martial Artist wouldn\u2019t at least pick up Become the Hammer.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m usually the first to say \u201ccharacters in-universe don\u2019t pick their Charms\u201d, and that\u2019s true - but if they\u2019re mastering Martial Arts than clearly that\u2019s a basic expression of Exalted excellence that reflects that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T07:23:00-07:00","id":1217387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1217336#post1217336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> &quot;I notice that when your anima flares, it doesn't flare in a certain way! You are running away from your spiritual gifts and spitting on the eyes of the Dragons! You pitiable lout!&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWhy not? They don't have any social Charms. Inspire action to create shame, in a public venue where responding violently makes <i>them</i> look like the asshole (if they can even manage violence through the shame).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T07:25:15-07:00","id":1217388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1217347#post1217347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Fire Aspect flaring iconically and a Fire Aspect in Fire Aura flaring iconically do, I think, look the same (not 100% sure on that).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThey do not. They explicitly do not. It's one of the first things said in the Elemental Aura rules.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T07:29:16-07:00","id":1217390,"title":"","content":"They'd look pretty similar. It's mostly a matter of intensity.<br /> <br /> You'd notice if you saw one enter aura with their anima up, but you might not be able to tell by itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T07:33:57-07:00","id":1217392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1217387#post1217387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bWhy not? They don't have any social Charms. Inspire action to create shame, in a public venue where responding violently makes <i>them</i> look like the asshole (if they can even manage violence through the shame).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, we'll have to go our separate ways on this one. That is not something that is a thing in my view of the setting.<br /> <br /> I don't believe Anima Flaring is such a structured phenomena that is so scrutinized as to be an object of insult.<br /> <br /> There are numerous different reasons why the Aura may not show, maybe they used different Aspected Charms, they may have spent from Personal, not enough peripheral.<br /> <br /> For this to be even noticeable, this would have to be someone that has watched yo uflare many times, and then there aren't any codified or provable way the Anima should flared on that particular situation.<br /> <br /> There is no expected normal result for the denigrating comparison to be made against.<br /> <br /> So its kinda hard for it to be a thing, in my view anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 05-10-2018, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T07:46:28-07:00","id":1217396,"title":"","content":"<i>That</i> line was mostly me commenting &quot;hey, person who doesn't want to take any of the oh-so-weak and pathetic Dragon Blooded Charms; how are you going to handle social interactions&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bCombined with a bit of an observation that there might be a few noticeable deficiencies in a character that can't be substituted for with fight stuff.<br /> <br /> \u200b<i>And</i> the fact that, since the social interaction rules have actual weight and significance, it can be possible for the rules to model saying a thing to a person and having it have an effect enforced by mechanics that cannot simply be overridden by disparities in physical power (or out-of-character knowledge or decision making).<br /> <br /> \u200bStill, the Dragon Blooded, especially those of the Realm, are prone to being touchy about social status, combative, and reasonably spiritual. The setting details in What Fire Has Wrought directly draw a line between the sensation of connection to the substance of the world, and their perception of themselves as its divinely ordained rulers. And, as the developers noted in their Charm commentaries, quite a few of their powers are a bit flashier than those of Solars.<br /> <br /> \u200bFire can erupt from their mouths when they taste poison!<br /> <br /> \u200bI think all of these details that are actually in the book can effectively come together to create scenarios in which a Dragon Blood who inexplicably does not want to use any of their own Charms is noticeable to somebody, that such a somebody might take a manner of offence, and that even if they didn't, they would say some words that can hurt like a knife anyway because those galas can be rather catty.<br /> <br /> \u200bYou know, a bit like the fiction that was used to introduce the Great Houses of the Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T08:28:55-07:00","id":1217411,"title":"","content":"I understand where you're coming from, I just don't think it would get to the point of scrutiny of observing Aura.<br /> <br /> Flaring at all, yeah, I can see an argument for criticism of not flaring at all, like:<br /> <br /> &quot;Did you see Tilati's speech? I thought it was too contained, she should've been awash in fire... I just don't think she gave it her all.&quot; (Even if they didn't flare because of Personal Essence use, someone with a bone to pick could say the lack of visuals was a disappointment)<br /> <br /> &quot;You lost because you are a coward! Afraid to exercise your Divine Right to Power, couldn't even bring yourself to manifest your Anima! Disgraceful&quot; (after having lost a duel without flaring)<br /> <br /> But;<br /> <br /> &quot;Ha Tilati! You are a wretched fool! Care to tell me why your Anima wasn't of a WHITE fire, but just fire during that speech? Why are you squandering the Blood of the Dragon coursing through your veins?!&quot;<br /> <br /> I just can't see it.<br /> <br /> I don't think people concern themselves whether Tilati's speech was so moving because of her Ability and Elemental Essence, or because she has Ligeia's Allure, an Artifact choker that enchants the user's voice.<br /> <br /> Specially since Artifact bonding is such a big part of Dragon Blooded Nature and Culture. They are second only to Solars in that respect, and they carry an enormous Arsenal, they have Heirlooms, they are proud of these things. It is very ingrained in the culture, why would it be insulting to dedicate yourself to master a family Relic? There are whole martial traditions based on this.<br /> <br /> The same with Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> Like I said, I think expectations of flaring could be a thing, but not so far as to criticize Aura.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 05-10-2018, 11:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T08:42:30-07:00","id":1217415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1217411#post1217411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think people concern themselves whether Tilati's speech was so moving because of her Ability and Elemental Essence, or because she has Ligeia's Allure, an Artifact choker that enchants the user's voice.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's all it does, it probably doesn't cost Essence.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T08:52:28-07:00","id":1217419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1217415#post1217415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If that's all it does, it probably doesn't cost Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;enchants the user's voice&quot; was a short hand for having Evocations related to inspire/instill through voice related means.<br /> <br /> And remember, even if something does cost Essence, a user might decide to use Personal Essence, which has no visible effect at all.<br /> <br /> So people who would actually care about minutiae on the matter and study these things would know that they actually have no clue as to when someone should or shouldn't be flaring, much less what sort of minor detail a particular DB's banner should look like on a specific instance.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T09:46:22-07:00","id":1217429,"title":"","content":"I've fallen into a very silly rabbit hole. One that opens on the surface with a wry comment about what somebody said regarding their response to Dragon Blooded Charms, and descending through layers of defensiveness in response to it being taken too seriously (including by myself) and deconstructed to the finest detail.<br /> <br /> \u200bMaybe my brother is right about CinemaSins after all.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry Ghosthead, I tried.<br /> <br /> \u200bBah, nothing wrong with the search function on <i>this</i> forum; I'll find fan projects myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T10:59:44-07:00","id":1217449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1217429#post1217429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bBah, nothing wrong with the search function on <i>this</i> forum; I'll find fan projects myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you miss <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1217267#post1217267\">the link</a> on the last page?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T11:08:47-07:00","id":1217453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1217449#post1217449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did you miss <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1217267#post1217267\">the link</a> on the last page?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T11:13:23-07:00","id":1217454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1217411#post1217411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand where you're coming from, I just don't think it would get to the point of scrutiny of observing Aura.<br /> <br /> Flaring at all, yeah, I can see an argument for criticism of not flaring at all, like:<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Did you see Tilati's speech? I thought it was too contained, she should've been awash in fire... I just don't think she gave it her all.&amp;quot; (Even if they didn't flare because of Personal Essence use, someone with a bone to pick could say the lack of visuals was a disappointment)<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;You lost because you are a coward! Afraid to exercise your Divine Right to Power, couldn't even bring yourself to manifest your Anima! Disgraceful&amp;quot; (after having lost a duel without flaring)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh hey, something cool came out of this silly argument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T18:00:32-07:00","id":1217843,"title":"","content":"Just double-checking. I'm using the houserule of having Crafts work like Lore (i.e. specialties open up new applications, as opposed to having to buy completely separate ability ratings). I've already house ruled the 3 Solar Charms that needed tweaking because of this, but it doesn't seem that it'll conflict with ANY Dragon-Blooded Charms. Anyone catch any I missed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T11:33:33-07:00","id":1228917,"title":"","content":"I had an epiphany on the Great House founders that felt worth posting but not significant enough to deserve it's own thread. So, Necromancy!<br /> <br /> Most of the dead founders seem like they were truly fascinating individuals and create incentive to play a Dragon-Blooded game in an earlier part of the Realm's history but I found Sesus and Cynis a little lacklustre compared to the rest and I've finally put my finger on why. They acknowledge and provide context for the deeply rooted stereotypes of their houses* so that their decedents can get on with things.<br /> <br /> *more Cynis in Scions of Note, but elsewhere Sesus is noted as having had her cheek slit for a night of adulterous beauties suggesting some self-control issues. Plus the whole fact that Ragara isn't dead makes me wonder if her glorious death in battle was Fire Aspects gonna Fire Aspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-01T03:40:40-07:00","id":1315848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1228917#post1228917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had an epiphany on the Great House founders that felt worth posting but not significant enough to deserve it's own thread. So, Necromancy!<br /> <br /> Most of the dead founders seem like they were truly fascinating individuals and create incentive to play a Dragon-Blooded game in an earlier part of the Realm's history but I found Sesus and Cynis a little lacklustre compared to the rest and I've finally put my finger on why. They acknowledge and provide context for the deeply rooted stereotypes of their houses* so that their decedents can get on with things.<br /> <br /> *more Cynis in Scions of Note, but elsewhere Sesus is noted as having had her cheek slit for a night of adulterous beauties suggesting some self-control issues. Plus the whole fact that Ragara isn't dead makes me wonder if her glorious death in battle was Fire Aspects gonna Fire Aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Necromancy, eh?<br /> <br /> I kinda feel like there's never been a strong idea of who Cynis is. He was male in 1st. She has been female since 2nd. As a historical character she's never been fleshed out as much as her daughters. And there's no strong reason to elaborate on her, or scope for her to show agency. (Most of my characters are Cynis because I love how the living house is portrayed.)<br /> <br /> Likewise I feel like Sesus's recharacterisation has left her simulantenously burdened by legacy but without legacy to draw upon. She has character constraints left-over from being Ragara's half-brother but no strong background to define who she is. Or, rather, was, as she's not exactly a prominent figure with agency in the game's default setting.<br /> <br /> I'd love to see a historical supplement (kind of in the vein of Shards meets Wonders) which has scope to flesh Sesus and Cynis out more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-19T06:08:03-07:00","id":1319446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1197474-dragon-blooded-kickstarter-starts-on-the-27th?p=1217843#post1217843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just double-checking. I'm using the houserule of having Crafts work like Lore (i.e. specialties open up new applications, as opposed to having to buy completely separate ability ratings). I've already house ruled the 3 Solar Charms that needed tweaking because of this, but it doesn't seem that it'll conflict with ANY Dragon-Blooded Charms. Anyone catch any I missed?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I think it's solid in that aspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T10:10:43-07:00","id":1323990,"title":"","content":"Aaaand Backerkit just charged for addons. Prepare yourselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}